window.AKK_MARQUIS_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_MARQUIS_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: System, Let's Unbind Ourselves","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi had died.","Then she came back to life.","But how long she could stay alive—hours, days—was still unknown.","“Pain... it hurts so much!!!”","The moment Jiang Yunxi regained even a sliver of consciousness, she was engulfed by endless agony.","They said pain came in thirteen levels. Jiang Yunxi felt that what she was experiencing had to be level fourteen.","The emperor of all emperors.","It was like a massive truck was running over her body again and again.","A fragment of her memories from before she lost consciousness resurfaced.","“So death is this painful.”","She had thought it was a final burst of awareness before death and had quietly waited for her consciousness to fade away. Yet instead, her mind grew clearer and clearer.","“What’s going on? Wasn’t I already dead? Then how...”","“Has Miss woken up yet?”","“Not yet.”","Two unfamiliar voices reached her ears, and Jiang Yunxi froze.","What was this “Miss” business?","Didn’t they call people in hell things like this ghost or that ghost?","Did ghosts need to sleep too?","The next instant, those questions seemed to trigger some kind of switch. Her head throbbed, and a flood of memories came rushing in.","Just as she was about to sort through them, an excited voice rang out in her mind.","【Host, you’re finally awake!】","【Host, I’m your System Sprite.】","Caught completely off guard by the voice, Jiang Yunxi nearly had a heart attack.","She could practically see her great-grandmother waving at her.","【Host, aren’t you surprised? Delighted?】","【I checked your memories. I know you’ve always wanted a storage space and a system!】","A System Sprite... and it was hers!","She had bonded with a system. Did that mean she wasn’t dead after all?","After reading novels for so many years, Jiang Yunxi had seen people bond with systems before—but never ghosts.","What was more, although she had not yet had time to organize the memories that had just flooded into her mind, she had caught glimpses of them.","Those memories did not belong to her.","Memories that weren’t hers, plus a system... as a veteran web-novel reader, Jiang Yunxi arrived at one conclusion.","She had transmigrated.","【System, what exactly is going on?】","【How did you bind to me?】","【Am I still alive?】","System: 【Host, you died, but then you came back to life.】","Jiang Yunxi: The art of saying nothing had truly been mastered by this thing.","Her body hurt too badly for her to waste time bantering with the system, so she impatiently urged, 【Speak plainly.】","System: 【I am speaking plainly.】","Sensing the intense fluctuations in its host’s emotions, the system did not dare keep joking and hurriedly explained.","【When you thought that, since you already had terminal cancer and only had a few days left to live anyway, you might as well trade your life for someone else’s and chose to take a bullet for a Chinese soldier, you died.】","【Completely and utterly dead.】","Jiang Yunxi: 【Then how did I come back to life?】","【Did you save me?】","The System Sprite spoke rapidly.","【To be precise, it was the Chinese soldiers who saved you.】","【It was my first time carrying out a mission. Because I was inexperienced, I went to the wrong time and space and happened to pass over your world.】","The System Sprite’s tone was full of chagrin.","【Those soldiers were desperate to save you after you were critically injured protecting their comrade. Their urgency was so strong, and their magnetic field so intense, that it affected me.","Somehow, I ended up binding with you after your body died and your soul left it.】","【The Main System discovered that I had gone to the wrong time and space—and even bound myself to the wrong host—so it came to correct the mistake.】","Yet, bound by the merit of those soldiers, the military souls and accumulated merit of the entire Huaxia armed forces were protecting you. It couldn’t forcibly sever the bond.","If it accidentally caused your soul to scatter and vanish, the System Realm would have thoroughly offended Huaxia.】","You Huaxia people are not easy to provoke. Setting aside the ancient great powers, even the hosts bound to various systems over the years would form a considerable force if they joined together.","【The Main System had no choice but to make the best of a mistake and kick both your soul and me, your system, into this time and space.】","【The Main System said that hosts can be replaced, but the time and space cannot.】","The Main System had even secretly instructed it to keep a close eye on her and make sure she didn’t get herself killed.","With all that merit and the protection of Huaxia’s military souls, if anything happened to her...","Forget this little shrimp of a system—even the Main System wouldn’t get away unscathed.","Naturally, the system didn’t dare let its host know that. It was afraid she would become reckless, knowing she had nothing to fear.","And then...","Jiang Yunxi understood.","She was glad that, in that moment, she had followed her instincts.","She had traded what little life she had left for the soldiers’ safety, never expecting such an outcome.","She had been given another chance at life, and she even had a system by her side.","She believed that, back in the modern era, the country would not treat her family unfairly.","The money they had borrowed for her treatment should be enough to pay off, and there might even be some left for her parents.","Although she had an older sister, so her parents would not be left without anyone to care for them in their old age, this at least proved that she had not been entirely useless.","This deal, Jiang Yunxi felt, was an absolute steal.","From what the system had just said, she had also picked up some information: apparently, she had powerful backing.","Even the Main System did not dare offend it, much less this little system.","Perhaps, from now on, when she did things...","Fortunately, the system could not access every thought in her mind. Otherwise...","【Why does everything hurt so much?】","【You brought me into this body—did you harm its original owner?】","【If you did harm her, who would be responsible for that?】","With merit protecting her body and all this transmigration business, Jiang Yunxi was beginning to believe in such mystical matters.","If she had harmed the original owner of this body because of her arrival, would that karma fall on the system—or on her?","Surely it could not be her fault. She had not asked the system to place her in this body.","If anyone was to blame, it should be the system—or the Main System!","【Rest assured, Host. Before you entered this body, its original owner had already died.】","【This system is a law-abiding, upstanding system. I would never do something as cruel as taking a life without regard.】","Jiang Yunxi did not feel even the slightest bit embarrassed.","Such matters had to be made clear from the start, otherwise there would be disputes later on.","【Then how did the original owner die?】","【It wasn’t revenge, was it? Am I safe now?】","【My whole body hurts. Is it because the original owner was injured, or because my soul and this body are incompatible and rejecting each other?】","【Can my soul remain in this body?】","【And what kind of system are you?】","【Please don’t tell me you’re some kind of mission system or romance-conquest system.","Let me tell you, I hate doing missions most of all, and I hate having to pursue and win over someone even more.","I’ve been single since birth. I’ve never dated, I don’t know how to date, and I definitely don’t know how to win someone over.】","【If failing missions or being unable to conquer the target means I’ll be erased, then you might as well let me die right now.】","[So I won’t have to spend every day on edge afterward, worrying that one day I might fail to complete a mission...】","Relying on what she believed was her backing, Jiang Yunxi made her stance clear right away: she didn’t want to do missions, and she didn’t want to pursue or win over anyone.","Jiang Yunxi fired off so many questions in a row that she completely stunned the system.","Hadn’t she wanted a system very badly? Why was she being so picky the moment they bonded?","Hosts these days were far too difficult to manage. She was the worst host it had ever had.","The system was deeply relieved that, before the Main System had kicked it over here, it had worried that the host might fail her missions and die, thereby offending Huaxia. So it had modified the system core.","Otherwise...","The system’s silence made Jiang Yunxi’s heart skip a beat. Could the system she’d bonded with really be a mission system—or some kind of romance-conquest system?","Then she was doomed.","She might as well give up immediately.","Having read plenty of novels, she knew those two kinds of systems were complete traps. If you failed a mission or didn’t reach the required affection level, they’d shock you with electricity or strike you with lightning.","Someone like her would be finished sooner or later.","If she was going to die sooner or later anyway, she might as well die sooner and reincarnate sooner.","Maybe, with all that accumulated merit, she could be reborn in Huaxia. Eighteen years later, she’d be a fine young woman again.","【System, let’s unbind.】"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: System, I Have It So Hard","paragraphs":["【System, let’s sever our bond!】","The words struck like a thunderbolt out of nowhere, crashing the System’s CPU.","The System never imagined that merely failing to respond in time would earn it a threat from its Host to sever their connection.","It hadn’t even done anything! It had only been thinking about how to answer its Host.","After all, it had originally been designed as a mission system. But then the Main System made a change, giving it the functions of two different systems.","The Main System had instructed it to let its Host enjoy gossip without risk or worry, while also finding a way to have the Host complete the original system missions without her knowing.","If a mission wasn’t completed, the punishment originally meant for the Host would instead fall on it.","Although the severity of the punishment had been reduced somewhat, it would be delayed until after this Host severed their bond, when it would be reflected in the System’s overall KPI evaluation.","When the person who was originally supposed to be punished was the Host, but the punishment had instead become its responsibility, even the System Sprite felt that it was getting a raw deal.","It felt there was nowhere it could go to seek justice.","But the Main System had said that if it hadn’t run into the wrong time-space and accidentally become bound to its current Host while gossiping, none of these troublesome matters would have happened afterward.","If it didn’t take the blame, then who would?","Even so... despite that... it still felt wronged.","It had taken such a huge risk for its Host, and not only did the Host know nothing about it, she was even threatening to sever their bond.","As a novice system binding itself to a Host for the first time, if its Host voluntarily severed the connection right after the binding, the only thing awaiting it would be being sent back for reconstruction.","Its system life was supposed to have begun with it making a name for itself in the world of systems. Instead, it was about to end before it had even started.","It kept its Host in its heart, while its Host kicked it straight into a ditch.","The System was suffering.","The System was crying pitifully.","It hurriedly sought help from the Main System, asking whether it could conceal its identity as a mission system, lest...","It was having such a hard time.","Had the Main System forgotten that it was only a novice system too? Could it really shoulder such a huge responsibility?","You’re afraid of Huaxia and don’t dare let my Host die, so you come bully me instead.","Fortunately, because of Jiang Yunxi’s special nature, the Main System had been paying close attention to the situation on their side. Its reply arrived in an instant.","After receiving the Main System’s response, the System hurriedly answered,","【Host, rest assured. This System is neither a mission system nor a strategy system. It’s merely an ordinary Gossip System.】","Jiang Yunxi felt inexplicably disdainful of the Gossip System. What use was there in binding herself to a gossip system?","Gossip was only good for passing the time!","With that time, she might as well play on her phone or read novels.","Come to think of it, where had she been transported? Were there phones and tablets here?","Jiang Yunxi had received far too many memories, and her entire body was in unbearable pain. She had no mind to sort through them just then, so she simply asked directly,","【System, you still haven’t told me what era this is, or what happened to the original owner of this body.】","【Ding—】","【The Gossip System is now officially at your service.","As for the gossip concerning this body—in other words, you, Host—would you like to hear it?】","Jiang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍Yunxi: 【Tell me.】","How could she refuse? At the very least, this would help her figure out her current identity—and let her see whether this Gossip System was actually any good.","The System inhaled sharply: I’m very good.","The System: 【The original owner of this body was also named Jiang Yunxi.】","Jiang Yunxi: “Good. At least I won’t have to get used to another name.”","[She is currently nine years old, the Fifth Miss of the Marquis of Pingyang’s household, a daughter born to Madam Zheng, the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang’s Secondary Wife.","Because she was born after a difficult labor that left her in poor health, she had always been kept deep within the inner chambers and rarely went out.]","Jiang Yunxi: “······”","From “the Marquis of Pingyang’s household,” “daughter of a secondary wife,” and “the Heir’s Secondary Wife,” she deduced that she had transmigrated to ancient times.","Wasn’t the modern era perfectly fine? If not that, she could at least have gone to some interstellar future. Why did it have to be ancient times?","Please, let it not be the dynasty with the queue hairstyle.","Jiang Yunxi immediately interrupted the System. [System, don’t tell me I’ve transmigrated into the Qing dynasty, okay?]","[Rest assured, Host. This is not the Qing dynasty. It is a dynasty that does not exist in your history—the Yunzhao Kingdom.]","So it was an entirely fictional world.","Fictional was good. Fictional was wonderful. Fictional was absolutely fantastic.","A fictional world meant that no matter what she did here, she would not alter the history of her own timeline.","With the huge weight in her heart finally lifted, Jiang Yunxi urged, [Go on.]","[Yesterday was a holiday from the household academy. The original host was playing hide-and-seek with the maids in her family’s rear garden.","She hid behind a particular ornamental rock, never imagining that someone would sneak up behind her, knock her unconscious with a stick, and quietly throw her into the lake.]","[By the time she was rescued, she had been soaking in the water for far too long and remained unconscious.","The blow to her head had caused a blood clot in her brain. On top of that, she had been submerged for so long that her lungs became infected. With her high fever refusing to break, she eventually died.]","Jiang Yunxi frowned. [So this is an inner-household power struggle?]","What kind of inner-household power struggle was this? It was even more brutal than palace intrigue. They were using real weapons and actually killing people.","At this rate, how many people could possibly be left alive in the Marquis of Pingyang’s household?","The fact that the entire household had not already been wiped out was probably a miracle.","Jiang Yunxi asked with complete confidence,","[Was the person who did it acting on the orders of the original host’s primary wife? Or was it one of her legitimate or secondary sisters? Or perhaps one of the other concubines of the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang?]","As if she hadn’t read countless novels all these years.","Aside from those people, who else would want to get rid of the original host?","Sigh. Why had she transmigrated to ancient times? And why had she ended up as a physically frail daughter of a secondary wife?","Jiang Yunxi was deeply worried about her future.","With enemies lurking everywhere, could she, a complete novice at inner-household intrigue, survive in the marquis’s household with the help of this seemingly unreliable Gossip System?","Just listen to her title: the Fifth Miss.","In ancient times, sons and daughters were generally ranked separately. From that title alone, it was obvious that the Marquis of Pingyang’s household had quite a few children.","The struggle for power was sure to be······","[Host, you’re mistaken.]","Jiang Yunxi: “······” Why did her face feel so hot?","She had only just tried to show off her cleverness, and she had already been proven wrong.","Was there a crack in the ground she could crawl into?","Or perhaps someone could bring her a block of tofu so she could bash her head against it.","Pretending nothing had happened, she said, [You say I’m wrong, so why don’t you tell me who actually knocked out the original host and threw her into the water?]","[They must have been trying to drown her, right?]","The System replied, [It is true that someone wanted to drown her, but it wasn’t any of the people you just listed.]","[The original host could only be called unlucky. She chose the wrong place to hide while playing hide-and-seek with the maids.","There was a cave not far from the ornamental rock where she was hiding. Two people were inside playing cards.]","[The original host made a noise, startling the two of them.","They saw the original host and thought she had discovered them. To keep their secret from getting out, they decided to silence her for good.]","Jiang Yunxi was baffled. [Playing poker is just playing poker. Why would they kill someone just because they were seen?","It was only a game of poker! Was that really worth it?]","Was it worth taking the original host’s life?","As soon as the words left her mouth, Jiang Yunxi froze. She suddenly recalled the movie recaps she used to watch on TikTok.","Aside from card games, “playing poker” seemed to have another meaning.","It was all the System Sprite’s fault for being so up-to-date—she hadn’t caught on right away.","Suppressing the urge to cough awkwardly in her mind, Jiang Yunxi quickly cut off the System before it could explain.","[All right, no need to explain. I know what “playing poker” means now.]","[Just tell me who that shameless pair is.]","Now that she had taken over this body, the original host’s enemies were her enemies. She had to avenge her.","Just then, the voice of a middle-aged woman drifted over.","“Has Fifth Miss woken up yet?”","“The Old Madam has been worrying about her. She sent me over to take a look.”","The System’s voice suddenly turned shrill. [Host, it’s her.]"]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: She's here, she's coming with rat poison","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi was in the middle of asking the system who had killed the original owner when a woman’s voice suddenly rang out.","At the same time, the system shrieked, 【Host, it’s her.】","Her? What did it mean, “her”?","Oh. It was talking about the pair of adulterers who had killed the original owner.","But did it mean the woman who had spoken, or the Old Madam she had mentioned?","The Old Madam... Jiang Yunxi drew in a sharp breath. Wasn’t that the original owner’s grandmother?","The woman who had committed adultery and killed the original owner couldn’t be the Old Madam—the original owner’s own grandmother, could it?","If it really was the Old Madam, how was she supposed to avenge the original owner?","Destroying her own clan outright?","Would she be struck by lightning for that?","Just as Jiang Yunxi was growing increasingly uneasy, the system spoke again.","【The nanny who just spoke is the woman from that adulterous pair. Her name is Nanny Kong, an old servant from your grandmother’s quarters.","As for the man, he’s her lover—the steward in charge of the stables in the outer residence.】","Good. There was no need to worry anymore. It wasn’t the Old Madam.","【Steward Ma was the one who knocked the original owner unconscious with a club. Nanny Kong then threw her into the lake.】","Excellent. She had found the culprits. Nanny Kong and Steward Ma, was it? Just wait until this young lady recovered. She would make sure the two of them paid with their lives for the original owner’s death.","The system spoke again.","【Host, there’s some juicy gossip about Nanny Kong. Do you want to hear it?】","Of course she did. This was the perfect opportunity to learn more about her enemy.","【Spill!】","【Nanny Kong was a young maid whom the Old Madam brought over from her maiden family. Later, the Old Madam arranged her marriage to a servant of the Pingyang Marquis’s Residence.","Her husband made a mistake once and was expelled from the residence.","Because Nanny Kong had pleaded with the Old Madam on his behalf, she escaped being implicated and continued serving at the Old Madam’s side.】","【Since the man had been dismissed for committing an offense, he had a blemish on his record and could never find a decent job. He survived by relying on Nanny Kong to support him.","But he was the sort of man who enjoyed living off a woman while still acting like her master. Whenever he was in a bad mood, he took it out on Nanny Kong. After suffering this way for years, the couple gradually grew estranged.】","Did Jiang Yunxi feel sorry for Nanny Sun?","At first, a little. But the moment she remembered that this woman had killed the original owner, all her sympathy vanished.","Instead, she felt that Nanny Kong deserved everything coming to her. Sometimes, only a villain could deal with another villain.","【Nanny Kong’s life was miserable, and Steward Ma happened to be acquainted with her husband. Knowing about her circumstances, he took advantage of her vulnerability and comforted her repeatedly. The two of them eventually began an affair.","And once they started, it continued for many years.】","【Oh, and Nanny Kong’s second son is actually Steward Ma’s child.","Fortunately, the boy resembles Nanny Kong, so no one else noticed anything.】","Impressive. Jiang Yunxi almost wanted to applaud them.","They had carried on an affair in a crowded and watchful marquis’s residence for so many years. They had even produced a child, yet no one had discovered them.","The original owner had really been unlucky. She hadn’t even uncovered their affair. Just because they suspected her, she had been...","【Host, this is bad!】","Jiang Yunxi’s heart jolted.","【Nanny Kong has come with murderous intent. The handkerchief hidden on her contains rat poison.】","【She’s afraid you’ll wake up and expose her affair with Steward Ma. She’s here to finish the job and silence you for good!】","Damn it! This woman was ruthless. She had actually come back to deliver a second blow!","What was wrong with people in ancient times? Did human life really mean so little to them?","Jiang Yunxi tried to call for help, only to discover that this body seemed to be beyond her control. She couldn’t even open her eyes, let alone get up and cry for help.","Sensing her struggle, the system hurriedly explained:","【Host, this body currently has pneumonia and a high fever. On top of that, your soul has only just entered it and hasn’t adapted yet, so you won’t be able to wake up for a while.】","Jiang Yunxi panicked.","【Then what do we do? Hurry up and save me!","I’m lying here completely helpless. Isn’t that just making it convenient for her to poison me?】","【You and I are in the same boat now. If one of us prospers, we both prosper; if one of us suffers, we both suffer. You can’t just stand by and watch me die.】","Although she had threatened the system earlier, saying that if it made her complete missions and pursue men, she would rather die sooner, Jiang Yunxi still didn’t want to die now that the moment had actually arrived.","After all, a bad life was still better than no life.","And besides, she would be dying at the hands of her enemy.","If she let her enemy have her way, she was afraid she wouldn’t be able to rest in peace—even the lid of her coffin might not stay shut.","【Host, I can’t do anything right now.","I can only speak inside your mind. It’s not as if I can call for help on your behalf.】","Jiang Yunxi was furious. What a useless system! She had known it couldn’t be relied on.","With such a worthless system, how was she supposed to survive in this ancient world, where she had been thrown straight into a life-or-death crisis?","【System, after I die, I’m going to file a complaint. I’ll report your entire system realm for treating human lives as worthless.","You only know how to bind yourselves to hosts. You don’t take responsibility for anything else. You’re all about killing without bothering to bury the dead.】","The system’s CPU nearly began smoking.","What should it do? Its host was about to die, and it was unlikely to complete the main system’s mission.","The system realm was certain to offend Huaxia, and it would inevitably be sent back for reprogramming as well.","The system glanced over its administrative interface. It was so familiar, yet so strange. It had to memorize every detail. After this, it might never see them again.","Suddenly, it spotted two lines of data, and its eyes lit up.","【Ding! Host successfully consumed the original owner’s gossip. Gossip Points +300.】","【Ding! Host successfully consumed Nanny Kong’s gossip. Gossip Points +100.】","Jiang Yunxi, who was preoccupied with saving her own life, barely paid attention when she heard the two notifications.","【Host, there’s a way!","I have a system shop. You can use 100 Gossip Points to unlock it, then buy an Antidote to All Poisons.","That way, even if she poisons you, you won’t have to worry.】","At that moment, the system’s voice sounded like the most beautiful, wonderful music in the world to Jiang Yunxi.","【Unlock it, unlock it! Do it now!】","【Buy it, buy it! Get it immediately!】","【All right, Host. I’ll unlock the system shop and purchase the Antidote to All Poisons right away.】","It felt as though a century had passed. In reality, less than five seconds later, the system spoke hesitantly.","【Host, the purchase failed. You don’t have enough Gossip Points.】","What a useless system!","Had it been deceiving her just now?","Didn’t it know the prices of the items in its own shop?","【How many points are we short?","Can’t you give me a discount, or let me buy it on credit?】","【Discounts and credit both require approval from the main system.】","More procedures. Always more procedures. At that moment, Jiang Yunxi hated those procedures with every fiber of her being.","【Then hurry up and get approval.】","Although she was speaking only in her mind, Jiang Yunxi felt as if she had shouted herself hoarse.","While Jiang Yunxi and the system were discussing Nanny Kong’s secrets and desperately trying to find a way to save her life, Nanny Kong had already finished speaking with the maids and matrons in Jiang Yunxi’s courtyard. She was now walking step by step toward Jiang Yunxi, who lay on the bed.","Nanny Kong’s footsteps were steady. Each step landed on the gray brick floor with a soft click-click, like someone striking Jiang Yunxi’s heart with a hammer and making her nerves draw taut.","To her ears, that sound was no different from the approach of the Grim Reaper.","She was coming. She was coming, carrying rat poison with her.","At that moment, Jiang Yunxi’s soul, which was already poorly attuned to the body, seemed ready to leave it again.","She struggled desperately to open her eyes and call for help, but her body felt as though it had been nailed to the bed. She couldn’t move a muscle, and not even the faintest sound could escape her throat.","All she could do was listen as the footsteps drew closer and closer, becoming clearer with every step, until they finally stopped beside her bed.","“Poor Fifth Miss!”","Jiang Yunxi felt someone gently stroking her face. The touch was incredibly light, yet to her it felt as heavy as a thousand jun.","That ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍voice belonged to Nanny Kong.","Clearly, it was Nanny Kong who was touching her.","Was the next step going to be pressing a handkerchief smeared with rat poison over her face...?","“How could you have fallen into the lake so carelessly and nearly drowned yourself like this?”","“Nanny, just hearing about it makes my heart feel as though it’s being torn apart. I can only imagine how the Old Madam must feel.”","Jiang Yunxi thought, “Aaahhh... That Kong woman, you poisonous old hag! Stop putting on such a shameless act. Wasn’t it you and your lover who attacked me from behind, knocked me unconscious, and threw me into the lake, leaving me in this state?”","Outside the room, a woman staggered on her feet and nearly fell."]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Zheng, what did I hear","paragraphs":["The woman was none other than Madam Zheng, the biological mother of the original owner, Jiang Yunxi, and the Secondary Madam of the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang. She glanced around, but there was no one there.","Then what had been the voice she heard just now...?","“Suju, did you hear anything?”","Suju shook her head. “Madam, this servant didn’t hear anything.”","Madam Zheng was astonished. “You didn’t hear it? You didn’t hear a woman’s voice?”","Suju shook her head again. “This servant truly didn’t hear anything.”","Madam Zheng frowned. The voice continued to ring in her ears.","【That vile Nanny Kong, that old hag! If you wanted to have an affair with Steward Ma, couldn’t you do it in your own home? Why did you have to sneak around in the Marquis’s Residence?","I caught you in the act, and because you were afraid I’d expose you, you decided to kill me.】","【How dare you two commit regicide!】","【You’ve already harmed me so badly that I’m unconscious, yet you still won’t let me go.","You actually came back to silence me a second time, and now you’re trying to poison me with rat poison.】","【If I really die, I’ll haunt you even as a ghost!】","【Is anyone there? Hurry and send someone! Save this poor child!】","【Heavens above, earth below, open your eyes! Strike this murderous pair of adulterous dogs dead!】","【My dear father and mother, come save your daughter!","I don’t want to be killed by my enemies a second time!】","【This lousy System is useless too! It said it would think of a way to save me, then vanished without a trace!】","【I don’t want to die twice in one day!】","Madam Zheng’s expression changed drastically. Even if she had been a fool, she would have understood who the owner of that voice was by now.","It was her Yunxi.","Although she didn’t understand why the maid couldn’t hear it while she alone could, this was not the time to worry about that.","Someone was trying to poison her Yunxi with rat poison.","Madam Zheng lifted her skirts and hurried forward in great strides.","Suju was stunned. What was wrong with the Secondary Madam? Why had she completely abandoned all concern for propriety?","It seemed that Fifth Miss had been running a high fever and remained unconscious for so long that even the Secondary Madam had lost her composure.","Jiang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍Yunxi felt the hand on her face withdraw.","“Why is Fifth Miss sweating so much?”","Another voice rang out, clearly belonging to a young woman.","“Nanny Kong, the Young Miss has had a high fever that won’t go down. She’s been breaking out in cold sweats constantly.”","“Then let this old servant wipe her sweat for her.”","The moment she heard that, Jiang Yunxi was terrified out of her wits.","【Ahhh! Nanny Kong, that poisonous old hag, is going to wipe my face with a handkerchief contaminated with rat poison.","If she rubs it over my nose or mouth, won’t I be doomed to remain unconscious forever?!】","【Someone help! Save me! Murder!】","【System, Main System, I hope your nineteenth-generation ancestors are doing well! I’m throwing in one extra generation—no need to thank me.】","Although she couldn’t open her eyes and see anything, Jiang Yunxi seemed to have developed a third eye. She could almost picture a fierce-looking old nanny with a face full of flesh and a vicious expression, wearing a benevolent smile as she held a handkerchief.","【Young Miss, Nanny loves you!】","【Love my head!】","【You wretched Nanny Kong, send my regards to your second—】","The door was suddenly shoved open with a tremendous bang. It rebounded, only to be held open by someone.","At the same time, a woman’s furious shout rang out.","“Stop! Stay away from my daughter!”","Hurried footsteps sounded. Jiang Yunxi heard someone rush over, shove Nanny Kong away from the bedside, and pull her into her arms.","Her face was abruptly buried in a soft bosom. That softness...","At that moment, Madam Zheng’s heart was pounding violently, as though it might leap straight out of her mouth.","The nanny standing beside her daughter just now had been Nanny Kong, the Old Madam’s personal attendant. She had even been holding a handkerchief and was about to press it against her daughter’s face.","She must be the “vile Nanny Kong” and “old hag” mentioned in that voice. And that handkerchief...","That voice had truly been Yunxi’s.","Nanny Kong had been shoved back several steps without warning. She only managed to steady herself by grabbing the bedpost.","She frowned as she looked at Madam Zheng, who was holding Fifth Miss.","Although Madam Zheng was the Secondary Madam of the Heir, Nanny Kong was a trusted servant of the Old Madam and had never considered the Heir’s concubine worthy of her attention.","She gave a cold laugh. “Madam Zheng certainly has quite the imposing manner.”","“This old servant came out of the goodness of her heart to visit Fifth Miss on behalf of the Old Madam and help wipe her sweat, yet you nearly injured me.”","“Are you dissatisfied with the Old Madam, Madam Zheng? Are you planning to defy her?”","“You’re talking nonsense! I have no dissatisfaction with the Old Madam. It’s clearly you...”","Madam Zheng opened her mouth, wanting to repeat what Jiang Yunxi had said, but the moment she tried to mention it, no sound came out.","“Yunxi said...”","She tried several more times and finally understood. She could hear her daughter’s strange inner voice, but she was apparently forbidden from telling anyone else about it.","Just then, the voice rang out again.","【This is my mother? My real mother?","Mother, could you not hold me so tightly? You’re a little too well-endowed—I’m practically suffocating.】","【Don’t let Nanny Kong and her lover drown me, and don’t let the rat poison kill me, only for me to end up suffocating in your arms.】","Madam Zheng was now one hundred percent certain that what she was hearing was indeed her daughter’s inner voice.","She quickly loosened her hold on the girl, but didn’t dare let go completely.","She was afraid that Nanny Kong might use the handkerchief in her hand...","The handkerchief! Right—the handkerchief!","Her daughter’s inner voice couldn’t be revealed to others, so she couldn’t use it to bring down Nanny Kong and her lover. But wasn’t the handkerchief in Nanny Kong’s hand proof enough?","“Quick, come and seize Nanny Kong! Take the handkerchief from her!”","“Have someone examine it carefully and find out exactly what’s on it!”","The maids and older servants in the room froze.","Nanny Kong, however, was startled. How did Madam Zheng know there was something wrong with the handkerchief?","Feeling guilty, she tried to stuff it into her sleeve while saying, “Madam Zheng, what do you mean?”","“This old servant came to see Fifth Miss out of the goodness of her heart, yet you’ve ordered people to seize me and inspect the handkerchief in my possession?”","“Could it be that you suspect this old servant harbors ill intentions toward Fifth Miss?”","Nanny Kong’s stern voice and obvious guilty reaction immediately aroused suspicion in the maids and servants, who had initially thought Madam Zheng’s order was rash.","They no longer hesitated and immediately followed Madam Zheng’s instructions, surrounding Nanny Kong.","Nanny Kong naturally tried to escape. The rat poison on the handkerchief could not be explained away.","But even with all her strength, she was no match for so many people. She was quickly subdued.","“Madam Zheng, you’d better remember that I belong to the Old Madam. You dare—”","“Enough,” Madam Zheng interrupted her. “Tie Nanny Kong up and gag her. Isn’t the physician waiting in the room next door? Go and bring him here. Have him examine the handkerchief carefully.”","【Host, I’m back.】","【Host, the Main System agreed. From now on, you can borrow against your account. The limit is only one thousand, though.】","Just like in those Hong Kong movies—the police always showed up at the very last moment.","【System, why didn’t you wait until I was dead before coming back?】","【If I’d relied on you, the grass on my grave would already be three feet tall.】","【As expected of a useless System. When it really mattered, I still had to rely on my mother.】","Still, how did my mother know there was something wrong with Nanny Kong’s handkerchief?","Could it be that she caught Nanny Kong tampering with rat poison?","The System quickly scanned the situation and soon figured out what had happened while it was searching for the Main System.","Once it understood everything, it felt rather embarrassed. It was all the Main System’s fault—why had it gone off to deal with the aftermath in another time and space at a moment like this? It had caused quite a delay.","Fortunately, the host’s biological mother had rescued her. Otherwise...","To make amends, the System scanned Nanny Kong once more and uncovered even more of her secrets.","【Host, when Nanny Kong and her lover were harming you, they were seen by a craftsman who had come to repair the railing around the lake. He was the one who told people that you had fallen into the lake.","He’s currently debating whether to use this to blackmail...】"]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: System, Where's My Compensation","paragraphs":["The System was just preparing to atone for its mistakes by telling Jiang Yunxi that it had found witnesses who could establish the guilt of those two when Madam Zheng’s personal maid hurried in.","“Madam, this is bad! The physician just said that the handkerchief Nanny Kong used to wipe the young lady’s face contained a large amount of rat poison.","“Nanny Kong was trying to harm the young lady.","“The physician would like to come in and examine her thoroughly.”","Madam Zheng felt a little annoyed that the maid had come in at such an inopportune moment, interrupting her daughter’s conversation with that so-called System.","Still, she had heard the most important part: the craftsmen who had repaired the railing by the lake on the day her daughter fell into the water. Now she knew who they were.","“I understand. Go and invite the physician in.”","Thinking of Nanny Kong’s attempt to harm her daughter, Madam Zheng knew she had to inform the Heir and Madam as well.","Although she was a secondary wife, that title was merely a pleasant one. In the end, she was still a concubine and had no authority to deal with such a matter.","“Send someone to invite the Heir and Madam too, and tell them that Nanny Kong tried to harm the young lady.”","“And also...”","Her daughter might be unconscious, but her mind was clearly awake.","Madam Zheng did not want them to know that she could hear her daughter’s thoughts.","“We’ll discuss it outside.”","Madam Zheng carefully laid down the daughter she had been holding close in her arms, then left the room with Suju.","Jiang Yunxi: [Useless System, did you hear that? Nanny Kong was caught red-handed. The rat poison in the handkerchief is evidence. We don’t need you at all.]","[You really are completely useless. When I needed you to save my life, you were nowhere to be found. Now that someone else has saved me, you’ve come crawling out to take credit.]","[From now on, all I need is my mother. She can keep me alive. All you do is send me to my death!]","The System blocked both its host and the Main System, then continued cursing up a storm. Its language was truly foul.","It was just unclear whether it was cursing its host, the Main System, or both.","When she still received no response from the System after a long while, Jiang Yunxi frowned.","[System, why aren’t you saying anything? Do you think I’m right?]","The System’s voice came through, sounding somewhat ingratiating.","[Host, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍you can’t blame me this time. It was all the Main System’s fault. It wasn’t here just now...]","[Enough with the excuses. I nearly died because of you two. Don’t you think I deserve compensation?]","[Compensation?] The System raised its volume, dragging out the final syllable. [But you’re fine, aren’t you?]","Jiang Yunxi arched a brow.","[The fact that I’m fine is thanks to you?]","The System hurriedly contacted the Main System. Fortunately, the Main System did not drop the ball this time.","[Compensation is possible.]","The corners of Jiang Yunxi’s lips curled upward.","That was right—she had earned four hundred Gossip Points from gossiping twice earlier. She had spent one hundred to unlock the System Shop, leaving her with three hundred.","But three hundred points were not enough to exchange for a Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill...","Jiang Yunxi cleared her throat.","[System, tell me about this Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill. How many points does it cost?]","[The Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill is exactly what its name suggests. After taking it, one becomes immune to all poisons. It can prevent any poison found in the mortal world.","[There are three versions. The low-grade version costs five hundred Gossip Points and lasts for five years. The mid-grade version costs seven hundred Gossip Points and lasts for ten years. The high-grade version costs fifteen hundred Gossip Points and lasts for life.]","She had transmigrated to ancient times, and she was a concubine-born daughter. There was probably no avoiding the struggles of an inner household.","Poisoning was one of the most common methods used in such schemes, and it was extremely difficult to guard against.","She really needed this Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill.","And if she was going to get one, she wanted the best.","[System, I’m a very easily satisfied person. I’m not greedy at all.","[For my compensation, I’ll take the high-grade Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill.]","[It’s only fifteen hundred points. That’s just a few pieces of gossip. It’s not much at all, don’t you think, System?]","[Beeep...]","An emotionless electronic voice rang out.","[Warning. The System has insulted its host. One warning issued.]","Jiang Yunxi arched a brow.","[System, you dare insult me? I think my compensation is too low now. That System Shop of yours...]","[Agreed, agreed. The compensation will be the high-grade Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill.] The System’s voice was filled with urgency.","It was worried that if it hesitated any longer, its host would raise the price again.","It would have to speak seriously with the Main System later. This host was far too crafty. The Main System needed to grant it greater authority, otherwise next time—","[Hand it over!]","System: [Host, you can’t move your body right now. Even if I give it to you, you...]","[It should dissolve the moment it enters my mouth, right? After all, it’s made by the System?] Jiang Yunxi asked.","That was how it always worked in the novels she had read.","The System sounded rather proud.","[Of course.]","Jiang Yunxi relaxed.","[Then put it directly into my mouth.]","Good things had to be safely secured—or rather, safely swallowed.","What good was it to leave it in someone else’s hands? What if the System pocketed it or switched it with something else?","Jiang Yunxi deliberately left the System unblocked so that it could hear her private doubts.","Soon, she felt a foreign object suddenly appear in her mouth. A sweet, refreshing flavor spread through her, followed by a warm current that rose throughout her body and lingered for quite some time.","[Host, this body was weak from birth because of a difficult delivery. You’ve been taking medicinal decoctions for years, and there’s quite a lot of medicinal toxicity accumulated in your body.","[After taking the Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill, those accumulated toxins have been cleansed as well. Your body should feel somewhat lighter and more comfortable.]","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes lit up, and she hurriedly asked:","[What about my inherent weakness?]","The System’s answer immediately shattered her hopes.","[Host, it’s a Hundred-Poison Immunity Pill. It’s for detoxification and poison prevention, not for treating illness.]","Jiang Yunxi clicked her tongue. Fine. There went her hopes.","Then perhaps the System Shop had something else...","[Does the System Shop have any medicine for treating physical weakness?","[I can’t drag around this sickly body forever. How am I supposed to go out and gather gossip to earn Gossip Points?]","Although the System had no heart and therefore could not experience a pounding one, it felt as if its CPU were about to crash again.","This crafty host—what was she planning now?","Surely she wasn’t about to demand more compensation!","[Host, let me make one thing clear first. You’ve already received your compensation, and you’ve already used it. You have to keep your word. You can’t go back on it.]","[So there is something?] Jiang Yunxi asked, not entirely certain.","[There is, but you’ll have to earn it through gossip. You can exchange Gossip Points for it later. It won’t be free.]","Jiang Yunxi felt that the System was looking down on her. Had she ever said she wanted it to give her something for free?","Could it not question her character?","Although... well, she had not actually said that part out loud.","[How many pills would I need to completely cure this body, and how many Gossip Points would they cost?]","[One Health-Strengthening Pill is enough. It’s not expensive—five hundred Gossip Points.]","Only five hundred. That really was not expensive. She already had three hundred, so she only needed to gather gossip a few more times.","There was no hurry to deal with her physical weakness. She had plenty of time in the future. Her priority now was staying alive.","She had to remember that she currently had a cerebral hematoma, pneumonia, and a high fever that would not go down. If nothing was done, she would end up just like the original host.","But she only had three hundred Gossip Points. Would that be enough to deal with all these illnesses?","She also had to save those points to cure her physical weakness.","The System had sent her into this body. Didn’t that mean it bore some responsibility?","Still, judging from the System’s reaction just now, it clearly had no intention of offering any additional compensation.","She’d still have to rely on it to make money from gossip in the future, so she couldn’t push them too hard. She needed to come up with another plan—see if she could fleece them for a little more and squeeze out some extra benefits.","Once this opportunity passed, it might never come again.","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes flickered as she said nonchalantly,","【System, we’re already bound together. You owe me the newbie gift pack, right?】"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: Newbie Gift Pack, It Can Be Available","paragraphs":["Seeing that there was no way to keep exploiting the compensation loophole and fleece the System, Jiang Yunxi could only find another way.","Her eyes turned, and she said, 【System, according to the rules of your system world, every host gets a beginner’s gift package after binding with a system.","Where’s my beginner’s gift package?】","The System was dumbfounded. Hosts received beginner’s gift packages after binding with a system? Why had it never heard of that?","It certainly had not been mentioned during its pre-job training.","Nor was there any such provision in its rules.","The System said, 【Host, are you sure you’re not mistaken? I’ve never heard of any beginner’s gift package.】","【How could there not be one? Every host bound to a system gets a beginner’s gift package.】","Jiang Yunxi was completely unreasonable, yet utterly confident. After all, she had backing.","This was her only chance to fleece the System, so how could she let it pass?","【System, don’t forget that this body is still unconscious. I have a high fever and pneumonia, and apparently there’s even a blood clot in my brain.","I might kick the bucket at any moment.】","【Are you sure the medicine in this era can cure me?】","If it could, the original owner would not have died from this illness.","【High fever and pneumonia—either one of those could be fatal in ancient times.","This body was already weak to begin with. If the fever keeps burning, how many hours do you think I can last?】","【What if I accidentally kick the bucket? Huaxia...】","Jiang Yunxi stopped there, making her point without saying too much.","Since the Main System had been so worried about her dying earlier, it should still be concerned now.","She ought to be able to use that concern to force some good things out of it.","【Putting everything else aside, you have to give me medicine to dissolve the blood clot in my brain, bring down the fever, and cure the pneumonia.","This was the original owner’s mess, after all. You can’t expect me to waste my gossip points treating it.】","At that thought, Jiang Yunxi suddenly realized that the Body-Strengthening Pill should probably be paid for by the System too. After all...","Having received the thoughts in Jiang Yunxi’s mind—and seeing the response the Main System had just sent it—the System hurriedly cut in before she could speak again.","【The beginner’s gift package, right? Yes, yes, we have one.】","The Main System had just replied that, from now on, as long as Jiang Yunxi’s requests cost no more than one thousand gossip points, the System no longer needed to ask for approval and could make its own decisions.","The Main System was worried that if it failed to respond in time again, it would be forced to pay compensation, or that Jiang Yunxi might actually die and then Huaxia...","However, the Main System had also said that it could not satisfy her every demand. Even when it did, it had to keep the price as low as possible and minimize its losses.","Medicine to clear the blood clot, reduce the fever, and treat pneumonia were all very ordinary medications. They were barely worth anything.","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes lit up. She had fleeced the System again.","But the System had agreed far too readily this time. There had to be a catch.","No, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍she had to ask for more.","【You need to prepare plenty of these medicines for me, in case the treatment doesn’t work.","Especially fever reducers. You need to prepare lots of those.","There’s no air-conditioning in this era, and winters are so cold that it’s easy to catch a cold or come down with a fever. With this frail body of mine, I could easily kick the bucket.】","The System gritted its teeth.","【Fine, no problem. I’ll put enough cold medicine in your beginner’s gift package for you to take every day for three months.】","It was being awfully generous. Apparently, cold medicine cost practically nothing in the System’s world.","Then...","【How can three months possibly be enough? This body is so weak...】","【Six months. I’ll give you enough to take every day for six months. Not one day more.】","Jiang Yunxi was delighted, though inwardly she put on a coy expression and asked, 【What about the expiration date?】","【Ten years. I’ll give you medicine with a ten-year shelf life. I guarantee it won’t go to waste.】","【Fine, then.】 Jiang Yunxi sounded indifferent. 【Give me some side-effect-free painkillers too. My whole body hurts.】","【All right.】","The System’s voice sounded somewhat listless.","There was nowhere for Jiang Yunxi to store all these things at the moment, so they could only be placed in the System’s inventory. She still felt uneasy about that.","It was like owning something without actually having control over it.","The main problem was that the System was far too unreliable.","She wondered whether the System Shop sold things like spatial rings. If it did, perhaps...","But then she thought of how the System had looked just now.","Forget it. She should not push it too far. She would still have to rely on it to earn gossip points in the future.","She had to take a long-term approach.","Still, she was a little unwilling to let the matter go.","【A beginner’s gift package definitely ought to include bonus gossip points.","Other people’s beginner’s gift packages all come with points rewards. I should get some too.】","【All right, no problem.】","Without giving Jiang Yunxi another chance to make a request, a mechanical voice rang out.","【Host, please claim your beginner’s gift package.","Would the host like to claim it?】","That was a ridiculous question. Naturally, she answered, 【Claim it.】","【Would the host like to open the beginner’s gift package?】","【Once opened, all items in the gift package will automatically be stored in the System’s inventory.】","【Open it, open it!】 Jiang Yunxi said impatiently.","【Beginner’s gift package opened. You have obtained: five Blood-Clot-Dissolving Pills, three full courses of pneumonia medication, eighteen boxes of fever reducers, ten boxes of ibuprofen, ten bottles of hemostatic powder, three bottles of diarrhea pills, five boxes of anti-inflammatory medicine, five bottles of cough syrup, five bottles of iodine solution, and 300 gossip points.】","Excellent. She was quite satisfied with this gift package.","Jiang Yunxi eagerly summoned the System interface. Her gossip-point balance was now 600, and she could also see the items in the System’s inventory.","【The Body-Strengthening Pill only costs 500 points, and I can exchange for it now. Should I...】","Forget it. She would wait until later.","That thing took effect immediately after being swallowed. The medical attendant was keeping watch over her right now. If she took it and suddenly recovered, wouldn’t she be exposed?","【System, give me some fever-reducing and pneumonia medicine first.","And don’t forget the medicine to dissolve the blood clot.】","Not long after taking the medicine, perhaps because of its effects, Jiang Yunxi began to feel drowsy. Somehow, she drifted off to sleep.","When it sensed that its host had fallen asleep, the System finally let out a sigh of relief.","That little schemer had finally gone to sleep.","In the past, when it had chatted with its seniors in the system world, they had all said that their hosts were very obedient and treated them like divine beings, fawning over them as if they were their grandfathers.","Why was its own host completely different? The host was the grand master, while the System was not even as important as a grandson.","And it was not the only one inferior to a grandson. Even the Main System...","Was Huaxia really so impressive just because it had soldiers and a military spirit? Even the Main System was afraid of it!","No, it had to take advantage of the host’s sleep and hurry to ask its senior systems what exactly was going on with Huaxia.","Clearly, Huaxia was not someone—or something—to offend.","...","After Jiang Yunxi fell asleep, Madam Zheng followed a middle-aged couple into her bedroom.","Upon seeing the three of them, the maids and older women keeping watch in the room hurriedly bowed and greeted them.","“Your Highness, the Heir’s Wife, Madam.”","Madam Zheng had been on edge the entire way, afraid that her daughter would keep muttering her thoughts and the two of them would hear everything.","Although she had already confirmed that no one besides herself could hear them, what if the Heir and the Heir’s Wife could?","Her daughter’s inner voice was completely different from the quiet, introverted way she had behaved in the past. Madam Zheng was worried that Jiang Yunxi would be reprimanded. Even more, she feared that they might take away her right to raise her.","Fortunately, the entire walk to the door had passed in silence, and only then did she finally relax.","She glanced at her daughter, who lay motionless on the bed. She did not know why Jiang Yunxi had clearly regained consciousness but still had not woken up.","Nor did she know why she herself could hear her daughter’s inner voice.","But Madam Zheng did not feel the slightest bit afraid anymore. Instead, she felt deeply fortunate.","She was fortunate that she had been able to hear her daughter’s inner thoughts and rescue her in time. Otherwise, her daughter might have been killed by that adulterous pair, while Madam Zheng herself would have ended up feeling grateful to Nanny Kong for coming to visit her daughter.","She had no idea what the System that allowed her to communicate with her daughter actually was, or whether it could awaken her.","From what the two of them had said, her daughter seemed to be short of money—so short that she had to buy things on credit.","How could that be acceptable? Although her daughter was only a concubine-born daughter, she was still a young lady of the marquis’s household. How could she ever be made to worry about money?","It seemed that Madam Zheng had been wrong to think her daughter was still young and never went out, and therefore not give her much spending money. She had allowed others to look down on her daughter.","Madam Zheng glanced at the Heir ahead of her.","Her daughter had suffered so much, and the chief culprit was none other than the Old Madam’s trusted nanny. Surely the Heir couldn’t remain completely indifferent.","Perhaps she needed to have a serious talk with him."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: Young Master, the concubine is ill.","paragraphs":["Looking at the pale-faced Jiang Yunxi lying on the bed, her principal mother, Madam Liu, said with a pained expression,","“Fifth Girl has truly suffered this time.","“It’s all the fault of that vile pair. If it weren’t for them, Fifth Girl would never have ended up in such a state.”","According to the household physician, Fifth Girl’s condition was extremely critical. She had always been frail, and after nearly drowning, she developed inflammation in her lungs. Her high fever refused to break, and there was a good chance she might not survive.","Though the child had not been born from her womb, Madam Liu had watched her grow up.","It had been Madam Liu who had arranged for Madam Zheng to enter the household back then. Although Madam Zheng was useless and had been brought in to suppress Madam Wei, she had ultimately failed to do so.","Fortunately, Madam Zheng had always treated Madam Liu with respect over the years, and the two children she had borne had likewise been respectful toward her.","Keeping the mother and son in the household helped showcase Madam Liu’s virtue, so naturally, she did not wish for Jiang Yunxi to meet with disaster.","After all, Jiang Yunxi was merely a concubine-born daughter. When the time came, Madam Liu could simply send her out with a dowry, and she would pose no threat to Madam Liu’s own children.","Although the girl was still young, she was already remarkably beautiful. If she could marry into a good family, she might even be able to support her eldest brother in the future.","With that thought in mind, Madam Liu naturally had no objection to currying favor with Madam Zheng.","“Heir, Nanny Kong and Steward Ma plotted against Fifth Girl. We have both witnesses and physical evidence,” Madam Liu said solemnly.","“They dared to commit such filthy acts in the residence and even plotted to harm their young mistress. Even if they were cut to pieces, it would not be excessive.”","“You must not let them off simply because Nanny Kong serves in the Old Madam’s quarters and was one of the Old Madam’s dowry maids.”","Madam Liu knew that, given Madam Zheng’s position, it would be inappropriate for her to say such things.","If word got out, Madam Zheng would inevitably be criticized for disrespecting her mother-in-law and overstepping her authority.","Madam Zheng could not say it, but as the lady in charge of the household, Madam Liu certainly could.","Moreover, Madam Liu was genuinely furious—and frightened.","In broad daylight, those two had dared to commit such an indecent act in the rear garden, engaging in an illicit affair.","If word spread, people would say that the Marquis’s household had terrible morals, and the marriage prospects of the children in the residence would suffer as a result.","This time, Fifth Girl had encountered them. But if it happened again and the victim was Eldest Daughter, then the one they silenced would be her Fei’er.","The moment Madam Liu imagined that the motionless girl on the bed was her Fei’er, a chill ran down her back.","She became even more determined that, even if the Old Madam objected, she would make the Heir and the Marquis report those two to the authorities and have them severely punished.","After hearing the Heir’s Wife, Madam Zheng also looked at the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang, Jiang Fengtang, with anticipation.","Naturally, she wanted those two dealt with as well.","They had attempted to kill her daughter several times. If they were let off lightly, wouldn’t everyone assume that she and her children were easy targets and continue bullying them in the future?","Looking at his daughter lying unconscious on the bed, Jiang Fengtang was likewise filled with fury.","He had few children—only four sons and three daughters—and treasured every one of them. Naturally, he did not want anything to happen to any of them.","This youngest daughter in particular had been frail since childhood. It had taken great effort to raise her to this age, and she had nearly lost her life at the hands of servants.","The household physician had even said that he could not be certain whether she would wake up, and had urged Jiang Fengtang to find an imperial physician to examine her.","Thinking of the adulterous pair who had caused all this, Jiang Fengtang hated them to the core.","He said coldly, “Let them off? How could that be? I’ll have their lives.”","“In a moment, I’ll have them bound and brought before Father and Mother. I’ll tell them everything and send them to the authorities for punishment.”","“They dared to murder their mistress. Not only will they pay, their families won’t escape punishment either!”","Madam Liu and Madam Zheng were naturally very pleased with the Heir’s answer.","Madam Zheng was just about to thank the Heir and the Heir’s Wife when a commotion arose in the courtyard, drawing everyone’s attention.","Madam Liu frowned. “What are the servants in the courtyard doing? Don’t they know that Fifth Girl needs quiet to recuperate? How can they be making such a racket?”","She turned to Madam Zheng. “Madam Zheng, Fifth Girl is still young, and the servants in her courtyard likely don’t obey her properly.","“When you have time, you should help her discipline those servants. Don’t let them take advantage of their young and inexperienced mistress to bully her.”","“If a maid or senior servant had been accompanying her this time, that vile pair would never have succeeded.”","Madam Zheng did not think the Heir’s Wife was using the opportunity to criticize her before the Heir or imply that she was an uncaring mother who had failed in her duty to guide her daughter. Instead, she fully agreed.","“The Madam is right. I have indeed been neglectful,” she said. “From now on, I will properly discipline the servants in Yunxi’s courtyard and guide Yunxi as well.”","Hearing the commotion outside, Jiang Fengtang’s anger also surged. He said sternly to Madam Zheng, “If anyone refuses to submit to your discipline, go to the Madam—and come to me as well.","“We will stand up for you.”","Madam Zheng hurriedly curtsied. “Then I thank the Madam and the Heir in advance.”","At that moment, someone outside began shouting loudly,","“Heir, the concubine is feeling unwell and wishes you to go see her.”","“Heir, the concubine is ill and wants Physician Wu to examine her.","“But ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍Fifth Miss’s people have kept the household physician here and refuse to let him go. Fifth Miss and Madam Zheng clearly don’t regard the concubine at all. Please go and uphold justice for her!”","Hearing the somewhat familiar voice, everyone in the room knew who had arrived.","It was Chunlan, the senior maid serving Madam Wei.","The maids serving the Heir’s Wife had always been given names beginning with “Xia,” meaning summer. Madam Wei, wishing to outshine the Heir’s Wife, had given most of the maids around her names beginning with “Chun,” meaning spring.","Madam Liu could not help sneering. “Madam Wei is ill again?","“Of the three hundred and sixty-five days in a year, is there a single one when she isn’t sick?","“Even Fifth Girl, who was born after a difficult delivery and has always been frail, and Younger Sister Zheng, whose health was damaged, have not been ill as often as she has.”","“She merely wants to win favor through illness. After all these years, does she think no one can see through her?”","Jiang Fengtang’s face darkened.","Although that might have been true... his wife did not need to put it so bluntly.","“She simply heard that I sent someone to summon you home early and assumed something important had happened. She was afraid the benefits might fall into someone else’s hands, so she wanted to intercept you, charm you into submission, and keep the advantage for herself.”","Jiang Fengtang’s expression darkened further.","“And now she claims that there’s no household physician available because Madam Zheng and Fifth Girl are withholding him?","“She’s so well-informed—could she really not know that Fifth Girl has been unconscious for two days and still hasn’t woken up?”","“Madam Zheng has been keeping watch over Fifth Girl for two days as well. When would she have had the time to scheme against Madam Wei?”","Madam Zheng was also seething with anger. For once, she disregarded her usual restrained nature and her habit of avoiding competition with Madam Wei. She curtsied and said,","“Heir, I did not stop anyone from taking the household physician.","“I have been here with you and the Madam, questioning those two people just now. I had no idea that Younger Sister Wei had sent someone to ask for a physician.”","“Besides, there is more than one household physician in the residence. The one staying here with Fifth Girl is Physician Chen, who has always been responsible for tending to the health of the young masters and misses and specializes in pediatrics. He is not Physician Wu, whom Madam Wei usually uses.”","Jiang Fengtang suppressed his anger and said, “I know. This is not your fault.”","Even if the residence had only possessed one physician and Madam Zheng had truly withheld him, Jiang Fengtang would still have thought it was justified.","No matter how much he favored Madam Wei ordinarily, when his daughter’s life was at stake, he was not foolish enough to lose his judgment.","Chunlan continued shouting outside, completely ignoring the servants’ reprimands. Looking at his daughter lying quietly on the bed, Jiang Fengtang was overcome by an extraordinary fury.","He strode out of the room and into the courtyard, where he bellowed furiously,","“Have you no sense of propriety at all?","“You’re nothing but an ignorant servant, yet you dare run into the young miss’s courtyard and make such a scene. You’ve shown complete disrespect toward the Secondary Madam and the young miss. Is this how Madam Wei taught you?”","“My lord, the concubine is ill—”","“She’s ill every other day. Do you really think I don’t know that not a single one of those illnesses is genuine?” Jiang Fengtang cut her off.","The servant had clearly been spoiled by Madam Wei. Instead of admitting her wrongdoing when reprimanded, she actually dared to argue back.","Thinking of his own daughter, who had been harmed by two servants who knew nothing of their place, and seeing the resentment on the maid’s face, Jiang Fengtang took his anger out on her.","“Since Madam Wei doesn’t know how to teach her servants, I’ll teach her myself.”","“Someone gag her and bind her outside the courtyard. Give her thirty strokes of the cane.","“When you’re finished, throw her back to Madam Wei and have her teach her properly.","“If there’s a next time, sell her outright.”","“And punish Madam Wei by making her copy the household rules twenty times.”","...","When Madam Wei saw Chunlan being carried back like a torn rag and heard the messenger repeat the Heir’s words, her hand slipped. In a fit of rage, she accidentally knocked over the tea set, vases, and other furnishings in the room.","“Madam Zheng, Jiang Yunxi, just you wait!”"]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: We're about to starve to death, and you're still eating melon","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi felt as though someone had a vicious grip on her stomach, squeezing tighter and tighter with every passing moment.","Her stomach was utterly empty, and the burning ache of hunger made it impossible for her to sleep any longer. She opened her eyes.","Before her was a pale pink gauze bed curtain embroidered with trailing lotus vines, and a faint fragrance lingered in the air.","Beneath her lay a soft, cool brocade quilt, smooth and delicate to the touch.","[Host, you’re awake.]","The sudden voice in her mind reminded Jiang Yunxi of what had happened earlier.","Well then—she had transmigrated!","There was no time for sighing over her fate, much less for melancholy. Right now, Jiang Yunxi only wanted something to eat.","If she didn’t eat soon, she felt she might drop dead on the spot.","Remembering her identity after transmigrating, Jiang Yunxi knew there had to be maids keeping watch in the room. She opened her mouth, intending to call for someone.","Perhaps this body had been bedridden for too long and was still running a fever. Her throat was painfully dry. She opened and closed her mouth several times, but no sound came out.","Helpless, Jiang Yunxi—whose entire body ached—could only endure the pain and raise a hand to knock hard against the bedframe.","She thought she had used a great deal of strength, but in reality, the sound was barely audible. With the quilt muffling it further, the young maid standing several yards away with her head lowered did not hear a thing.","She knocked twice more. When no one came, she assumed there was no one in the room. Having exhausted what little strength she had, Jiang Yunxi could only give up.","[Is there anyone here? Come take care of me already!","I’m practically starving to death!]","Jiang Yunxi raged helplessly in her heart.","[Even if you want me dead, at least let me have a full meal first.","Dying from overeating is still better than dying of starvation.]","[They say that if you become a starving ghost, you won’t be able to eat your fill in your next life either. I absolutely refuse!!!]","If her awful friends ever heard that Jiang Yunxi had actually starved to death, they would laugh their heads off.","When they paid their respects to her during the Qingming Festival, they would probably burn whole roast pigs, chickens, and geese for her.","Madam Zheng had spent the night in her daughter’s quarters. After taking care of matters concerning herself and her daughter’s courtyard, she returned to continue watching over her girl.","The moment she reached the outer room of her daughter’s bedchamber, she heard her daughter’s thoughts. She immediately rushed inside, taking three steps in two.","Her daughter said she was hungry—did that mean she was awake?","As soon as Madam Zheng entered the room, she asked the young maid standing guard, “Has Miss awakened?”","“No, Madam. Miss hasn’t awakened yet,” the maid answered directly, without even checking.","Afraid that no one would attend to her again after hearing their exchange, Jiang Yunxi hurriedly replied in her heart.","[Awake! I’m awake!]","[I’ve been awake for a while now. I’m so hungry I feel like I could eat an entire cow.","But my throat hurts, and I can’t call out. I knocked on the bedframe for ages, but no one paid any attention.","I thought no one had been left here to watch over me. Turns out there was someone after all.","Is this maid deaf or blind?]","Jiang Yunxi felt utterly wronged.","In all her life, she had never experienced hunger like this.","Not even during the hungriest days of her three years in high school had she been this starving.","And now she was the daughter of a marquis’s household—a noble young lady, the child of a high-ranking official.","Was there any marquis’s daughter more miserable than her? First, the servants in the household had tried to harm her several times, and now even the maid assigned to watch over her was so inattentive.","Just what sort of person had the original owner been, that everyone thought they could bully her?","Just wait until she recovered...","Hearing her daughter’s thoughts, Madam Zheng hurried to the bedside. At once, she saw her daughter awake, her eyes darting about.","That little expression on her face—so aggrieved and pitiful.","Madam Zheng’s heart immediately ached for her. She rushed forward, gathered her daughter into her arms, and began calling her “my precious girl” and “my darling.”","At the same time, she did not forget to turn and scold the young maid.","“I told you to attend to Miss in her room. Is this how you attend to her?”","“You didn’t even notice that Miss had woken up?”","“All you do is laze around.”","Remembering what her daughter had said in her thoughts just now—that she could not call out, and had knocked on the bedframe for ages without anyone responding—","The maid had clearly been standing in the room. If she had stood a little closer, or simply glanced over from time to time, there was no way she would not have noticed that her daughter was awake.","She was plainly afraid of catching the illness and had not dared come too close.","[Host, there’s some gossip about this little maid. Want to hear it?]","Jiang Yunxi was furious. [Gossip, gossip—gossip is all you ever think about!","Can gossip fill my stomach?]","[I need food to save my life right now, not your useless gossip!]","The system instantly cowered. This host was far too unreasonable.","Who said gossip was useless? Gossip earned Gossip Points, and those could be put to great use.","Hearing her daughter once again thinking about how hungry she was, Madam Zheng no longer had the mind to reprimand the little maid. She told the maids and older servants who had followed her in,","“Drag this useless girl out. When I have time later, I’ll deal with her properly.”","When the little maid heard that Madam Zheng intended to punish her, she dropped to her knees in fright and tried to plead her case. Madam Zheng, however, cut her off sharply.","“If you dare raise your voice and disturb Miss, your punishment will be doubled.”","“Cover her mouth and drag her out.”","At once, several older maids stepped forward and hauled the little maid away.","“Suju, hurry and bring something suitable for Miss to eat.","“Miss hasn’t eaten anything for three days. She’s only had a little soup, so she must be starving by now.”","[Yes, yes—I’m practically starving to death. Hurry up and bring me food.","If you waste any more time, I’ll put on a live demonstration of ascending to heaven on the spot.]","Seeing that Miss had awakened, Suju was overjoyed.","“Please rest assured, Madam. Since we did not know when Miss would wake, it would have been too late to prepare something only after she did. Food has been kept warm in the outer room the whole time.","“I’ll bring it in right away.”","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes remained fixed on Suju’s departing back, as though she could summon the food just by staring hard enough.","Looking at the daughter in her arms, who would not spare her so much as a glance and only kept staring after Suju, Madam Zheng could not help feeling helpless.","“Look how ravenous my daughter is. She really must be starving.”","Remembering that her daughter had just said her throat was dry and she could not speak, she turned to Auntie Wu, who had just returned after seeing the little maid out.","“Auntie Wu, quickly bring some water. Make it warm. Miss has been asleep for so long—she must be thirsty.”","Before the food arrived, water would do. At least she could fill herself up with it for the moment.","After drinking two cups in a row, Jiang Yunxi still wanted more, but Madam Zheng stopped her.","“Yunxi, no more. Save some room for food.”","“Didn’t you say you were hungry?”","Just then, Suju entered with another maid carrying a tray.","The other maid caught sight of Jiang Yunxi leaning against Madam Zheng and hurried forward first, tears streaming down her face.","“Miss, you’re finally awake. You frightened this servant half to death.”","“You falling ill gave everyone quite a fright.","Madam has kept watch by your bedside for days and nights on end, and all us servants have been...”","Jiang Yunxi was on the verge of a breakdown. The food was right in front of her, yet she still could not eat it.","This woman just kept chattering on and on. Couldn’t she see that the child was staring at the dishes with eyes practically glowing green?","If she had the strength, she would have pounced on the food and snatched it for herself.","[Ah... I’m so hungry! Can you stop keeping me from eating?!]","Hearing her daughter’s near-hysterical cry, Madam Zheng’s scalp went numb.","She hurriedly cut the maid off. “Suxin, forget everything else for now. Attend to your young miss and let her eat first.","She hasn’t had a proper meal in three days. She must be starving.”","“Ah—yes...”","With tears welling in her eyes, Jiang Yunxi looked at Madam Zheng, who was holding her.","[This is my mother—my real, actual mother!","Yesterday, she saved my life from that bitch Kong, and today she’s pulled me back from the brink of starvation again and again!","From now on, she is my truest, dearest mother!]","Madam ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍Zheng found it rather amusing. Was there such a thing as a fake mother?","This child had become much livelier after being ill.","That was a good thing. Before, she had seemed far too lifeless.","With the maid’s help, Madam Zheng adjusted Jiang Yunxi’s posture, letting her lean against her while the maid fed her.","In truth, Jiang Yunxi wanted to eat by herself. Being fed was far too embarrassing.","Even during chemotherapy, she had rarely received this kind of treatment.","The system’s voice sounded again. [It’s mainly because you think she feeds you too slowly to keep up with your pace.]","Jiang Yunxi replied, [No one will mistake you for a mute if you keep quiet.]","Madam Zheng: ...","“Suxin, feed her faster.”"]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Eating Melon While Watching Shows","paragraphs":["After downing two bowls of porridge, the emptiness in her stomach finally eased, and Jiang Yunxi at last had time to complain about the food in her heart.","[Why is it all porridge? This won’t keep me full. I’ll be hungry again in no time.","I want meat. Big mouthfuls of meat.]","Having just experienced what it was like to go hungry, Jiang Yunxi didn’t want to go through it again so soon.","Madam Zheng chuckled helplessly. This child...","“Xi’er, you’ve only just woken up. You haven’t had a proper meal in three days, so for now you can only eat some porridge to ease your stomach.”","“Tomorrow—tomorrow, Mother will have someone make you chicken soup and chicken-soup noodles.”","“Once you’re better, tell me whatever you want to eat. Mother will pay the kitchen to make it for you.”","Jiang Yunxi had been sick before. How could she not know that patients shouldn’t eat anything too greasy? She was only grumbling for the sake of it.","Still, how did her mother understand her so well? Jiang Yunxi hadn’t even said anything, yet Madam Zheng had already guessed what she was thinking.","Then again, given that the original Jiang Yunxi had been born weak after a difficult delivery, Madam Zheng had probably been worrying over her since childhood. It wasn’t strange that she knew her daughter so well.","With food in her stomach, Jiang Yunxi no longer felt so anxious, and she gradually slowed down her eating.","[System, didn’t you say you had some gossip about that little maid? You can tell me now.]","She had been too hungry to listen to gossip earlier, but now she could enjoy some.","After all, gossip earned her gossip points.","Besides, she glanced at the plain porridge and tasteless side dishes. She might as well use gossip as a condiment.","The host was finally willing to listen to gossip. The System could finally earn some income.","Every time its host listened to gossip, she gained gossip points, and the System could skim a little off the top as well.","That wily System had tricked it several times, leaving it deeply in debt.","On top of that, with this host’s cunning personality, she would probably find more ways to swindle it in the future.","It had to get this sly host to listen to more gossip, pay off its debt, and save up a little more. Otherwise, it would end up in debt again later.","[Host, that little maid was placed in your courtyard by your half-sister.]","Madam Zheng frowned. That little maid was Jiang Yunshu’s person?","No wonder she had been so careless in serving her daughter.","She had stayed in the room to keep watch, yet hadn’t even realized that her daughter had woken up.","Jiang Yunshu had arranged for her to stay by her daughter’s side. She certainly couldn’t have had good intentions. Madam Zheng might as well take this opportunity to drive the girl out.","Jiang Yunxi, who still hadn’t fully adjusted to her current identity, instinctively reacted when she heard that the maid had been sent by her half-sister.","[My half-sister? Who’s that?]","Madam ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍Zheng’s heart jolted.","“My heavens! My daughter has had a high fever for so long. She couldn’t have been burned stupid, could she?","‘My half-sister’? Who else would you mean? You only have one half-sister.","You make it sound as though you have several.”","Just as Madam Zheng was wondering whether she should ask her daughter a few questions to confirm that the fever hadn’t damaged her mind and turned her into a fool, Jiang Yunxi’s next thought immediately put her at ease.","[Oh, you mean Jiang Yunshu.","She’s the one who arranged for that maid to come?","What did she put her in my courtyard for?]","[What else? To spy on you, of course.","But that maid wasn’t originally placed there by Jiang Yunshu. Jiang Yunshu bought her off later.]","[That maid knew she had someone backing her, and she also thought Bibi was a sickly weakling. So whenever... she didn’t care much about serving Bibi.","Several times when Bibi fell ill, that maid was on night watch but didn’t pay attention. Bibi kicked off her quilt, and the maid, busy sleeping soundly herself, didn’t even bother to cover her.","Everyone knew Bibi was frail, but no one suspected her. That only made her grow even more careless in her duties.]","At some point, Madam Zheng had tightened her grip around Jiang Yunxi’s arm.","The pain made Jiang Yunxi swallow the porridge that had just been stuffed into her mouth in a hurry.","“Mother, please don’t squeeze so hard. You’re hurting me.”","“Ah—oh.” Madam Zheng came back to herself and quickly let go.","Worried that she might accidentally hurt her daughter again, she stopped holding Jiang Yunxi’s arm and instead clutched the quilt covering her.","Madam Zheng was seething. That little maid could not be let off lightly. She would have someone interrogate her thoroughly later.","And Jiang Yunshu could not be let off either.","She needed to take advantage of the Heir’s current guilt toward her daughter and report the matter to him, so that he would punish Jiang Yunshu properly.","Otherwise, once the Heir was bewitched by Madam Wei, and that mother and daughter coaxed him around, the matter might be brushed aside yet again.","But when her daughter and the System talked about her, why did they keep calling her “old Bibi” and “Bibi”? If Madam Zheng hadn’t known who they were talking about, she would have been completely baffled.","[By the way, she followed us to the rear garden this time.","She was supposed to hide, and that maid was supposed to find her. But the maid was being lazy and went off to play with someone else. That’s why Bibi wasn’t found until much later, delaying her treatment.]","Jiang Yunxi thought, [Holy crap. So she was an accomplice.","And she’s harmed Bibi more than once!]","[That’s right.]","[She’s Bibi’s maid. What good would come to her if Bibi died?","If she didn’t want to serve Bibi, she could have said so clearly and left.]","[How could she not want to serve Bibi? Bibi had a gentle nature and a mild temper. She rarely punished the servants, so compared with the other young masters and misses in the household, she was much easier to serve.","Her mistress was easy to handle, and every time she made her mistress ill, she could run to Jiang Yunshu to claim credit and receive a generous reward. It was practically the perfect arrangement.]","[Holy crap. So she treated Bibi as a way to make money, deliberately making her sick so she could profit from it.]","The System said, [Bingo. Exactly.]","Jiang Yunxi felt her fists clench. That little maid was utterly inhuman.","And Jiang Yunshu was no better. How could anyone be so cruel to her own younger sister?","She had known that the ancient inner households were full of unrest, but most conflicts were between legitimate and illegitimate daughters. She hadn’t expected there to be such viciousness even between half-sisters...","After sorting through the original owner’s memories, Jiang Yunxi couldn’t help frowning.","[System, Jiang Yunshu is fifteen by nominal age, while Bibi is nine. There’s a six-year difference between them.","Bibi couldn’t possibly be a threat to her, so why can’t she tolerate Bibi?]","[Bibi was already frail, and Jiang Yunshu had people make her sick time and again. She’s clearly trying to take Bibi’s life.","Could Bibi have offended her somehow?]","The System said, [I don’t know.]","Jiang Yunxi inhaled sharply.","[You don’t know? Aren’t you the omniscient Gossip System, the all-knowing Gossip System? How can you not even know this?","You knew that Nanny Kong’s lover was Steward Ma. How can you not know why Jiang Yunshu wants to harm me?]","The System replied righteously, [Host, I’m only a beginner-level system. My functions aren’t powerful enough yet.","I can only learn someone’s gossip after meeting that person. I can’t extend my investigations to other people.]","[By listening to the little maid’s gossip, I could find out that Jiang Yunshu instructed her to harm you, but I can’t learn Jiang Yunshu’s motive.]","Jiang Yunxi: Useless System.","Still, the System was somewhat useful. At the very least, it had revealed the enemy hiding in the shadows.","She just couldn’t offend Jiang Yunshu too badly for now.","[Then what do you need in order to find out?]","[You have to see her in person once. Once I’ve seen her, I’ll be able to listen to her gossip in the future and find out why she hates you.]","Seeing her once shouldn’t be difficult. They were sisters from the same household, after all. There would surely be opportunities to meet.","[Oh, and that little maid had grown very bold after getting away with harming you several times without being discovered.","The silver and jewelry Jiang Yunshu rewarded her with are all hidden in a chest in her room.]","[Jiang Yunshu is bold too. She actually gave away jewelry she didn’t even like. Those are all clear-cut pieces of evidence.]","Madam Zheng lowered her eyes. Perfect, that saved her the trouble of hunting for evidence herself.","Jiang Yunxi: This is great. Once I recover from this illness, I'll frame that little maid with some petty mistake, search her belongings, and expose the whole mess.","[Ding! Host has successfully eaten the drama of the backstabbing little maid. Gossip points +100.]","Jiang Yunxi was over the moon. Another 100 points added to her tally.","The Gossip-Eating System was the best by far, way better than those quest systems or romance conquest systems.","But she couldn't let the System know that, or it would get too complacent.","[System, from now on, every time I successfully eat a piece of gossip, report my total current gossip points, okay? That way I don't have to go check the count myself.]","[Understood, Host. Happy to assist.","Host's current total gossip points: 700.]","System, I'm so happy. I finally got some points coming in today, I'm one step closer to paying off all my debts.","Keep pushing forward.","[Host, there is a piece of gossip related to your biological mother. Would you like to eat it?]"]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Someone Wants to Harm Your Mother","paragraphs":["Hearing the system in her daughter’s mind say, 【Host, there’s some juicy gossip about your birth mother. Want to hear it?】 Madam Zheng was struck numb.","After hearing her daughter’s inner thoughts several times, and after what had happened with Nanny Kong, Madam Zheng had come to completely trust the system’s abilities.","It could definitely dig up every one of her secrets.","Although she had never committed any crimes or done anything wrong, she still had private matters she did not want anyone to know about.","And she certainly did not want her daughter to know.","That would be far too embarrassing.","Madam Zheng opened her mouth, wanting to stop it, but she had clearly forgotten what had happened the day before.","She tried to speak, only to discover that no sound came out.","Madam Zheng was even more dumbfounded. She could not even stop the system. What was she supposed to do?","Perhaps she should leave immediately. Hadn’t the system just said that as long as it had never met someone, it could not expose their gossip?","But they had already met. Even if she left, the system could still expose it.","What was she going to do?","While Madam Zheng was fretting, Jiang Yunxi was struggling with the same dilemma.","Should she hear the gossip about her own mother or not?","If she did, it seemed somewhat inappropriate.","If she learned that her mother had done something bad, how was she supposed to treat her afterward?","Her mother seemed to have treated the original owner quite well. She had stayed by her daughter’s side while she was ill. She was clearly a good mother.","If Jiang Yunxi found out that she had done something wrong, could she really bring herself to do anything to her?","But if her mother had truly committed some unforgivable evil, the education Jiang Yunxi had received would make it impossible for her to pretend she knew nothing.","Rather than being put in a difficult position later, it would be better to...","【System, I don’t want to hear it.】","System: Other than when she had been desperately hungry just now, the host had never refused gossip before. Why was she refusing this time?","【Host, gossip about yourself or your relatives earns more gossip points than gossip about outsiders.】 The system tried to tempt her.","Jiang Yunxi was resolute. 【I’m not listening.】","【Host, it’s fine. Just listen. Your mother won’t know that you’ve learned her secret.】","Madam Zheng: I know. I heard everything.","Daughter, whatever you do, don’t listen.","Perhaps because she was overly agitated, Madam Zheng shifted a few times. This startled Jiang Yunxi, who was in her arms, and drew the girl’s attention away from the system.","Earlier, Jiang Yunxi had been so hungry that although she had noticed Madam Zheng, she had not had the time to think about anything else.","Now that she was full and satisfied, she finally had time to look properly.","The moment she turned her head and saw Madam Zheng, Jiang Yunxi froze in stunned amazement. Her heart began to pound wildly.","【Oh my heavens, my mother is gorgeous!】","Madam Zheng could not help but blush faintly.","What was wrong with this child? Why was she acting as if she had never seen her mother before?","Could the fever really have damaged her brain?","Madam Zheng could not help worrying again that her daughter had been turned into a fool.","Madam Zheng was wearing a lake-blue, brightly embroidered brocade dress, with elegant orchids embroidered along the hem.","Her long, black hair, dark as a waterfall, was simply gathered into a bun and adorned with two plain hairpins.","Though her attire was simple, everything was perfectly balanced, giving her a dignified and refined air.","【Holy crap, my mother is beautiful!","Forgive my lack of education. I’ve racked my brains, but I can’t think of any other words to describe her. All I know is that she’s beautiful.","Beautiful is enough.】","【With my mother’s bearing and presence, anyone who didn’t know better would think she was a young lady from an aristocratic family.","She’s practically a fairy descended to earth.】","【With her poise, anyone who didn’t know better would think she was the lady of the house from some prominent family.】","System: 【Your mother really is a young lady from an aristocratic family. With that kind of bearing and presence, there’s nothing strange about it.","She was raised from childhood to be the lady of the household.】","Jiang Yunxi frowned. 【Then how did she end up as a concubine?】","Madam Zheng’s eyes darkened.","Was her daughter blaming her? Blaming her for becoming someone else’s concubine and making her a child of secondary birth as well?","【That’s because...】","Jiang Yunxi suddenly realized what was happening. 【System, shut up. I don’t want to hear it.","You’re definitely trying to use this opportunity to make me listen to gossip about my own mother.】","【I’m telling you, whether my mother is a principal wife or a concubine, she’s still my mother.","I believe she must have had her reasons for becoming a concubine.】","【So what if she’s a concubine? My mother is so beautiful that even as a concubine, she’s the most beautiful one.","She’s a concubine who looks just like a principal wife.","Haven’t you noticed that all these maids and nannies address her as Madam? They obviously acknowledge in their hearts that she’s no different from the principal wife.】","Madam Zheng’s slightly downcast mood instantly brightened like the sky after a shower, and she was delighted.","At the same time, she found herself both amused and exasperated. How could this child praise her mother like that?","And ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‍what did she mean by “a concubine who looks just like a principal wife”? That was not something one could say casually. A concubine was a concubine. Even if she was treated as a secondary wife, she was still a concubine.","It seemed she would have to teach her daughter properly in the future and stop her from saying such careless things, lest she attract people’s hatred.","The Heir’s Wife had already treated the three of them—mother and children—quite well.","That was partly because Madam Zheng had always shown the principal wife the utmost respect and acted with great caution, while also making sure that her two children understood their status and never competed with the legitimate children.","But the principal wife truly was fairly broad-minded.","The system was furious. What was wrong with this host? It was speaking perfectly clearly. Why couldn’t she understand?","Had it ever said that her mother was unattractive? Had it ever said that she should not have become a concubine?","It already knew why she had become one. It knew she had her own difficulties. How could it possibly blame her?","【Host, can you stop taking my words out of context?","Did this system ever say that your mother isn’t beautiful? Did I ever say she shouldn’t have become a concubine?】","【I’m telling you to listen to the gossip about your mother for a reason.","It’s for your sake, and for your mother’s.】","As she listened to the system’s voice growing even louder than her own, Jiang Yunxi inexplicably felt like backing down.","But even if she lost, she could not lose face. She absolutely could not let the system get the upper hand.","If she allowed it to climb all over her, wouldn’t she be unable to stand up to it in the future?","From beginning to end, she had to make sure the system understood who was the host and who was merely the system.","Jiang Yunxi planted her hands on her hips like a tiny tyrant and raised her voice even louder, determined to overpower the system.","【Then tell me how exactly you’re helping me and my mother.】","Madam Zheng’s ears were filled with the sound of the host and system arguing. Their voices were so loud that her head began to buzz.","Her daughter was still a child, and whatever this system was, it acted like an immature child too. It could actually get into an argument with a child.","The system grew angrier and raised its voice again.","【Your mother suffered difficult deliveries both times she gave birth. When she gave birth to you, she nearly died along with the baby.","Before she became pregnant with you, she even miscarried once. Do you really think all of that was accidental?】","Jiang Yunxi fell silent.","Madam Zheng’s heart jolted as well. From the system’s words, it seemed that none of those incidents had been accidents.","Jiang Yunxi unconsciously lowered her voice. 【So none of it was accidental? Someone was trying to harm my mother?】","Seeing that the host had lowered her voice, the system felt that it had finally gained the upper hand. It felt as if it were about to ascend to a higher plane of existence.","Perhaps it should no longer be content with remaining a basic system. After exposing gossip several times, it was probably time for it to level up.","【Naturally.","How could there be so many accidents, all of them happening to your mother?】","【Your mother is still being poisoned from time to time!】","The system threw out yet another bombshell. Madam Zheng clenched her fists, while Jiang Yunxi’s eyes widened in fury.","Excellent. Her forty-meter broadsword was already impatient to taste blood.","Niohuru Jiang Yunxi was about to make her dazzling entrance.","【Who exactly is trying to harm my mother?","I’ll find that person and hack them into pieces!】","Memories steeped in countless novels came rushing back.","【System, hurry up and tell me—is it Madam? In other words, my nominal stepmother?】"]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: It's Too Hard to Support a Family","paragraphs":["“System, tell me quickly. Was it my nominal stepmother who harmed my mother?”","Hearing her daughter ask the System that question, Madam Zheng’s heart tightened.","“I don’t know.”","Hearing that answer, Jiang Yunxi flopped backward in frustration. Madam Zheng, who was holding her, was caught off guard and fell backward with her.","Madam Zheng’s head struck the bedframe with a loud thump.","Jiang Yunxi was no better. Her head slammed into Madam Zheng’s chest, causing a second injury.","Once she realized the position they were in, Jiang Yunxi regretted it terribly.","She shouldn’t have assumed she was still on her six-foot bed, with pillows behind her and free to fall backward however she pleased.","See? She’d hurt someone again.","Her whole body was sore, and she didn’t have the strength to climb up on her own, so she could only call out, “Mother, are you all right?”","“Mother, I’m sorry. It’s all my fault. I forgot for a moment that—”","Seeing how guilt-ridden her daughter was, Madam Zheng had no time to worry about the pain in her head and chest. She quickly comforted her. “Don’t worry, Yunxi. Mother is fine.”","The maids and nanny beside them immediately came forward. They first helped Jiang Yunxi up, then helped Madam Zheng settle herself.","One nimble-handed maid hurriedly rubbed the back of Madam Zheng’s head and massaged her chest.","They had finished eating, and Madam Zheng was worried that Jiang Yunxi might get emotional again and hurt someone else. Jiang Yunxi spoke up.","“Help me lie down. Don’t carry me anymore.”","“My whole body hurts. I’ll be more comfortable lying down.”","Hearing Jiang Yunxi’s thoughts, Madam Zheng no longer insisted on holding her. She quickly ordered, “Help Miss lie down.”","“Go see whether the medicine is ready, and whether the household physician has arrived.”","“Is it bitter Chinese medicine? I refuse to drink it.”","“I have medicine from the System. It’s much more effective than Chinese medicine, and I don’t have to suffer through the bitterness.”","“If I hadn’t taken two doses of medicine from the System, I probably wouldn’t have woken up yet.”","Madam Zheng couldn’t help coughing once. They still had to prepare the medicine, or outsiders might become suspicious.","At worst, she would send everyone away when her daughter drank it and find an excuse to leave as well.","The household physician still had to examine her daughter. Otherwise, there would be no explanation for her sudden recovery.","After complaining, Jiang Yunxi continued pressing the System about the question from earlier.","“System, how can you not know whether my nominal stepmother was the one who harmed my mother?”","The System sighed. “Host, did you forget what I told you earlier?”","“By learning your mother’s secrets, I discovered that someone was trying to harm her. I also found out that the midwife who harmed her was connected to a concubine in the household surnamed Wei.”","“As for anything else, I can’t tell just by learning your mother’s secrets.”","“I’ll know once I see your stepmother in person.”","Before Jiang Yunxi could ask again, the System hurriedly added, “And don’t ask whether that concubine surnamed Wei is the real mastermind. I can’t tell just by learning your mother’s secrets.”","“I’ll have to learn Concubine Wei’s secrets to know.”","“If you want to uncover the truth, you’d better recover quickly and take me to meet your stepmother and Concubine Wei.”","“Oh, and your half-sister too.”","Madam Zheng closed her eyes, hiding the emotions in them.","Madam Wei. Very well.","You harmed me, and your daughter harmed mine. From now on, we are enemies.","Madam Wei might be favored, but she did not manage the household. The midwife she used had been hired by the Heir’s Wife. Even if the midwife had entered the residence a few days early, could Madam Wei really have conspired with her in just those few days?","Did Madam Wei even have that kind of brains?","But if the Heir’s Wife was behind it, the System should have known. It even knew about Nanny Kong and Steward Ma.","Madam Zheng felt a headache coming on.","“Forget it. There’s no point thinking about it when I can’t figure anything out.”","“I’ll wait until my daughter meets...”","Jiang Yunxi sorted through the System’s words and finally clarified a few things.","“Both of the difficult births and the miscarriage were connected to Concubine Wei?”","The System nodded, then remembered that it had no physical form and Jiang Yunxi couldn’t see it nod. It quickly answered aloud, “The midwives involved in both births deliberately caused trouble and delayed the deliveries.”","“As for the miscarriage, it happened because your mother took medicine with cooling properties.”","“The medicine was administered by a maid whom Madam Wei had planted beside her.”","“Oh, right. That maid has since become a nanny. She served your mother for a long time and is still working in your mother’s courtyard.”","“She even continues to sneak things your mother shouldn’t be eating into her meals.”","“Who is it?”","The System gave her a name, but Jiang Yunxi had no idea who that was.","Jiang Yunxi didn’t recognize the name, but Madam Zheng did. In her heart, she immediately sentenced that woman.","Now that she understood the System’s limitations, Jiang Yunxi stopped asking questions and could only say, “Next time I find a chance to go to my mother’s courtyard, I’ll figure out a way to meet her.”","“Then you can learn her secrets and expose everything she’s done.”","“Find all the evidence proving that she colluded with Madam Wei.”","“All right, Host.”","Madam Zheng lowered her eyes. It seemed she would have to keep that woman around a little longer, so that her daughter could...","This System of her daughter’s was far more useful than having someone else interrogate the woman.","People said that those who survived a great disaster would have good fortune afterward. Looking at her daughter, Madam Zheng could see that it was true.","“Host, although your mother’s health is somewhat better than yours, it still isn’t very good.”","“If she doesn’t take proper care of herself, I’m afraid she won’t live much longer.”","Madam Zheng smiled inwardly. She had known this for a long time.","When she gave birth to her daughter, she had barely survived. Being able to accompany her daughter as she grew up was already a blessing beyond measure.","If Heaven could give her a few more years—enough to see her daughter marry and have children—that would be even better.","But would Heaven grant her such a wish...?","Jiang Yunxi’s heart tightened. She couldn’t help looking toward Madam Zheng, only to meet her mother’s gaze.","Feeling the love that could not be concealed in those eyes, Jiang Yunxi grew embarrassed and turned her face away.","In her modern life, her biological parents had both been reserved people who were not good at expressing their feelings. She had never been looked at like this before.","It left her at a loss.","“System, you said that one Body-Strengthening Pill could cure my frail constitution. What about my mother?”","“Host, don’t worry. One Body-Strengthening Pill can cure her as well.”","“So you need to hurry up and learn more secrets. Then you can earn more gossip points and exchange them for the pills.”","“You and your mother need one pill each, which means you’ll need 1,000 points.”","“Like you, your mother has taken medicine for many years and has also been deliberately poisoned. A Pill of Immunity to All Poisons is necessary too.”","“You know the price of that pill. The lifelong version costs 1,500 points. Altogether, that makes 2,500.”","“Oh, and you also have a full brother.”","“His birth was quite difficult too, so his health is probably...”","“You and your mother have both been deliberately targeted. It’s hard to say whether your brother has escaped the same fate.”","In order to make its host stronger and encourage her to uncover more secrets, the System was working itself to the bone. After all, the more secrets she uncovered, the more kickbacks it could earn.","After doing the math, Jiang Yunxi felt as though dark clouds had gathered over her head. The total for her and her mother was already 2,500 points. Add the 2,000 points needed for her brother, and that made 4,500.","She could choose not to care about that brother, but Jiang Yunxi knew that in ancient times, where sons were valued over daughters, life would be extremely difficult without a full brother to support her—whether in her own family or in her future husband’s household.","Although she also had an older legitimate brother and two half-brothers, she had not grown particularly close to any of them, having spent most of her life secluded in the inner chambers.","Besides, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‍in the original host’s memories, her own brother had always treated her well. Jiang Yunxi couldn’t possibly abandon him.","Before she had even gotten started, she was already saddled with 4,500 in debt. Jiang Yunxi felt the pressure mounting.","【System, is there any quick way to earn Gossip Points?","The pressure of supporting a family is just too much.","I only have 700 right now, and I’m still a long way from 4,500.","I’m afraid the requirements will only get higher from here.】","【Yes. Consume more gossip.】","【Once I level up, the range of gossip you can consume will expand, and the Gossip Points will come pouring in.】","Forced beneath the burden of supporting her family, Jiang Yunxi gritted her teeth.","【Eat, eat, eat! I’ll consume gossip like my life depends on it.】","【From today onward, the moment I open my eyes, I’m going to hunt for gossip.","From now on, just call me the Little Gossip Expert.】","【Host, you’ve been consuming your mother’s gossip all this time. Why not finish it?","If you don’t finish it, you won’t get any Gossip Points, will you?】"]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: Your Mother Once Had Someone She Admired","paragraphs":["When the System asked whether she wanted to finish eating her birth mother’s gossip, Jiang Yunxi gritted her teeth. 【Eat it!】","She had already eaten this much of her mother’s gossip. She might as well get it all over with in one go.","Judging from what she had learned so far, her mother didn’t seem to have done anything shameful. If anything, she was the victim—the biggest innocent fool of them all.","Since that was the case, there was nothing to worry about.","Even if her mother had done something wrong, only she and the System would know about it. They could simply pretend they didn’t.","Who knew? Perhaps if she dug deeply enough, she might even find the culprit who had harmed her mother.","Madam Zheng wanted to stop her, but judging from what had happened just now, there was no way she could.","Still, simply standing there and listening to her daughter eat her own gossip was rather embarrassing.","“Forget it. If I can’t afford to provoke it, I can at least hide from it.”","Although she wanted to know what kind of gossip the System was about to reveal—and whether it would expose more details she didn’t know—Madam Zheng truly couldn’t bear to stay any longer.","“Forget it. I’ll go outside and listen.","“Judging from what happened yesterday, I should still be able to hear everything even if I’m outside...”","In any case, she could hear her daughter’s thoughts from outside the room, and without having to face her directly, it wouldn’t be quite so embarrassing.","“Yunxi, get some rest. Mother is going to deal with that little maid from earlier.”","When Jiang Yunxi heard that she intended to deal with the maid, she wanted to stop her. Her mother probably didn’t yet know that the girl had been planted by Jiang Yunshu. If they dismissed her without investigating, wouldn’t that be letting Jiang Yunshu off too easily?","Madam Zheng seemed to understand what she was thinking and spoke before she could say anything.","“She was so careless in her duties. I’m going to question her carefully and find out what she was really thinking—and who sent her.”","At that, Jiang Yunxi’s hand, which had been reaching out like Erkang’s, slowly withdrew.","【I wonder if it’s true that mothers and daughters are connected by heart. My mother can actually guess what I’m thinking.","【First she knew I was hungry, and now she knows I want to investigate whether someone ordered that little maid to do this.】","Madam Zheng felt deeply awkward inside. If it weren’t for... how could she possibly have guessed?","Unable to explain herself, Madam Zheng hurried out, taking several people with her.","Jiang Yunxi closed her eyes and pretended to sleep while focusing on the gossip.","【Your mother’s maiden name is Zheng Qingzhi. She comes from the prestigious Zheng family, a respected scholarly clan. Your maternal grandfather was once the head of Qinglan Academy.","【Qinglan Academy was founded by the Zheng family and has been around for more than a hundred years.】","【Wow...】 Jiang Yunxi couldn’t help exclaiming. 【A school with a tradition spanning more than a century was founded by the Zheng family. No wonder they’re considered a prestigious scholarly clan.】","Jiang Yunxi knew that academies in this era were nothing like modern schools, and Qinglan Academy had been established for more than a hundred years.","Many officials in the imperial court had probably studied there.","Jiang Yunxi frowned, unable to suppress her doubts.","【A woman from a prestigious scholarly family, the daughter of an academy headmaster—someone who values her reputation above all else. She’d probably rather marry a poor scholar than become the concubine of a son from another aristocratic family.","【So how did my mother end up...?】","Hearing her daughter’s doubts, Madam Zheng, who was listening to her thoughts outside while ordering people to search the little maid’s room, couldn’t help sighing inwardly as memories of the past surfaced.","The System truly had a storyteller’s instincts. It deliberately let out a sigh before saying:","【This goes back to the previous struggle for the throne.】","【To put it simply, your maternal grandfather refused to support any particular prince. He didn’t want the academy to become a breeding ground for one prince’s faction. That prince considered him stubborn and disobedient, so he decided to eliminate him.","【After a series of fabrications and framed charges, your maternal grandfather was convicted.","【He had been wrongfully accused, his reputation and a scholar’s integrity stained beyond repair. In the end, he died to prove his innocence.","【He died and escaped all his troubles, but that left his wife, children, and the rest of the family behind...】","Jiang Yunxi knitted her brows tightly. 【My maternal grandfather was framed. Didn’t anyone else do anything?】","【That man was a powerful contender for the throne. Even if people knew your maternal grandfather had been wronged, what could they do?","【And so your mother went from being a young lady of a prestigious scholarly family—the daughter of an academy headmaster—to the daughter of a disgraced criminal.】","【You also have an older maternal uncle and a younger maternal aunt. Your uncle is the eldest, while your aunt is the youngest.","【Once the family’s reputation was ruined, your mother happened to be at the age when marriage proposals came calling. Naturally, arranging her marriage became a difficult matter.】","【That was when the wife of the Marquis of Pingyang’s heir came to the family and proposed a match on behalf of the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang—in other words, your father. She wanted your mother to become his secondary wife.","【Your father had once been your maternal grandfather’s student. At the time, he asked his wife to make the proposal for two reasons. First, he was worried about his teacher’s family and wanted to protect them under the Marquis of Pingyang’s household, deterring anyone who might try to take advantage of them.】","【I have to say, your father handled that part quite well. He was much better than those ungrateful, heartless wretches.","【At the very least, he was willing to provide help when your family was at its most desperate. Of course, the fact that he made your mother his concubine is open to criticism—but what else could he have done? He was already married and even had children.】","【He had continuously supported your maternal grandmother, your uncle, and your aunt, paying for their education and daily expenses and allowing them to live with servants attending to them.","【You have to understand that, at the time, that prince was still a powerful contender for the throne.","【Later, once the struggle for succession had settled and that prince had lost, your father joined forces with other officials who had studied at Qinglan Academy to overturn the case against your maternal grandfather. They restored his good name and returned the family property that had been confiscated.","【Judging from all this, your father really was beyond reproach.】","【Host, you should know that some of the people who harmed your maternal grandfather had also come from Qinglan Academy.","【Compared with them, this System has to give your father a huge thumbs-up.】","Outside the room, Madam Zheng couldn’t help smiling faintly. Although the Heir had been rather questionable in his treatment of Madam Wei, he truly had an impeccable character.","If he hadn’t shown her family such great kindness, she would never have willingly become his concubine and spent all these years keeping a low profile and enduring everything in his household.","Hearing the System praise him, Jiang Yunxi grew somewhat curious about her cheap father, whom she had never even met.","【Actually, it was the Heir’s Wife who suggested making your mother a concubine.","【Madam Wei is your father’s maternal cousin. She ran wild in the inner household and didn’t even show the Heir’s Wife any respect.","【The Heir’s Wife thought that your mother was your father’s junior schoolmate and that, now that her family had fallen into trouble, your father had always remained concerned about her. She assumed he had feelings for your mother, so she arranged the match on his behalf, hoping to use your mother to suppress Madam Wei.】","Jiang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍Yunxi couldn’t help rolling her eyes.","How had she ended up in ancient times?","A woman arranging for her own husband to take a concubine—in other words, finding him a mistress. In modern society, that would be an utterly outrageous, world-shattering thing.","Yet in ancient times, it had become something expected of the lady of the household.","If, after she grew up, her future husband asked her to arrange a concubine for him, Jiang Yunxi felt she might consider arranging for him to become a widower instead.","Given her current status as a daughter of the Marquis’s household, even if she was only a secondary daughter, she should still receive a respectable dowry when she married.","Her husband’s family probably wouldn’t be of low status either, so she likely wouldn’t have to worry about money.","Women in ancient times didn’t need to work for a living.","As for managing household affairs, she was a secondary daughter. She probably wouldn’t become the principal wife of a clan heir or the lady of the house.","At most, she would become the wife of a secondary son or the youngest son of the principal wife. She wouldn’t have to manage the household.","That meant she could have both money and free time.","She would first find a way to move out and live separately, then arrange for herself to become a widow.","Money, free time, no need to serve her parents-in-law, no need to manage the household, and no pressure to bear children.","Damn, it was practically her dream life as a wealthy widow.","Of course, it would be even better if she could have a child or two before becoming widowed.","While Jiang Yunxi was lost in her fantasies, the System continued rambling on.","[But who would have thought that after your mother entered the household, she was so grateful for your father’s kindness to her family that she didn’t want to cause him any trouble. She always chose to keep the peace, treating those above her with deference and those below her with kindness. She never competed with Madam Wei for status.]","[That left the Heir’s Wife completely unprepared.]","Jiang Yunxi observed a moment of silence for her stepmother. She had thought that by supporting one woman to suppress the other and provoking them into fighting, the Heir’s Wife could sit back and reap the benefits.","Who could have expected that the two of them wouldn’t fight at all? Instead, another formidable rival had appeared.","Fortunately, her mother wasn’t one to stir up trouble. Otherwise, the Heir’s Wife would probably have had a massive headache.","[Still, your mother’s arrival wasn’t entirely without effect.","With your mother there as a comparison, Madam Wei really doesn’t dare act as arrogantly as she used to.","She’s your father’s cousin, while your mother is your father’s junior fellow disciple. They’re both “younger sisters”—so who’s afraid of whom?]","Madam Zheng frowned. What was that last sentence supposed to mean?","[Your mother was sabotaged twice during difficult labors and even suffered a miscarriage once. I’ve already mentioned that before, so I won’t go into it again.]","[Host,] the system said excitedly, [let me tell you something. Before your mother was married, she had someone she was in love with.]"]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: The Extraordinary Uncles and Aunts","paragraphs":["When the System said, “Host, before your mother was married, she had someone she was fond of,” Madam Zheng panicked.","How did this System know everything?","What admirer? Even she herself didn’t know about that. How could it?","And Yunxi was still just a child. How could it say such things in front of her without the slightest regard?","Madam Zheng had no idea that the soul inhabiting her daughter’s body was that of someone in her twenties—only a few years younger than herself.","It was one thing for her daughter to know about other matters. It was even fine for her to learn about the dangers of human nature. But this matter... absolutely could not be allowed to reach her ears.","But how was she supposed to stop it?","Just then, a servant entered to report, “Madam, Physician Chen heard that Miss has woken up and would like to come examine her.”","Madam Zheng was overjoyed. “Quick, quick, invite him in.”","With Physician Chen making a fuss nearby, her daughter surely wouldn’t keep gossiping about her with that System.","Madam Zheng entered her daughter’s bedchamber first and instructed her softly, “Yunxi, don’t go to sleep yet. Wait until the physician has examined you.”","“The medicine will be ready soon too. Take it before you sleep.”","And stop chatting with the System about my gossip. You’ve taken all those other medicines, so you’d better pray that the physician doesn’t notice anything unusual.","At that moment, the brainwaves of Jiang Yunxi and Madam Zheng miraculously synchronized.","【Damn, System, I woke up this quickly because of you, not that physician. But no one can know about your existence—or those medicines. If he takes the credit, won’t he be getting credit for something he didn’t do?】","The System nodded firmly. 【Naturally.】","Jiang Yunxi frowned. 【Wouldn’t that be setting him up?","What if he starts thinking he’s an amazing doctor? Next time something like this happens, he might treat someone without knowing his own limits and end up making them worse. Wouldn’t that be harming people?】","【He isn’t stupid. He should know how capable he is and probably won’t claim all the credit.】","【Hard to say. What if he...】","While helping her daughter tidy herself up, Madam Zheng said casually,","【Physician Chen does have some skill. Over the years, the young masters and misses in the household have all benefited from his care.","Your health has also been nurtured and maintained thanks in large part to him.","He’s a very modest man.】","What Madam Zheng meant was: Yunxi, stop worrying about this.","【A very modest man?】 Jiang Yunxi’s mind relaxed a little. 【Then he probably won’t claim this as his own achievement. Maybe he’ll blame it on luck—or my good fortune.","In any case, he’s taken care of my health for so many years. Even if he hasn’t earned the credit, he’s put in the work. Letting him take a little advantage won’t hurt.】","Remembering her daughter’s earlier inner thoughts, Madam Zheng suspected that Yunxi seemed rather short of those gossip points.","Her eyes shifted, and she smoothly changed the subject.","“Physician Chen has rendered great service by waking you this time. The Marchioness will certainly reward him, and your father will too once he returns from the office.","“I’ll have to give him a good reward myself later.”","Jiang Yunxi’s eyes widened. 【The physician already receives a monthly salary.","If he cures me, he’ll get three extra rewards on top of that!】","“Once Physician Chen has checked your pulse and confirmed that your condition has improved, I’ll also send someone to inform your grandfather and grandmother.","“You’ve been unconscious for several days, and they were terribly worried. We must let them know as soon as possible so they can set their minds at ease.”","“When they learn that Physician Chen cured you, they’ll surely reward him too.”","Jiang Yunxi began counting on her fingers.","Three plus two equals five.","So, after she recovered, Physician Chen would receive five rewards.","Her mother didn’t count, since she had no idea how much money Madam Zheng possessed. But the other two couples were the Marquis and the Marchioness, and the heir and the Heir’s Wife. Their wealth went without saying.","Their rewards would definitely be lavish.","【Physician Chen is going to make a killing this time.","And curing me wasn’t even his doing.】","Exactly!","Yunxi, weren’t you worried about how to earn those so-called gossip points? Physician Chen is taking advantage of you, so just dig up some gossip about him and claw back a little of what he’s getting.","Stop targeting your poor mother.","Thinking of those five rewards, Jiang Yunxi felt as though she could see piles of little coins flying away from her.","If only all that money could be given to her.","Part miser and part cheapskate, Jiang Yunxi grew furious.","【System, dig into him. When Physician Chen arrives, investigate him thoroughly.","Ideally, find out everything—even whether he wet the bed as a child.】","【He’s getting so many benefits from me. I have to find a way to make up the difference!】","Since the host had taken the initiative to start gossiping without needing any prompting, how could the System refuse?","【Don’t worry, Host. I’ll investigate him thoroughly later. I won’t even spare the space between his toes.】","That wording sounded oddly unpleasant. Jiang Yunxi looked disgusted.","【Forget the spaces between his toes. Just strip his secrets bare.】","【Don’t worry, Host. Leave it to me.】","Remembering that she had already finished eating up her mother’s gossip but still hadn’t received any gossip points, Jiang Yunxi reminded the System,","【System, I’ve finished with my mother’s gossip. Shouldn’t you give me my reward now?】","The System was bewildered. 【Finished? No, you haven’t. I haven’t even told you about your mother’s admirer from before she was married.】","Madam Zheng was numb with dismay.","Why ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍did it still want to continue?","Couldn’t this System stop while it was ahead?","【What’s there to say?】 Jiang Yunxi put her hands on her hips like a tiny shrew. 【So what if my mother had someone she liked before she was married?","Who hasn’t had someone they admired when they were young?】","【I refuse to believe you’ve never had someone you liked, System.】","Madam Zheng felt warm inside.","People always said that daughters were their mothers’ little padded jackets, and it truly was the case.","Though it seemed her daughter had learned a rather eclectic assortment of things. How did she even know about youthful admiration?","It seemed that in the future...","The System said in a small voice, 【But the person your mother liked wasn’t your father!】","【So what if it wasn’t my father? My mother didn’t cheat on him or betray him.","Even if she had cheated on him, so what? Wouldn’t that mean my father had wronged her first?】","Madam Zheng’s face flushed.","Her daughter’s inner thoughts were far too bold. How could she say such things?","She didn’t know whether the Heir could hear her daughter’s thoughts either. If he could...","Madam Zheng didn’t dare imagine it.","As Madam Zheng trembled with anxiety, Jiang Yunxi continued to let her tongue run wild.","【My father is allowed to have wives and concubines, along with a whole bunch of legitimate and illegitimate children, but my mother isn’t allowed to have someone she likes?","If he hadn’t taken advantage of her when she was in a difficult position, my mother might be the principal wife of some other household by now.】","【My mother has done nothing wrong just because she had someone she liked. Even if she had eight or ten admirers, she still wouldn’t be in the wrong.","And that was before she married. Even if she had continued to—】","Seeing that her daughter was about to say something shocking, Madam Zheng hurriedly stopped her by deliberately calling out loudly toward the door,","“Has Physician Chen arrived yet?”","Her loud voice successfully interrupted Jiang Yunxi before she could finish.","A maid’s voice rang out from outside. “Madam, Physician Chen has arrived.”","Eager to dig up the physician’s gossip and recover her losses, Jiang Yunxi no longer had time to argue with the System.","【System, just remember one thing: my mother and I are on the same side. I’ll support her no matter what.】","Seriously, her father had four sons and three daughters. What rank did she even hold in his heart? She was probably at the very bottom.","But in her mother’s heart, she might not outrank her elder brother, but she was definitely second.","Jiang Yunxi had that much self-awareness.","【That’s enough gossip about my mother. Just give me the gossip points.】","The System felt aggrieved. There was still plenty it could say about Madam Zheng, but its host clearly didn’t want to listen anymore.","Fine. It would just have to find another opportunity later.","[Host, I’ll only say one thing.","No, make that two.]","Before the host could refuse, the System began speaking directly.","[Your maternal uncle is now an official at court. He serves as the Vice Commissioner of the Office of Transmission, a fourth-rank official with the authority to participate in state affairs and offer counsel.","Your younger maternal aunt entered the palace and is now Consort Duan. She has a son, a prince who is five by traditional Chinese reckoning—in other words, your cousin.]","[Holy crap.]","[Ding! The host has successfully uncovered gossip about her mother. Gossipy Points +200. Current Gossipy Points: 900.]"]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: The Imperial Prince Cousin Is a Death Warrant","paragraphs":["When Jiang Yunxi heard that her maternal uncle had also entered government service and now held a fourth-rank post, and that she even had a maternal aunt who had borne a prince, her mind went completely blank.","Just moments ago, she had been told that her maternal grandfather had been convicted of a crime, and that his entire family was relying on her father’s protection and financial support. She had even thought that her mother must be worried sick about her family and had been scrimping and saving every day to send money back home.","No wonder she wore hardly any jewelry. Her family must be short on money.","She had been thinking that if she married, she would have to find a way to bring along a generous dowry and spend the rest of her life doing nothing. Now it seemed even that hope was gone.","After all, she had read enough novels and watched enough television dramas to know that a concubine-born daughter’s dowry was usually paid only partly by the household treasury. The rest had to be saved up over the years, with additional help from her birth mother.","She was just thinking that she would have to find ways to make more money in the future when, in the very next moment, she became a relative of a prince—a member of the imperial clan.","The change was so sudden that she had no idea how to react.","With a prince for a younger cousin, could she perhaps just...","[Host, what are you daydreaming about? He’s only five by traditional reckoning. How is he supposed to protect you? The emperor has a whole harem and plenty of sons. Do you really think he’ll acknowledge you as an imperial relative?]","[Haven’t you seen those dramas? The unfavored consorts and princes live worse than servants. And you still want to...]","Madam Zheng frowned. What was a television drama?","And how could consorts and princes possibly live worse than servants?","Did this system, which had appeared out of nowhere, even know what it was talking about?","Madam Zheng wanted to angrily demand an explanation, but the moment she opened her mouth, she once again discovered that she could not make a sound.","Jiang Yunxi frowned. [My mother is so beautiful. My little aunt can’t possibly be anything less. How could she be unfavored?]","[If she were favored, would she only hold the position of a consort?]","[You know perfectly well that the inner palace and the imperial court are connected. Apart from your maternal uncle, does your little aunt have any other support in the court?]","[Perhaps she entered the palace for your maternal uncle’s sake!]","That was true. Just think of Consort Hua. If she had not had a powerful elder brother, she would never have been favored for so many years or acted so arrogantly in the imperial harem.","And ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​‍Little Bird An had no powerful family behind her, so she could only be bullied by everyone.","[Think about why your maternal grandfather was convicted. Then think about your princely cousin. Do you still want to enjoy the benefits he brings?]","Jiang Yunxi’s good mood vanished completely.","[System, shouldn’t I be grateful that he’s still young and hasn’t been dragged into the struggle for the throne yet?]","[He’ll grow up eventually. Unless the throne changes hands before he comes of age, he won’t be able to escape it.","And because of your mother and you, the Marquis of Pingyang’s household—and even the family you marry into in the future—will be seen as being on his side. Even if you want to stay out of it, you won’t be able to.]","This time, even Madam Zheng could no longer remain calm.","As she watched Physician Chen enter with a young assistant and bow to her, she could only say woodenly, “Physician Chen, please examine Fifth Miss carefully.”","Thinking about the fate of the princes who had lost the struggle for the throne, as well as the fate of all those who had supported them, Jiang Yunxi instantly wilted like a balloon punctured by a needle.","Her future looked bleak. Jiang Yunxi wanted to run away again.","[System, do you think it’s too late for me to go back now?]","Returning to Huaxia would mean being reborn yet again, probably into another family that wasn’t particularly well-off, and inevitably becoming a corporate drone stuck working nine-to-nine, six days a week. But at least her life would be safe. She wouldn’t have to play a game where she could lose her head at any moment, or take part in some version of “let’s wipe out nine generations of the family.”","Madam Zheng frowned. Yunxi wanted to go back—but go back where? Wasn’t the marquis’s residence her home?","Seeing that things were going badly and fearing that her host might be frightened into running away again—or threaten to sever their bond and start squeezing every last benefit out of it—the system hurriedly tried to comfort her.","[Host, there’s no need to be afraid. You still have me.","As long as you gather gossip and save up plenty of gossip points, there are all kinds of life-saving items in the system store.]","[If you don’t want your cousin to get dragged into the struggle for the throne, find a way to meet him in the future and persuade him. If that doesn’t work, we can give him... you know.","Once the struggle for the throne is over, we’ll restore him.]","Jiang Yunxi raised an eyebrow. That did not sound like such a bad plan.","As long as she could keep herself alive, it would not hurt for her cousin to suffer a little.","Madam Zheng was frantic. You mangy system, what did you mean by “give him... you know”?","What were you planning to do to my nephew?","Just say it out loud! I swear I won’t beat you to death!","Yunxi, don’t let that wretched system fool you. He is your own flesh-and-blood cousin, and he is a prince. You must not listen to that system and hurt him.","If anyone finds out, the entire marquis’s household will...","The consequences would be no different from being dragged into the struggle for the throne.","Just then, a man entered the bedchamber, followed by a boy carrying a medicine chest. The system loudly reminded her,","[Host, the physician is here. Shall we dig up his gossip?]","For the sake of keeping her head attached to her neck, Jiang Yunxi clenched her teeth and decided that she had to gather as many gossip points as possible.","[Dig.]","She was having such a difficult time. Just moments ago, she had owed only 4,500 points. Now it looked as though the debt might multiply several times over.","Other people transmigrated into noble families with distinguished identities, legitimate births, and lives where they could simply lie back and enjoy themselves.","She had transmigrated as a concubine-born daughter, nearly died the moment she arrived, and found herself surrounded by wolves on every side.","She had a relative who seemed to possess an impressive status, but after taking a closer look—oh, he was actually a harbinger of death.","Madam Zheng hurriedly looked toward Physician Chen, wanting to confirm whether he could hear the system.","Judging from the reactions of the maids and older servants in the courtyard, they could not. But what if the physician could?","[Host, we’ve struck gold! There’s a huge secret.","Physician Chen has a huge secret.]","When she saw that neither Physician Chen nor his assistant showed the slightest change in expression, as if they had not heard a thing, Madam Zheng finally let out half the breath she had been holding.","The bed curtains had already been lowered. Jiang Yunxi’s hand extended beyond them, with a square of silk draped over her wrist.","She did not need to speak with Physician Chen herself, which suited the somewhat socially anxious Jiang Yunxi perfectly.","[What is it? System, hurry up and tell me.]","[Physician Chen’s name is Chen Zhiling. His family has practiced medicine for generations, and he began studying medicine from an early age.","But he has a rebellious streak. Ever since he was little, he never wanted to study medicine. He wanted to pursue literature and take the imperial examinations.","His family refused and insisted that he learn medicine. Neither side would give in, so in the end, they made him study both.]","Madam Zheng could not help sneaking a glance at Physician Chen, who was calmly examining her daughter’s pulse with his eyes closed.","She had not expected this seemingly mild-tempered man to be so stubborn. He had even refused to give in to his parents and elders.","He had supposedly wanted to pursue the civil examinations and enter government service, so how had he ended up becoming a physician after all?","Judging by his expression, he clearly had not heard her daughter’s thoughts. Otherwise, he would not be so calm.","Perhaps because mother and daughter were connected by heart, Jiang Yunxi asked the exact same question.","[Then how did he end up practicing medicine again? Did he eventually discover that he wasn’t cut out for studying?]","[Studying medicine is still studying, isn’t it? He was able to chew through such thick medical texts. The classics required for the civil examinations shouldn’t have been beyond him either.","Surely medical texts are much harder than those formulaic examination essays.]","[Host, don’t interrupt. You’ll understand once you let me finish.]","Jiang Yunxi was quite tolerant of the system when it was telling her gossip. Thus, she did not get angry. Instead, she said calmly,","[Go on, System. I promise I won’t interrupt.]","[Physician Chen is actually quite impressive. He studied two disciplines at once. At fifteen, he passed the prefectural-level examination and became a licentiate. At eighteen, he passed the provincial examination and became a provincial graduate.]","Jiang Yunxi worked it out based on the bits of ancient history she had picked up from TV dramas and novels.","[So does that mean he’ll have to take the metropolitan examination and then the palace examination before entering the court as an official?]","System: [That is correct.","But on his way to the capital to take the metropolitan examination, while passing through a stretch of mountain forest, an unexpected turn of events will occur.]","Now that’s more like it.","Jiang Yunxi clutched the quilt tighter.","Physician Chen frowned. “Fifth Miss, I’m only taking your pulse. Please relax.","Your heart is beating so fast that I can’t feel your pulse at all.”"]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: Dr. Chen of the Chen Manor, the Bandit Chief's Son-in-Law","paragraphs":["Madam Zheng listened to the System’s gossip and found herself on edge as well.","When she heard what Physician Chen had to say, she realized that her daughter might have fallen into the same trap as she had. She hurriedly said, “Yunxi, don’t let your imagination run wild. The physician just said your fever has gone down considerably. It won’t burn your brain. Just relax and let Physician Chen examine your pulse properly.”","What Madam Zheng was really thinking was: Yunxi, don’t let the System continue gossiping for now. Wait until after your pulse has been examined.","A pulse examination took a full quarter of an hour. If anything went wrong halfway through, they would have to start all over again.","Going back and forth like that would waste far too much time.","The mother and daughter were on exactly the same wavelength. Jiang Yunxi hurriedly reminded the System,","[System, wait a little longer before you continue. Let me finish having my pulse examined first.]","Although she was dying to know what happened next, Jiang Yunxi still forcibly suppressed her gossip-loving soul and made herself relax so Physician Chen could examine her pulse.","After finally completing the examination, the maid tucked her hand back beneath the quilt. Jiang Yunxi had no interest in listening to the results and hurriedly asked,","[System, hurry up and tell me! What unforeseen event happened to Physician Chen on his way to the capital for the imperial examinations?]","As for the results of the examination, with all those medicines produced by the System, she wouldn’t have any problems anyway. Who had the patience to listen to Physician Chen ramble on with a bunch of medical theories she couldn’t understand?","Madam Zheng also wanted to hear the System continue, but she still had to listen to her daughter’s medical report.","Unlike Jiang Yunxi, she did not have complete faith in the System’s medicines.","[Physician Chen encountered bandits who were robbing travelers.]","Jiang Yunxi had watched analyses on short-video platforms before. According to those analyses, bandits in ancient times generally wouldn’t rob candidates traveling to the capital for the imperial examinations.","First, candidates traveling to the capital for the examinations carried a yellow banner bearing the words “Imperial Examination by Order of His Majesty” or “Ministry of Rites Examination.” It symbolized that they were traveling under the emperor’s orders. Robbing them was tantamount to defying imperial authority.","Second, candidates who had passed the provincial examination already qualified as reserve officials and might become government officials in the future.","The bandits feared that if they robbed such a person, they would suffer retaliation later—or even provoke the imperial court into launching an extermination campaign against them.","Jiang Yunxi asked: [Even if Physician Chen encountered bandits robbing travelers, once they learned he was a candidate on his way to the capital for the examinations, they wouldn’t do anything to him, would they?]","[Under ordinary circumstances, that would indeed be the case.","But unfortunately, Physician Chen happened to encounter a special circumstance.]","[What special circumstance?] Jiang Yunxi immediately grew interested.","[If not for the fact that this particular bandit group had a female chief who took a liking to Physician Chen because he was young and handsome, then...]","Madam Zheng coughed several times.","Physician Chen asked, “Madam, what’s wrong?”","Madam Zheng waved her hand. “Nothing, nothing. I accidentally choked on my saliva.”","Jiang Yunxi thought: [My mother is still like a child. She can even choke on her saliva while talking.","I never do that.]","Madam Zheng clenched her fist. “It’s all because of you, you little ingrate.","I ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​‍wonder if you’ve been reading too many romance stories lately. You’ve actually picked up all sorts of indecent ideas.”","“Looks like I’ll have to be more careful from now on. Yunxi isn’t allowed to read those trashy stories anymore. They’ve completely warped her temperament.”","Seeing that Madam Zheng was all right, Jiang Yunxi urged the System on,","[System, hurry up and tell me! Did some female bandit chief take a fancy to Physician Chen and want to drag him up the mountain to become her husband?]","The System replied: [There was no female bandit chief or bandit chieftain’s husband, but there was a bandit chieftain’s son-in-law.]","[The bandit chief had no sons, only one daughter. She loved reading stories about talented scholars and beautiful maidens and wanted to marry a scholar.","But she was the bandit chief’s daughter. Which scholar would be willing to marry her?","Then they just happened to run into Physician Chen, that unlucky fellow. He was not only a scholar, but a provincial graduate on his way to the capital for the examinations—far more impressive than an ordinary scholar.","Those bandits wanted to curry favor with their young mistress, so they tied him up, hauled him up the mountain, and presented him to her.]","Jiang Yunxi’s mind had already conjured up a scene of a beautiful woman forcing herself on a scholar—a scene that would need to be censored before anyone could watch it.","[What happened afterward? Did Physician Chen submit?] she asked impatiently.","Madam Zheng stole a glance at Physician Chen.","“Physician Chen has been living in our residence for all these years, but I’ve never heard of him having a wife. He does have a son, though.”","[Let me tell you, Host. The story between those two was absolutely spectacular. First they... then they... and finally they...]","Jiang Yunxi’s strange laughter grew louder and louder as she exclaimed,","[System, be more detailed. Explain it properly.]","[System, how did the bandit chieftain’s daughter overpower him? What position did they use? Be specific.]","[System, you can’t just skim over this part. Go on, tell me...]","Madam Zheng’s face grew darker and darker. Several times, she opened her mouth to speak, but no words came out.","Her expression left Physician Chen and all the maids and matrons nearby utterly baffled.","Fifth Miss was already in much better condition than she had been yesterday. Yet judging from Madam Zheng’s expression, she seemed even less satisfied.","In fact, she looked even more dissatisfied than yesterday.","What exactly did Madam Zheng think? Did she feel that Fifth Miss shouldn’t have recovered, or that she was recovering too slowly?","But comparing her attitude yesterday with today, it really did look as though she felt Fifth Miss shouldn’t have gotten better at all.","Could it be that Madam Zheng thought Fifth Miss’s frail body, constantly falling ill every few days and dragging her down, would be better off if she simply didn’t survive this time?","Fifth Miss had been harmed by someone from the Marchioness’s household. If Fifth Miss truly failed to recover, Madam Zheng and her son could use the Marchioness’s guilt to obtain quite a few benefits.","Oh, heavens! Madam Zheng usually appeared to be such a loving mother, always showing Fifth Miss how much she cared about her. Who would have thought she was actually this kind of person?","Madam Zheng had no idea that her dark expression, caused by hearing her daughter’s rather bold and rather scandalous words, had ruined her reputation.","Everyone else had already assumed she was planning to use her daughter’s death to gain power and benefits.","[That’s how the two of them really got together, and the bandit chieftain’s daughter became pregnant.]","[Unfortunately, the bandit chieftain’s daughter later died in childbirth. There was no doctor on the mountain, and Physician Chen was the only one there. Although he did his best, he still couldn’t save her.","Fortunately, he was able to save their son.]","Hearing this, even Jiang Yunxi couldn’t help sighing.","The two of them had clearly come to love each other. They had wanted to spend the rest of their lives together. Why couldn’t Heaven have let them?","[Later, another bandit group took a fancy to that mountain stronghold because of its dangerous terrain. The original bandits were no match for them. Most of them were killed, while the rest fled down the mountain to save their lives.","To protect his son-in-law and grandson, the bandit chief suffered severe injuries. Physician Chen did everything he could to treat him, but he still failed to save him.]","[Why didn’t he take the imperial examinations again after coming down the mountain?]","The System replied: [He had spent several years living in a bandit’s den. How could he explain that to anyone?","If he told the truth, his son would become the son of a bandit. And afterward...]","[In fact, that entire bandit group had originally gone up into the mountains because they had been driven to it by famine. They had only done so to survive and hadn’t committed any truly heinous acts.","They were all dead. Why make it so that their names would never rest in peace even after death?]","[His wife had risked her life to give birth to their son.","His father-in-law had treated him well throughout all those years and had ultimately sacrificed his own life to protect him and his son. How could Physician Chen bear to ruin their reputations after death?]","[Physician Chen regretted only that his medical skills had been inadequate and that he had been unable to save his wife and father-in-law.","After that, he gave up on the imperial examinations and devoted himself to studying medicine.","He feared that if he took another wife, his second wife might mistreat the son whom his wife and father-in-law had given their lives to protect. So he never remarried and raised his son alone.]","Through the bed curtains and folding screen, Jiang Yunxi watched Physician Chen’s silhouette as he wrote out the prescription.","【System, Physician Chen really is a good man. The Eldest Miss didn’t choose the wrong man to abduct as her husband!】","System: 【He certainly is a good man—and a good father.】","Madam Zheng couldn’t help agreeing inwardly.","Jiang Yunxi: 【He’s much better than my deadbeat father.】","System: Are you really brave enough to let your father hear that?"]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: My Mother Is My Mother, But My Father May Not Be My Father","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunxi: “System, how many concubines does my father have?","Three, four, five, or ten?","With a beauty like my mother, he doesn’t know how to treat her properly and even lets Madam Wei bully her. What is wrong with him?","Is ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‍Madam Wei even as beautiful as my mother?","With so many concubines, plus his wife, how has he not exhausted himself to death yet...”","Madam Zheng’s forehead creased with worry. Afraid her daughter might say something even more outrageous, she hurriedly called out loudly, “Someone, take the prescription to the pharmacy and have the medicine prepared!”","She successfully cut off whatever her daughter had been about to say.","Jiang Yunxi: “...”","“My mother looks so gentle. Why is she always making such a fuss? She scares me half to death every time.”","Madam Zheng clenched her teeth.","Although she was happy that her daughter was defending her, could the girl please stop spouting such outrageous nonsense?","Otherwise, Madam Zheng feared that one day her foolish daughter would anger her to death.","For now, Jiang Yunxi was only saying these things in her thoughts. But what if she accidentally blurted them out one day?","Or what if the Heir could hear her thoughts too? Then...","The System: “Host, if your father doesn’t take concubines, you won’t exist!”","Jiang Yunxi pouted. “Who says I wouldn’t exist?","If my mother hadn’t married my father, then with her looks, grace, and character, she might have become the principal wife of some other household.","And I would have followed my mother and become a legitimate young lady.”","Madam Zheng sighed. Child, given your mother’s circumstances back then, no prominent family would have dared marry me as their wife.","Even those who came to propose marriage mostly wanted me as a concubine, or even as a mistress.","If not for that, I would never have readily agreed when the Heir’s Wife came to ask me to become a secondary wife and even took the initiative to offer to look after my family.","It was true that your father favored Madam Wei, but I never resented him. In fact, I was even very grateful to him.","The System: “... Without your father, how could your mother have given birth to you?”","Jiang Yunxi: “System, that’s where you’re mistaken.","I was born by my mother, not by my father.","My mother is definitely my biological mother, but my father might not be my biological father!”","Madam Zheng’s fists tightened.","What was this foolish child implying? Was she suggesting that Madam Zheng had cheated on the Heir?","Very well. In a little while...","Forget it. She would wait until the child recovered before finding an excuse to beat her.","Otherwise, she would never be able to vent her anger.","The System: “Host, your mother would be furious if she heard that.","Although your mother had someone she loved before she married, she never did anything that betrayed your father.”","Jiang Yunxi: “...”","Oh no. She hadn’t explained herself clearly and had caused a misunderstanding.","“I didn’t mean it that way.","I mean that children are born by women, not men.","A child comes out of a woman’s womb, so the woman naturally knows that the child is hers.","When a child reincarnates, it also enters the woman’s womb specifically because of her.","“So even if my mother hadn’t married my father, I could still have reincarnated as my mother’s child.","But my father might not have been my father—unless I had been willing to change my mother.”","“System, do you understand what I mean now?”","The System: “It’s a little convoluted, but I understand.”","Madam Zheng understood as well.","Her heart filled with joy. This child simply loved clinging to her. She would rather change fathers than change mothers.","Forget it. Since the child had such a loving heart, Madam Zheng would let go of her earlier misunderstanding and not find an excuse to beat her.","Still, she had to find an opportunity to remind the girl to be more careful with her words in the future. She was always saying things that could easily be misunderstood.","Physician Chen, the maids, and the nurses all stood nearby, watching Madam Zheng’s expressions change.","One moment, her face was as dark as the bottom of a pot; the next, she was beaming with joy.","Look at what the Fifth Miss’s misfortune had done to Madam Zheng.","She had originally been a gentle, perfectly normal woman, but now she seemed to have lost her mind.","Jiang Yunxi’s senior maid, Suxin, said, “Madam must not keep watch over Miss tonight. Madam hasn’t rested properly for several days, and she’s beginning to lose her mind.”","Physician Chen felt that he could no longer stay. What if Madam Zheng suddenly went completely mad?","“Madam, the Fifth Miss has regained consciousness. Have the medicine prepared and boiled according to the prescription, then give it to her.","“After that, simply take good care of her as I instructed earlier.","“I’ll take my leave now and return this afternoon.”","Jiang Yunxi: “I have to take medicine? And it’s traditional Chinese medicine!”","“System, quickly prepare some medicine for me. I’ll take one dose, then go straight to sleep.","“If I fall asleep before the medicine is ready, I won’t have to drink it.”","Madam Zheng: “...”","“You’re quite clever, using sleep to avoid taking your medicine.","“But once you wake up, won’t you still have to drink it?”","Forget it. She would think of a way to help her later.","What if the two different medicines conflicted and made her ill?","The System: “Host, we haven’t finished with Physician Chen’s gossip yet.”","“We haven’t? No wonder you didn’t give me any gossip points.”","“Then go on.”","“Physician Chen’s son is already twenty-one, yet he still hasn’t married. Do you know why?”","“Twenty-one isn’t that old. Why the rush?”","“Host, men here usually marry at seventeen or eighteen. Some even marry at fifteen or sixteen.","“Physician Chen’s son is already twenty-one, and not only is he unmarried, he doesn’t even have a betrothal arranged. He’s already an old bachelor.”","All right. Her modern way of thinking had taken a moment to catch up. She had forgotten that this was ancient times.","The System had specifically brought up Physician Chen’s son, so it clearly wasn’t doing so without reason.","So was it because...","“Physician Chen’s son is gay. He doesn’t like women; he likes men.","“But that isn’t permitted in this era, so he’s been putting off marriage.”","As Madam Zheng was seeing Physician Chen out, she walked straight into the door.","“Madam, are you all right?” the nurse cried out in alarm.","Jiang Yunxi: “What happened to my mother again?”","The System: “She wasn’t watching where she was going and walked into the door.”","Jiang Yunxi: “...”","“Why can’t she ever take proper care of herself?","“She must have had people looking after her constantly to grow up this far.","“She’s either choking on her own saliva or walking into doors.","“I’ll have to tell her maids and nurses to keep an eye on her at all times from now on.”","Madam Zheng gritted her teeth.","Thank you for your concern.","As long as you stop blurting out shocking things every so often, I won’t end up like this.","Before, I couldn’t hear my daughter’s thoughts, and I had no idea she was this wild and unpredictable.","I was completely fooled by that quiet, reserved demeanor of hers.","Madam Zheng no longer knew whether suddenly gaining this ability was a blessing or a curse.","After hearing Madam Zheng tell the nurse that she was fine, Jiang Yunxi relaxed.","“System, hurry up and tell me whether Physician Chen’s son is gay.”","“What are they going to do? Physician Chen has only one son. If he’s gay and refuses to marry, what will happen to his family line?","“Although he hasn’t returned to the Chen family, there should be other members of the Chen family to carry on the family line. But his mother’s family line will end with him.","“People in this era place so much importance on that.”","The System: “Don’t worry. His son isn’t gay.","“He simply thinks his parents’ love is beautiful and wants a relationship just like theirs.”","Jiang Yunxi: “He wants a relationship like theirs? What does that mean?","“Does he also want to find the daughter of a bandit chief?”","“Mm-hmm.”","“He studied medicine under his father. Last year, he said he wanted to travel as an itinerant physician to broaden his experience.","Actually, he was looking for a bandit stronghold that wasn’t too ruthless and had a young lady in charge, so he could be kidnapped and taken up the mountain······】","【Hahahaha, is he insane?!","Everyone else avoids bandits, but he’s actually delivering himself straight to their doorstep.】","Madam Zheng covered her mouth with her handkerchief. She, too, felt that Physician Chen’s son seemed to be seriously unwell.","Why didn’t Physician Chen treat him?","It was true that doctors couldn’t treat themselves, but no one had said they couldn’t treat their own family.","【Isn’t he afraid they’ll just chop him up?!】","【Don’t worry, he isn’t stupid. He brought people with him and will scout the place out in advance.","Besides, he grew up in the Marquis’s residence and learned some martial skills from the guards. He’ll have no problem protecting himself.】","【System, do you think he’ll find one?】","The system replied, 【You’re asking me? Who am I supposed to ask?】","Jiang Yunxi said, 【Then I’ll just pray that he comes back safe and sound. It would be best if he finds one.","Otherwise, Physician Chen is going to be far too pitiful.】","What Jiang Yunxi didn’t know was that her words had stirred the merit earned by the soldiers who protected her, triggering certain reactions."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: The Poor Little Thing Unloved by Dad and Unloved by Brother","paragraphs":["“Dong’er, I’m giving you tomorrow off. Go home for the day,” Jiang Yunxi told the little maid in the courtyard.","Dong’er smiled. “Miss, there’s no need. I don’t have anything to do at home, so you don’t have to give me the day off.”","Ever since her mother died and her father married her stepmother, Dong’er had disliked going home.","Especially after her stepmother gave birth to a son, she became even less willing to return.","Every time she went back, her stepmother and father would rack their brains trying to get money from her.","Her monthly wages were never enough for them. They always had to find a way to squeeze even more money out of her.","Her little brother was the same. Every time she went home, he would drag her off to buy snacks—an entire pile of them—and wouldn’t give her even one bite.","He ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‍was always saying things like, “If you don’t give me money to spend now, then once you get married, I won’t stand up for you.”","“Mother said you’re nothing but a money-losing good-for-nothing. The money you earn is meant to be spent on me. If I don’t spend it now, it’ll be hard to spend it once you’re married.”","Jiang Yunxi did not hold back at all. “You have to go home. You absolutely must go.","“You’ve worked so hard taking care of me these past few days. You should take a proper day off and get some rest.”","If you don’t go home tomorrow, how will you run into your stepmother selling you for ten taels of silver to a forty-year-old lame man as his second wife?","That lame man has already had three wives die. Every one of them was beaten to death by him.","You’re only fourteen or fifteen years old, and you’ve served the original owner faithfully for several years. How could I bear to let you walk straight into a pit of fire?","Besides, hearing your story earns me one hundred gossip points. Of course I have to save you.","But if she goes back alone, she probably won’t be able to handle them. Should I send someone with her to give her an extra hand?","Who should I send?","Jiang Yunxi glanced left and right. None of the maids in her room seemed suitable. They were all too mild-tempered, and none of them were a match for her stepmother.","Madam Zheng suddenly spoke up. 【Since Miss wants you to go home, then go. Don’t let Miss’s kindness go to waste.】","【Go in the morning and come back in the afternoon.】","Having already learned everything from her daughter’s inner voice, Madam Zheng naturally could not stand by and watch the maid at her daughter’s side get bullied.","【Your home isn’t in the capital, so it’s inconvenient to travel back and forth. How about this? I’ll make arrangements shortly. The household will send a carriage, along with a matron and a guard to accompany you.】","Otherwise, Madam Zheng feared the girl might go home and never return.","Which matron should she send? Oh, right. Aunt Zhang from her own courtyard would be perfect. She was strong and sharp-tongued, and she would definitely leave that stepmother speechless.","Still, solving the problem this once wouldn’t prevent that stepmother from resorting to other tricks later. What then...?","Dong’er saw that both Miss and Madam were insisting, and had even arranged a carriage for her. Knowing it would be rude to refuse their kindness again, she could only say, “Thank you, Madam. Thank you, Fifth Miss.”","Jiang Yunxi had not expected her mother to solve the problem that had been troubling her.","“Mother, send a particularly sharp-tongued matron. Dong’er told me before that her stepmother is a formidable woman who bullies her all the time.”","Madam Zheng nodded. “Don’t worry. I’ll make sure we send someone fierce.”","Jiang Yunxi then reminded Dong’er, “No matter what happens when you go home, just remember this: you are my maid. If anything happens, I’ll stand up for you. No one else is allowed to bully you.”","Now that she had said this, and with someone from her mother’s side protecting Dong’er, the girl should not end up being forced to marry that wife-beater and dying soon afterward, as the system had said.","Madam Zheng also admonished Dong’er, “Miss is right. Whatever happens, Madam and Fifth Miss will stand up for you.”","The girl had signed a service contract with the household, not a lifetime indenture. If it had been a lifetime indenture, her stepmother would never have been able to interfere in her marriage.","After seeing what happened tomorrow and recognizing the true faces of her stepmother and father, perhaps the girl would finally see things clearly.","If she was willing to sign a lifetime contract, Madam Zheng intended to sign one with her privately, without going through the household, and put the contract in her daughter’s keeping.","After what had happened with the maid who betrayed her master, Madam Zheng felt that the maids serving her daughter should be people personally chosen by them, rather than servants belonging to the household.","With the contract in her daughter’s hands, the girl’s very life and death would be under her daughter’s control. Even if someone tried to bribe her into betrayal, she would have to think carefully before turning against her mistress.","Although the maids did not know why Miss had suddenly decided to send Dong’er home, they could tell from the way Madam and Miss were treating her—and from the special arrangements being made—that something unusual must be going on.","The small amount of resentment they had felt in their hearts immediately faded.","Madam Zheng was no fool. She naturally understood that her daughter’s sudden concern and special treatment of Dong’er might make the other maids feel resentful, so she quickly added, “Suxin, the same goes for all of you.”","“You’ve worked day and night taking care of Yunxi while she was ill. You’ve all had a hard time.”","“Once Yunxi has fully recovered, you’ll take turns having a day off. You can each rest for one day.","“For those of you born into servant families here, there’s no need to send a carriage to take you home. Madam will simply give you a generous allowance instead.”","“For those of you who aren’t household-born servants, Madam will arrange a carriage and a guard to escort you home.”","When the others heard that Dong’er was not the only one receiving such treatment, what was there left to resent?","They rose one after another and bowed, thanking Madam and Miss.","Jiang Yunxi felt terribly guilty. She had forgotten that fairness mattered—people did not mind having less, but they did mind others having more.","Fortunately, her mother had helped smooth things over.","Still, this meant her mother would have to spend quite a bit of money.","Thinking of her own rather meager private savings, Jiang Yunxi decided she would have to find a way to make some money.","Her mother was out of the question. She was a concubine, and given the circumstances under which she had entered the household all those years ago, she probably did not have much money on hand.","That meant she could only get money from my deadbeat father.","Right, where was her deadbeat father? She had a perfectly good father, so why had he never shown his face?","His daughter had nearly died, yet he had not even come to see her.","Even Madam, her grandfather, and her grandmother had sent people to visit after learning she had regained consciousness. Every one of them had brought gifts.","They were all medicinal herbs—good-quality ones, to be sure—but they weren’t money!","And she desperately needed money right now.","But where was her father? How could he not come?","Did he really care so little about her?","Jiang Yunxi frowned, once again worrying about her future. A neglected illegitimate daughter who was not favored by her own father—her future looked completely bleak.","She had wanted to coast through life, but with treatment like this, how could she possibly lie low and live comfortably?","【System, my father really doesn’t care about me, does he? I’ve been awake for three days, and he hasn’t even come to see me.","【This wasn’t some minor illness. I barely escaped death, and he still hasn’t come.","【Does he really dislike me that much?】","【System, can I exchange him for another father?】","【Right, I have an older brother too—my own biological brother—and he hasn’t come to see me either.","【I could understand if my half-brothers, half-sisters, and younger siblings didn’t come, but what gives him the right not to come?","【Can I disown this brother?】","【He even claimed he doted on me. It was all fake.】","【System, I’m just a pitiful little girl whose father doesn’t love her and whose brother doesn’t care about her.","【Ugh, take back the part about Mother not loving me. Mother still loves me. But I’m still a pitiful little girl whose father doesn’t love her and whose brother doesn’t care about her.","【How did I, Jiang Yunxi, end up in such a miserable state?】","Madam Zheng pressed a hand to her forehead. This girl...","She was just about to explain when she suddenly stopped.","If she explained now—right after her daughter had asked those questions—wouldn’t that expose the fact that she could hear her daughter’s inner voice?","Although her daughter’s thoughts could be irritating at times, she had to admit they were also quite entertaining.","At the very least, over the past few days, she had learned quite a few things about the maids and matrons in the courtyard through her daughter’s inner voice.","There was nothing more useful than knowing exactly who was whose spy and who was loyal and who was not.","Just as Madam Zheng was about to make up an excuse to explain why the heir and her son had not come to see her daughter, a sudden cry of alarm rang out from the courtyard.","“Young Master, how did you fall?”"]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: A Pair of Fools","paragraphs":["Jiang Yunzheng was twelve by nominal age and was currently studying at Qinglan Academy.","Although Qinglan Academy had briefly changed headmasters, not long after the previous succession struggle ended, the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang joined forces with several other officials who had graduated from Qinglan Academy to clear the headmaster’s name. Before long, the academy was once again returned to the Zheng family.","Uncle Zheng was still young and had already made up his mind to enter government service, so it would not be suitable for him to take over as headmaster of Qinglan Academy. Thus, he made the decision to select someone from a branch of the Zheng family who was outstanding in character and reputation and devoted to teaching and cultivating students to serve as headmaster.","In the current dynasty, apart from entering office through hereditary privilege or imperial favor, anyone who wished to become an official had to follow the regular path and pass the examinations step by step.","Under the rules governing hereditary privilege and imperial favor, the sons of noble families were allotted one or two places per household to study at the Imperial College. They could then take the metropolitan examination directly—the Spring Examination, held in the capital the spring after the Autumn Examination—without first having to sit the preliminary examinations.","The preliminary examinations consisted of the county and prefectural examinations, held once a year and presided over by the county magistrate and prefect. Those who passed were called licentiates-in-training; the academy examination, held twice every three years and presided over by the provincial education commissioner, after which successful candidates became licentiates; and the provincial examination, also known as the Autumn Examination, held once every three years, after which successful candidates became provincial graduates.","Jiang Yunzheng ranked fifth among the Marquis of Pingyang’s many grandchildren and was the third son of the Heir to the Marquis of Pingyang. Having no hereditary privilege quota left, he could only work his way up by taking the examinations step by step.","Fortunately, the Zheng family had Qinglan Academy. As a grandson of the Zheng family on his mother’s side, he did not need to find a way to secure a place there.","Qinglan Academy followed a ten-day schedule, with one day of leave after every ten days of classes. Today was the tenth day.","After finishing a full day of lessons, he packed up the bedding and luggage he needed to bring home. The moment he returned to the residence and entered the courtyard, he received some terrible news.","His younger sister, Jiang Yunxi, had fallen into a lake and remained unconscious for three days and three nights. She had only woken up the day before yesterday.","The moment Jiang Yunzheng heard this, he grew anxious. His sister had been unconscious for several days—his mother must have been frantic with worry. Why had no one gone to the academy to inform him?","He set down his things and, without even changing his clothes, hurried toward the rear courtyard.","The moment he entered his sister’s courtyard, he heard someone shouting about how her father did not love her and her brother did not care about her.","She had been so sick, yet they had not even come to see her.","Although the voice did not sound like his sister’s, it was clearly calling her Jiang Yunxi.","Who else could Jiang Yunxi be but his own sister?","His sister was even shouting that she wanted to exchange her father for a new one and did not want this brother of hers anymore.","How could Jiang Yunzheng withstand that? In his shock, he failed to watch his step, tripped over his own feet, and fell flat on his face.","Meanwhile, Jiang Yunxi was still complaining to the system.","[System, I’ve been sick for so long. I was unconscious for several days and have been awake for several days. Altogether, that makes six or seven days. Yet neither my father nor my brother has shown his face.","This clearly means they don’t care about me.]","With the help of his page, Jiang Yunzheng got to his feet and let the boy brush the dust off his clothes.","“Yanqing, did you hear something?”","Yanqing said, “Of course I heard something, Young Master. You fell so hard, and you hit the ground with such a loud thump. I’m not deaf—how could I not hear it?","“Not only did I hear the thump, I also heard you cry out in pain.”","Jiang Yunzheng had no mind to trade jokes with his page. “That isn’t what I’m talking about. I mean, did you hear Little Sister speaking?”","“Fifth Miss’s voice?”","Yanqing turned around and looked everywhere. “Fifth Miss isn’t even here. How could you have heard her speaking?”","Jiang Yunxi: [If they don’t care about me, then I won’t care about them either.","I don’t want them anymore.","System, do you think that’s all right?]","“Listen! She’s speaking again. Yanqing, can’t you hear her?”","Yanqing poked his head out and looked around once more. “Young Master, you must be imagining things. Fifth Miss isn’t here, and no one was speaking just now.”","As luck would have it, Jiang Yunxi fell silent at that very moment.","Jiang Yunzheng was no longer certain himself.","“Perhaps I heard wrong.”","Shuyin was waiting in the outer room. Jiang Yunzheng went straight to Jiang Yunxi’s bedroom.","They were brother and sister, and he could hear that there were quite a few people inside, so there was no need to observe so many formalities.","The moment he entered, all the maids and matrons in the room hurriedly bowed and greeted him.","“Fifth Young Master.”","When Jiang Yunzheng saw Madam Zheng, he immediately bowed.","“Greetings, Mother.”","At that moment, the voice he had heard earlier rang out again.","[Well, speak of the devil and he appears.","This is my own brother, is it? The brother whose sister was sick like this and unconscious for several days, yet he never even showed his face!]","The final note was drawn out, dripping with mockery.","Jiang Yunzheng abruptly looked up at his younger sister, who was sitting propped up in bed.","She was smiling at him, her mouth completely still, yet that voice continued inside his mind.","[He’s the Fifth Young Master, and I’m the Fifth Miss. We’re a pair of fives.","A pair of idiots.]","The system said: [Host, there’s no need to insult yourself so harshly. You’re ranked fifth, but that doesn’t mean you have to call yourself an idiot.]","[Oh, right. There’s one more coincidence I should remind you about.","Among the Marquis of Pingyang’s grandchildren, the two of you both rank fifth.","Among the children born to the same father, the two of you also both rank third. A pair of threes.]","Jiang Yunxi: [A pair of threes, then. At least we aren’t a pair of twos. That would make us double idiots.]","Jiang Yunzheng’s eyes widened. He pointed at Jiang Yunxi sitting on the bed and opened his mouth.","Jiang Yunxi could see his lips moving incessantly, but not a single sound came out.","Unable to hear his own voice, Jiang Yunzheng grew even more frantic as he loudly questioned Jiang Yunxi. He spoke with greater force, but still no sound emerged.","Madam Zheng, who witnessed the scene, knew that her son must have heard his sister’s inner voice just as she had.","The boy was still young and had not experienced much of the world. He was simply too easily startled.","Worried that he might hurt himself, she immediately rose, took her son by the arm, turned his head toward her, and gave him a warning look while shaking her head.","Out loud, she said, “Yunzheng, you’re home. It’s all Mother’s fault. Your sister fell ill, and I completely forgot that today was your day off from the academy. Since your sister was sick, I was worried that informing you would interfere with your studies, so I didn’t send anyone to notify you. Don’t blame me.”","Then Madam Zheng turned to Jiang Yunxi.","“Yunxi, it was Mother’s fault for not sending word to your brother. Don’t blame him.”","“When you first fell ill, your condition was too dangerous. I was so overwhelmed that I forgot to notify him. Later, when you woke up and began to recover, I thought he would be on break in a few days anyway, so I decided to wait until he came home to see you.”","“Next month, your brother will be taking the academy examination to earn his licentiate degree. I was worried that if he learned you were ill, he would be unable to concentrate on his studies, so I deliberately kept it from him.”","Jiang Yunxi still felt somewhat upset.","After all, the original owner had already passed away, and her own brother had not even seen her one last time.","But could she blame Madam Zheng? It did not feel right to do so. Madam Zheng had not known what was happening...","Still, Jiang Yunxi could be certain of one thing: in Madam Zheng’s heart, her son ultimately mattered more than her daughter.","Was she sad? Not really. She was not the original owner, after all.","People ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌‍naturally favored some children over others. It was perfectly normal for parents to show some preference.","Even in her own family, her biological parents always claimed that they treated their two daughters equally, but in reality, they were still somewhat biased toward her elder sister.","Jiang Yunxi was already used to it.","Although she tried to reassure herself, she still felt somewhat unsettled.","Sensing that Jiang Yunxi was feeling a little down, the system had no idea what was bothering her again and could only try to distract her.","【Host, would you like to hear some gossip about your own older brother?】","Jiang Yunzheng: Ah... where did my voice go?"]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: Mom, how about we invite the monks and Taoist priests over","paragraphs":["The moment Jiang Yunxi heard that there was gossip about her own brother, the resentment she felt toward him did not stop her for even a second.","【Eat it. Why not, when it’s free?","This is gossip points.】","After all her hard work over the past few days, she had already finished collecting the gossip about everyone in her courtyard, as well as the maids and old matrons Madam Zheng had brought with her. Yet she still had fewer than two thousand gossip points.","She was still far from the 4,500-point milestone.","There was no more gossip to collect from the people in her courtyard for the time being. She would have to wait until she recovered before expanding her search outward.","Now that her own brother had delivered himself to her door to give her some points, why would she not take advantage of it?","Jiang Yunzheng: Gossip? What kind of gossip?","Who was his little sister talking to?","Was she talking to a ghost?","Jiang Yunzheng’s face went deathly pale. He pointed at Jiang Yunxi and looked toward Madam Zheng, his mouth opening and closing as he spoke frantically.","Yet no sound came out.","When Madam Zheng saw this, she knew it wouldn’t do. If she did not explain things to this foolish son of hers, he might scare himself sick.","Noticing that he was covered in dust, she found an excuse and said, “You child, did you hear that your little sister was ill after you returned and rush over without even changing your clothes?”","“Your sister is sick, and her body is very weak. If you come over covered in dust, what if you make her condition worse?”","“Come outside with Mother at once. I’ll have someone fetch clean clothes from your courtyard. After you change, you can talk to your sister.”","Madam Zheng instructed Suxin, “Suxin, the bird’s-nest porridge I had prepared for Young Miss should be ready by now. Bring it over and have her drink it. Then give her some easily digestible pastries as well.”","“She’s been eating lightly these past two days, so the food hasn’t been very filling.”","Suxin hurriedly replied, “Yes, Madam.”","After giving her instructions, Madam Zheng grabbed Jiang Yunzheng and pulled him outside without giving him a chance to object.","Jiang Yunzheng did not want to leave. He still had no idea what was going on.","However, he was worried that struggling too hard might hurt Madam Zheng, so all he could do was look anxiously at Jiang Yunxi while allowing himself to be dragged away reluctantly.","Even after pulling him into the outer room, Madam Zheng did not stop. She continued dragging him directly toward Jiang Yunxi’s study.","“Mother, Mother, please don’t pull me,” Jiang Yunzheng pleaded, trying to free himself from her grasp.","“My little sister, she...”","“Be quiet.” Madam Zheng turned around and scolded him. “Just come with me obediently.”","The expression on Madam Zheng’s face frightened Jiang Yunzheng, and for a moment, he forgot to argue.","Seeing that her own maids and old matrons, as well as Jiang Yunzheng’s page, Yanqing, seemed intent on following them, Madam Zheng quickly stopped them.","“None of you are to follow us. The young master and I have some private matters to discuss.”","The servants immediately stopped when they heard this.","Once she had pulled her son into the study, Madam Zheng closed the door behind them.","“Mother, my little sister...”","Jiang Yunzheng opened his mouth to say that his little sister had not moved her lips, yet he had heard her speaking. But when the words reached his mouth, he found himself unable to make a sound.","Seeing him struggling to speak, Madam Zheng quickly said, “Stop trying. I can hear it too.”","“Only the two of us can hear it right now. None of the other maids, old matrons, or servants can hear anything.”","“We can hear it, but we can’t say anything aloud. Just like you—the mouth moves, but no sound comes out.”","Jiang Yunzheng asked, “Mother, should we go to a temple or a Daoist monastery and invite a monk or Daoist priest to come examine Little Sister?”","Madam Zheng rolled her eyes at him. “Don’t worry. Your sister isn’t possessed by a ghost. The thing speaking to her isn’t a ghost, and it doesn’t intend to harm her.”","“Luckily, I can hear it... Otherwise, your sister would have been killed.”","Madam Zheng briefly explained everything. Jiang Yunxi had accidentally discovered Nanny Kong and Steward Ma having an affair. Afraid that their secret would be exposed, they had plotted to murder Jiang Yunxi.","She also told him about Jiang Yunshu bribing a maid to harm his sister, as well as the secrets of the other maids in the courtyard.","As for her own matter, she did not mention it.","For one thing, they still did not know who the mastermind was. For another, she was worried that if her son learned about it, he would be unable to focus on his studies.","Jiang Yunzheng’s face was filled with shock. “So everything that the System told Little Sister is true?”","Madam Zheng nodded. “True. It couldn’t be any truer. So from now on, no matter what you hear, don’t be surprised.”","Jiang Yunzheng nodded woodenly. “I understand, Mother. What about Nanny Kong and Steward Ma? How did Father deal with them?”","“They were arrested and handed over to the authorities. Your father took your grandfather’s calling card and went there personally, asking them to deal with the two of them harshly. They probably won’t survive.”","“As for their families, they were hereditary servants of the household, so their property was confiscated and they were sold to a broker.”","At this point, Jiang Yunzheng’s face was filled with lingering fear.","“Thank goodness, thank goodness you could hear it, Mother. Otherwise, Little Sister would have died. And the person who tried to kill her would still be roaming free.”","Madam Zheng was equally relieved. “Exactly.”","“So from now on, no matter what you hear your little sister say, you must believe it.”","Remembering what the System had just said about there being gossip concerning her son, Madam Zheng suddenly grew anxious.","“Oh no. We’ve wasted too much time here. Who knows whether your sister and the System have started digging into your secrets yet?”","“No, I have to hurry back and listen. What if we’re too far away and miss something? That would be terrible.”","Although Jiang Yunzheng had heard Madam Zheng explain so much, he still wanted to personally witness the wonders of the System his sister had mentioned.","“Mother, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌‍I’ll go with you.”","Madam Zheng gave him a look. “You haven’t changed your clothes yet. I only used that as an excuse to drag you outside. If you go back in wearing the same clothes, we’ll give ourselves away.”","“Besides, you’re too bad at keeping your composure. If you let your expressions show when you hear your own gossip, it’ll be a problem.”","Jiang Yunzheng looked down at his clothes. He had been outside all day, and he had taken another tumble just moments ago. They were indeed rather dirty.","He was also worried that he might give himself away.","After thinking for a moment, he said, “Then I won’t enter Little Sister’s bedroom. I’ll sit in the outer room and listen. I could hear everything from the courtyard just now, so I’ll definitely be able to hear it from the outer room.”","That way, he would not have to worry about his expression betraying him and letting his sister discover the truth.","Madam Zheng nodded. “All right. Let’s hurry back.”","Meanwhile, Jiang Yunxi had been served a bowl of bird’s-nest porridge by the maids. After eating a few pastries as well, she was full and satisfied. She then went looking for gossip with the System.","【System, what kind of gossip does my brother have? Hurry up and tell me.】","The System replied: 【Host, congratulations! You’re going to have a sister-in-law very soon!】","Jiang Yunxi put on a look of shock.","【What the hell, System? Are you kidding me?","That little brat just now is only twelve by traditional reckoning—eleven by his actual age. In modern times, he wouldn’t even have graduated from elementary school.","Him? Getting married? Is he even a man?","Does he even have the necessary equipment?】","As Jiang Yunzheng followed Madam Zheng back, he nearly fell flat on his face again.","Fortunately, Madam Zheng reached out and caught him, helping him steady himself.","Madam Zheng looked at him with undisguised disdain. This child really did need more training.","Unlike her, after enduring several days of practice, she was now able to keep her emotions completely hidden no matter what she heard.","“Mother, did you hear what Little Sister just said?”","“She called me a little brat? She’s even younger than I am! What does that make her? A bratty little girl? An even littler brat?”","“What does she mean by asking whether I’m a man or whether I have the necessary equipment?”","“How am I not a man? Of course I have the necessary equipment!”","Jiang Yunzheng’s face turned bright red, all the way down to his neck, and even his voice grew rougher."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: Which genius found a woman for my elementary school brother","paragraphs":["Seeing the resentment on her son’s face, Madam Zheng hurriedly covered his mouth and lowered her voice. “Keep it down. Don’t let your sister hear you!”","Once Jiang Yunzheng nodded to show that he understood, Madam Zheng let go of him.","Jiang Yunzheng lowered his voice a little. “Also, what do ‘modern’ and ‘elementary school’ mean?”","“You’re asking me? How should I know? If you’ve got the nerve, go ask your sister.” Madam Zheng rolled her eyes at him.","“Your sister keeps spouting all sorts of strange words. I reckon that System of hers is the one telling her them.","“You’ll get used to it after a while. Don’t act like Jiang Yunzheng the Sheltered, making such a fuss over everything.”","Jiang Yunzheng the Sheltered: ...Mother, are you sure that’s polite?","Madam Zheng rubbed her forehead helplessly. “Also, haven’t you gotten the main point wrong?”","“Shouldn’t the real question be who is looking for a wife for you? Is it your father, the Heir’s Wife, the Marquis, or the Marchioness?”","Jiang Yunzheng wore an expression that clearly said: You’re asking me? Who am I supposed to ask?","I’m never home, while you spend every day cooped up here. If even you don’t know, why are you asking me, who’s never home?","Seeing that expression on her son’s face, Madam Zheng looked away. “Fine. I knew you were a good-for-nothing.”","Jiang Yunzheng the Good-for-Nothing: ......","[System, have you lost your mind? You want a twelve-year-old child to get married? Aren’t you trying to kill him?","[Doesn’t everyone say that one drop of essence costs ten drops of blood? If you let him get too close to women at such a young age, what if he develops a taste for it? Wouldn’t that ruin him for life?]","[He’ll ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‍end up with kidney failure and a short lifespan, won’t he?!]","Jiang Yunzheng looked horrified as he sought confirmation from Madam Zheng. “Mother, is that really what happens?”","“Otherwise, why do you think I keep warning you not to fool around with the maids?”","“Then why didn’t you tell me that, instead of teaching—”","Seeing the unkind look in his mother’s eyes, Jiang Yunzheng the Coward did not dare continue. In his heart, however, he secretly grumbled:","You teach the people who ought not to be taught, and refuse to teach the people who actually should be taught.","Madam Zheng gritted her teeth. “I didn’t teach your sister that.”","She cast a rather unfriendly look toward the bedroom. It was as though her gaze had pierced through the wall, passed through her daughter, and fixed itself on that creature called the System.","System, what exactly have you been teaching my daughter?","She knows even more about these things than I do, and I’m her mother!","Although... well... that said... System, you’ve taught her very well. Teach her more in the future, so my grandson doesn’t suffer later on.","Madam Zheng began spinning theories.","Her son was brilliant at his studies—the most accomplished scholar among all the Marquis household’s grandsons.","Could it be that the Heir’s Wife’s side...","Although the Heir’s Wife appeared to treat her stepson kindly, she surely wanted the Marquis’s household to pass to her own son in the future.","She certainly would not want a concubine-born son to be too outstanding and overshadow her own son.","But she valued her reputation and could not openly move against her stepson, so she could only find some other way to ruin him.","The Heir’s Wife came from an aristocratic family. She surely knew the dangers of letting a boy consort with women too young. Hadn’t the Eldest Young Master reached sixteen or seventeen without anyone being assigned to his rooms? They had only started selecting a wife for him when he was seventeen or eighteen.","Now that he was nearly twenty, they were finally making arrangements to set a wedding date.","So why were they in such a hurry when it came to her son?","She was his legitimate mother, and his marriage had to pass through her hands.","If she told the Heir that they should arrange a marriage for her son early and have his wife enter the household early, she would appear both virtuous and caring toward her stepson.","The only question was whether the Heir knew about it...","Even if the Heir did not know, the Old Madam ought to know.","But if the Heir’s Wife used the excuse that, “My health is poor, and I don’t know how much longer I have. I want to see my son settled before I go,” then even the Old Madam would find it difficult to object.","[Which brainless genius is trying to find a wife for my bargain-bin older brother at a time like this?]","Jiang Yunzheng thought of Madam Zheng and frowned.","[It couldn’t be my mother, could it?","[I’ve heard that people in ancient times liked to marry and have children very young, all for the sake of carrying on the family line.","[But twelve is still way too young.","[My mother can’t possibly be unaware of the harm that comes from boys... getting involved with women too early, can she?!]","[Very possible.","[After all, people in this era haven’t studied biology.]","Recalling Madam Zheng’s explanation just now, Jiang Yunxi couldn’t help sneering inwardly.","[She didn’t want to disturb his studies, so when I fell ill, she wouldn’t even let anyone tell him. Yet somehow she thought of finding him a wife.","[Getting married won’t distract him from his studies?]","[When you get right down to it, a daughter-in-law is family, while a daughter will eventually marry out. Once she’s married, she’s like water spilled from a daughter’s family pot—an outsider, right?]","[He can’t be distracted for an outsider, but he can be distracted for someone who’ll belong to the family?","[She’s really mastered the art of double standards!]","Jiang Yunzheng shot Madam Zheng a suspicious look.","Madam Zheng hurriedly shook her head. I didn’t. It wasn’t me.","Your sister is slandering me.","[Host, who said anyone was looking for a wife for your brother?]","Jiang Yunxi: [Wasn’t it you?","[Didn’t you just say congratulations because I’d soon be getting a little sister-in-law?]","[Host, listen carefully. I said “little sister-in-law,” not “sister-in-law.”","[Are “little sister-in-law” and “sister-in-law” the same thing?]","Jiang Yunxi was baffled.","Madam Zheng and Jiang Yunzheng were baffled too.","“Mother, do you understand now?” Jiang Yunzheng asked in an extremely soft voice.","Madam Zheng shook her head. “I don’t understand.”","“Then how does Little Sister understand?”","“Why don’t you go ask your little sister?”","[System, stop being so cryptic. Which brilliant genius is trying to get my elementary-school-aged brother a concubine?]","[Or maybe it isn’t a concubine. At his age, it should be called someone to teach him about sex, or perhaps a personal maid or bed warmer.","[Forget the terminology. The important thing is: who’s trying to arrange this?]","[Tell me quickly. I need to send them a banner and a letter of thanks to thank them for ruining people without end!]","[My forty-meter broadsword is already getting restless.","[This is child abuse! You’re trampling the young seedlings of our motherland!]","“Mother, I know what a letter of thanks is, but what’s a banner?” Jiang Yunzheng was a good child. If he didn’t understand something, he asked.","Madam Zheng looked at him. “Stop asking me about every little thing. You attend the academy, don’t you? You’re a proper scholar. Shouldn’t you know more than I do?”","Jiang Yunzheng looked embarrassed. “The teacher never taught us that.”","Madam Zheng had no choice but to explain once more. “Whatever new words you hear from your sister, don’t go asking everyone about them. No one else will know either.","“They all come from that System of hers. Only the System knows what they mean.”","Very good. Madam Zheng had now automatically found a source for all the strange words that came out of her daughter’s mouth.","Jiang Yunzheng beamed. “I understand, Mother. I’ll never ask again.”","Jiang Yunzheng made up his mind. As soon as he returned, he would write down all these unfamiliar words. Then he would wait for an opportunity to coax the answers out of his little sister.","These words were actually quite interesting. If he knew what they meant, he could use them to mess with his classmates... and leave them completely bewildered.","Jiang Yunzheng had no idea that this inadvertent act of his would end up helping his little sister quite a bit."]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: Someone Offers Themselves as a Bedmate","paragraphs":["When Jiang Yunzheng heard that his little sister was planning to carry a knife and go after the person who had tried to find him a concubine, his heart warmed.","“Mother, my sister is so good to me. She’s even willing to go hurt someone with a knife for my sake.”","“Forty meters, though. I don’t know how long one meter is, but forty is certainly no small number. A knife that long would be too heavy for your sister to carry.”","Madam Zheng, who had already spun an entire conspiracy theory in her head, was in no mood to be as relaxed as her son. She merely humored him.","“As long as you know your sister treats you well. You must protect her in the future. You have quite a few sisters, both full and half relations, but you only have one sister who shares both parents with you. You need to know which relationships are closer and which are more distant. Learn to distinguish family from outsiders.”","“Don’t worry, Mother. I’m not stupid.”","Madam Zheng pricked up her ears and listened carefully, afraid she might miss even a single word from her daughter.","She was determined to find out whether this was the Heir’s Wife.","If it was, she would not hesitate to set aside all propriety and bring the matter directly to the heir and the Marchioness. This concerned the lives of her son and grandson. She wanted to see how they would try to shield her.","If her modesty and forbearance had only encouraged them to lay hands on her children, then she would stop yielding from now on.","Her ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‍maternal family was no longer what it had been in the past, and her children were grown. If she continued to endure everything...","【Host, it isn’t that someone is trying to find your brother a concubine. Someone is offering herself to him.】","Madam Zheng, who had been preparing to rise up in righteous fury, immediately deflated like a punctured balloon.","So it wasn’t the Heir’s Wife after all.","She had known the Heir’s Wife couldn’t possibly be that foolish. Even if she used her poor health as an excuse, claiming she was afraid she might not live long enough to see her son marry and have children, all it would take was one question from the heir or the Marchioness for the lie to be exposed.","But soon, the fire in Madam Zheng’s heart began to blaze again.","Someone was offering herself to him? Who?","She glared angrily at her son and lowered her voice. “Have you got a maid in your courtyard who’s becoming too ambitious?”","Jiang Yunzheng looked utterly bewildered. “I have no idea. I’m only home for about three days a month.”","Madam Zheng frowned. “The system hasn’t made a single mistake all these days. It must be one of the maids in your room who’s getting ideas.”","The system continued to reveal the details.","【There’s a maid named Fanghua in your brother’s courtyard. She’s already seventeen or eighteen, old enough to be matched with someone. Her family has started looking for a husband for her, but she refuses to marry one of the household’s servants. She doesn’t want to marry an older steward, either.】","【She envies the concubines in the household. They all dress in fine clothes and jewelry, have people waiting on them, and live much better than ordinary maids.】","Jiang Yunxi’s tone was distinctly unfriendly.","【If she wants to become a concubine, no one is stopping her. Why does she have to ruin my brother’s life? She’s old enough to get married, but my brother is still young! He’s only twelve by nominal age. We don’t even know whether he’s fully developed yet, and she’s already planning to prey on him.】","【Isn’t this an old cow eating tender grass...】","At that point, Jiang Yunxi realized something was wrong. If a seventeen- or eighteen-year-old girl counted as an old cow, then what did that make her, with a soul that was twenty-three years old?","An extremely old cow?","She had just insulted herself along with Fanghua.","【In any case, my brother is still young. This is the time for him to work hard and study. We can’t let her corrupt him.】","【Actually, your brother wasn’t her first choice. She set her sights on your eldest brother first.】","Seeing the blank look on her host’s face, the system realized that Jiang Yunxi still hadn’t grown accustomed to the complicated distinctions between legitimate and secondary family members in this era. Aside from her full brother, she still regarded all her other brothers and sisters as outsiders.","【I mean the son of your legal mother, your father’s eldest legitimate son.】","【Your eldest brother is a highly sought-after match because he’s about to marry. Your legal mother is terrified that he might father a son by a concubine before then, making things awkward for his future bride and her family, so she has been keeping a strict watch over him.】","【The maids in your eldest brother’s courtyard have also formed an alliance. They won’t let maids from the other courtyards get close to him.】","Jiang Yunxi understood.","【The maids in my eldest brother’s courtyard probably want to take advantage of their proximity and get him first. They don’t dare make a move now because they’re afraid our legal mother will punish them. That wouldn’t be worth the risk. They’re probably planning to wait until my future sister-in-law enters the household before making their move and becoming my eldest brother’s concubine.】","【Exactly. She can’t get to your eldest brother, and she looks down on the young masters from the other two branches. That leaves only your second brother and your full brother. Your fourth brother is only six. Even someone as shameless as Fanghua wouldn’t set her sights on a six-year-old.】","【Then why doesn’t she go after my second brother? Why target my brother? My second brother is older, so wouldn’t he be more suitable?】","【Because your third brother is good at studying. He’s the most scholarly of all the young masters in the household. Your second brother is neither accomplished in literature nor skilled in martial arts, and his mother is an unfavored concubine. It’s obvious he won’t have much of a future. Fanghua isn’t stupid.】","Jiang Yunxi gave a derisive laugh.","【So should I thank her for having such discerning eyes and recognizing my third brother’s potential?】","【What about my brother, then? Does he have some special feelings for Fanghua? Did he give her the wrong idea and make her think she had a chance?】","Hearing her daughter’s words, Madam Zheng looked suspiciously at her son.","That was right. It took two to tango. If her son hadn’t given Fanghua some sort of encouragement, she wouldn’t have...","Jiang Yunzheng took two steps back. He shook his head in panic, frantically trying to remember who Fanghua was, what she looked like, and which maid she might be.","Little sister, don’t get me into trouble.","His mother’s eyes looked as though she wanted to eat him alive.","She was so talkative. If she misunderstood the situation, she would lecture him for one or two hours.","【Your brother is still young, and he’s devoted to his studies. He has no interest in such things. Every time he comes home these past few months, Fanghua has hovered around him and flirted shamelessly, but she might as well have been winking at a blind man.】","【Your brother even complained that she was disturbing his revision and told her to stay away.】","With that reminder from the system, Jiang Yunzheng finally understood which Fanghua they had been talking about.","So it was that maid with the deathly pale face, who had apparently rubbed so much scented powder on herself that he sneezed nonstop whenever she came near him.","Jiang Yunxi relaxed. It turned out Fanghua had simply been making advances all by herself. She even found the situation amusing enough to tease her brother.","【Oh, come on. My brother really is hopelessly insensitive. A pretty young lady likes him, and he doesn’t even know how to appreciate it.】","Jiang Yunzheng wore a thoroughly bewildered expression.","Little sister, you didn’t sound like this a moment ago.","It seemed that if he had shown even the slightest interest in Fanghua, she had been ready to go after him with a knife.","How had she managed to change her attitude so quickly?","Madam Zheng, who had previously been glaring furiously at Jiang Yunzheng, was quite satisfied now.","Being hopelessly insensitive was a good thing.","She patted her son on the shoulder. “Well done. Keep it up.”","Jiang Yunzheng beamed with relief.","Excellent. It seemed he had escaped another lecture from his mother.","Jiang Yunxi asked, 【System, how exactly is Fanghua planning to offer herself to my brother?】","【Fanghua’s parents have been pressuring her to go meet potential husbands. She’s found one excuse after another to delay it for several months, but she can’t put it off much longer.】","【Unfortunately, your brother is hopelessly insensitive, so she has decided to change tactics. She’s going to force the issue.】","【Knowing that your brother is coming home today, she plans to drug him tonight and make sure the deed is done.】","【She has already bribed several people in your brother’s courtyard, and she has the aphrodisiac with her.】","【Host, congratulations! After tonight, you’ll have a sister-in-law. If your brother proves capable, he might even give you a nephew or niece in one go. Perhaps more than one.】","【Your mother will soon be enjoying a peaceful life surrounded by grandchildren.】","Jiang Yunxi looked horrified.","A twelve-year-old becoming a father—what kind of utterly deranged situation was this?"]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22: The whole family wiped out, a capitalized tragedy","paragraphs":["When Madam Zheng heard that Fanghua was planning to give her son an aphrodisiac, she was nearly beside herself with rage.","He was still so young. If he took an aphrodisiac, the consequences would be...","Fanghua wasn’t trying to offer herself to him and become his concubine. She was trying to destroy her own son.","[Oh, right, Host. The aphrodisiac Fanghua got was meant for animals.","When she bought it, she didn’t dare let anyone know what it was really for. She only said she needed it to breed pigs. The person who sold it to her prepared a dose meant for an adult boar.","If that dose were used on your brother... Heh heh. You know what that means.]","[What’s more, to be safe, Fanghua bought two doses. She only said she was worried one might not work.]","[If she uses both of them, your brother will be lucky to survive.]","Madam Zheng’s legs went weak, and she collapsed to the floor.","Jiang Yunzheng hadn’t expected the consequences of using that medicine to be so severe either. Although he held himself together better than Madam Zheng and didn’t fall, his entire body was trembling, and cold sweat poured down his face.","Looking at his mother on the floor, he said in a quavering voice, “Mother, I’m scared. I don’t want to die.”","Jiang Yunxi: ...[What the hell... She...]","Jiang Yunxi launched into a nonstop tirade, cursing for more than ten minutes.","Under normal circumstances, Madam Zheng would have wanted to give her daughter a good lesson for using such filthy language. A young lady shouldn’t speak that way.","But at that moment, Madam Zheng only felt that her daughter’s cursing was excellent, wonderful—and far too mild.","After letting out all that anger, Madam Zheng actually felt somewhat calmer, and a little strength returned to her body. She struggled to get up, and Jiang Yunzheng hurried over to help her.","Although he felt it was beneath his dignity, Jiang Yunzheng had been cursing along with his sister in his heart just moments ago. As a result, he wasn’t quite as frightened anymore.","“Zheng’er, don’t be afraid. Now that we know about it, there’s no way we’ll let Fanghua’s scheme succeed.”","Meanwhile, after Jiang Yunxi finished venting, the System continued spilling the secrets it knew.","[Host, if we hadn’t been here, this time you would have—bleeped—died. Not long after your—bleeped—funeral, Fanghua would have made her move against your brother.","Your brother would have died on the spot. Your mother was already in poor health, and after losing both her children one after another, she wouldn’t have been able to bear the shock. She would have—bleeped—too...]","Jiang Yunxi: ...[So the three of them would have been wiped out.]","[That’s not all.","When your maternal grandmother heard the terrible news, she would have—bleeped—not long afterward either.","That was the original fate of this entire family.]","Madam Zheng had just managed to stand with her son’s help, but upon hearing the System’s words, she immediately collapsed again.","This time, Jiang Yunzheng didn’t escape either. He slumped to the ground beside her.","Jiang Yunxi: [This family is just too tragic.]","The System sighed. [Isn’t it?","Although this System doesn’t understand human emotions, even I think it’s tragic.","Utterly tragic!]","[So, Host, you don’t need to feel guilty for—bleep, bleep, bleep, bleep—. If it weren’t for you, this entire family would have been wiped out.","Just accept their kindness without worry. You don’t need to feel sorry for anyone.]","It wasn’t only their family, either. The entire Marquis of Pingyang’s household was destined to be wiped out as well.","But the System couldn’t tell her that. It involved the mission.","Otherwise, why did she think the System had chosen her instead of someone else to transmigrate into this family?","The Main System had said that the Host could be changed, but the time and place could not. The System’s overall mission objectives could not be changed either.","Jiang Yunzheng leaned close to Madam Zheng’s ear. “Mother, we really do have that thing called the System to thank.”","Madam Zheng nodded.","After holding it in for a long while, she finally asked, “Mother, what exactly is that bleeping supposed to mean? Why won’t it just explain itself clearly?”","“Mother doesn’t know either. Sometimes it just starts bleeping. Perhaps it’s talking about things we aren’t meant to know.","“But if it doesn’t want us to know, then so be it. Everyone is entitled to some privacy.”","Jiang Yunxi thought, [Now that we know Fanghua is plotting something sinister and that it would lead to such serious consequences, naturally we can’t let her have her way.","“It’s just a shame that I can’t tell them directly. How would I explain knowing all this while I’ve been bedridden in my room recovering?”]","Jiang Yunzheng looked at Madam Zheng. “So Little Sister doesn’t know that we...”","Madam Zheng shook her head. “She doesn’t know, and we can’t let her find out.","“You experienced it yourself earlier. The moment you try to mention this, you can’t get the words out.”","[Host, how do you plan to save your brother?]","Jiang Yunxi frowned, her face filled with worry. [I can’t tell them outright, so I’ll have to find another way.]","She thought it over. [How about keeping my brother from returning to his own courtyard at night?","“After all, it’s only for two nights.”]","But what excuse could she use?","[That’s it. I’ll make a scene.","“I’ll say that I’m this sick, yet my brother hasn’t even come home to see me. Clearly, he doesn’t regard me as his sister.","“I’ll throw a fit at my brother and my mother in a little while, insisting that my brother keep watch over me. He can sleep in the outer room and serve me tea and water as punishment.”]","[And I won’t let him return to his courtyard during the day either. He’ll stay here and look after me.","“I refuse to believe Fanghua would dare chase him into my courtyard to drug him.”]","The System said, [That could work.","“But will your mother agree?”]","[If she doesn’t, I’ll make an even bigger fuss. I won’t take my medicine, I won’t eat, and I’ll go on a hunger strike.","“If I go as far as threatening to starve myself, surely the two of them won’t still refuse.”]","The System said, [Why don’t you try it later?]","[Once they’ve changed and come back, I’ll tell them.]","Madam Zheng and Jiang Yunzheng exchanged a glance.","“Mother, don’t let Little Sister make a fuss. I’ll sleep in her courtyard tonight and tomorrow night. I won’t return to my own courtyard.","“I won’t go back during the day either. I’m afraid that...”","Although they were siblings, Madam Zheng worried that people would gossip if her son spent the night in his sister’s courtyard. Thus, she said, “Mother will stay with you both.","“We’ll just say that your sister survived this great ordeal, and the three of us want to have a candlelit heart-to-heart talk. We’ll all rest in your sister’s courtyard.”","[So we’re just going to let Fanghua off the hook?","“If you hadn’t interfered, she would have directly or indirectly caused several deaths.”]","Jiang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​‍Yunxi gritted her teeth. [We don’t have an excuse right now, so we’ll let her off temporarily.","“Once I’ve recovered, I’ll go to my brother’s courtyard and find some reason to deal with her.","“Even if I have to frame her.”]","[Not only Fanghua. None of the other maids in my brother’s courtyard can stay either. What if someone else gets similar ideas?","“I need to tell Mother to dismiss them all.","“My brother only stays home three days a month. He doesn’t need so many people serving him.","“We can keep the older female servants, the senior maids, and the male servants.”]","The System reminded her, [Without any maids, who will make your brother’s clothes?]","[Doesn’t the estate have embroiderers? Let them make them.","“Besides, there are still the maids from Mother’s courtyard and mine. The senior maids can sew too.","“In any case, we absolutely cannot leave any hidden dangers behind.”]","Madam Zheng kept nodding as she listened, finding her daughter’s idea quite sensible.","There truly couldn’t be any more maids in her son’s courtyard. Otherwise, there might be another Fanghua.","As for Fanghua, her daughter didn’t need to deal with her or resort to framing her. Hadn’t Fanghua been carrying that medicine on her person? Madam Zheng could take people to search her son’s courtyard shortly. They would find it immediately.","Using that as an excuse to punish her, even Fanghua’s family would have nothing to say.","Then, under the same pretext, she could clear out the maids in her son’s courtyard. No one else would be able to find fault with it.","Madam Zheng quickly whispered her plan to her son.","“Mother, I’ll do as you say. You can handle everything as you see fit.","“I won’t return to my courtyard these next two days.”","[Ding! Host successfully gossiped about her elder brother. Gossip Points +400. Current Gossip Points: 2,100.]","Jiang Yunxi: 【Wow, I just earned 400 points! This gossip was totally worth it.】","Her excitement lasted less than three seconds before Jiang Yunxi sensed that something was off.","【Wait a minute, System. I only got 300 points for digging into my own gossip before, and 200 for digging into my mother’s. How come I got 400 points for digging into my brother’s?","Are you, you lousy system, also practicing son preference and treating people differently?】","Jiang Yunxi was getting angry.","The System: ......【That’s so unfair, Host! I absolutely do not favor men over women.】","【Then how do you explain this?】","The System: 【If I say I don’t know, will you believe me?】","Jiang Yunxi: 【Do you think I will?】","The System’s CPU spun furiously, practically smoking.","【Host, is it possible that the reward is higher because this gossip involves several lives?】","Jiang Yunxi: ......","Well, perhaps. Maybe. Possibly.","Neither the human nor the system realized that, since this was a gossip system, the more people who joined in on the gossip, the greater the reward.","Previously, aside from Jiang Yunxi, only Madam Zheng had been in on the gossip. Now Jiang Yunzheng had joined them as well......","Unfortunately, neither of them knew that."]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: The Marquis's Daughter Also Lacks Money","paragraphs":["Once Madam Zheng and her son, Jiang Yunzheng, returned to Jiang Yunxi’s room, Jiang Yunxi began putting on an act.","“Mother, I know you said earlier that you didn’t tell my brother I was sick because you didn’t want to disturb his studies.","“Although that sounds reasonable, I still feel uncomfortable about it.","“I was this sick, and my brother didn’t even come to see me.","“He needs to be punished.”","Madam Zheng played along. “How does Yunxi want to punish him?”","Jiang Yunzheng said, “I’ll accept any punishment my sister wants to give me.”","Jiang Yunxi: “......”","Something felt wrong. Weren’t they supposed to argue with her?","Sensing ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​‍a trap, Jiang Yunxi cautiously continued, “I want my brother to wait on me for two days, day and night. He’ll bring me tea and water, and if I tell him to go east, he isn’t allowed to go west.”","When neither of them objected, Jiang Yunxi tried raising the stakes.","“He’s not allowed to return to his own courtyard, either. He has to stay here in mine. At night, he can have a temporary bed set up in the outer room and keep watch over me.”","Jiang Yunxi glanced at Madam Zheng, then at Jiang Yunzheng, ready to throw a tantrum and make a scene at any moment.","But what happened next left her utterly dumbfounded.","Only a few seconds after she finished speaking, Madam Zheng nodded.","“Of course. No problem.","“I think your brother should take good care of you for two days as well. Otherwise, wouldn’t that be letting him off too easily?”","Jiang Yunxi’s mouth fell open, and she froze.","Wasn’t this development a little strange? Wasn’t her mother supposed to...","“But to avoid giving people something to gossip about, I’ll accompany your brother.”","Jiang Yunxi: So your son is going to wait on your daughter, and you’re not supposed to feel sorry for him?","Weren’t you supposed to strongly object and say that your daughter was being rebellious and completely out of line?","Jiang Yunzheng said, “Then for the next two days, I’ll be my sister’s male maid and serve her to atone for my sins.”","Jiang Yunxi: You’re not even going to struggle a little? Don’t you feel like this is damaging your manly pride?","Before Jiang Yunxi could react, Madam Zheng made the final decision.","“Then it’s settled.","“Zheng’er, go pour your sister some tea.”","“Yes, Mother,” Jiang Yunzheng replied cheerfully, immediately going to pour the tea.","“You two siblings chat for a while. There are some things I need to handle in my courtyard. I’ll come back once I’m finished.”","Looking utterly bewildered, Jiang Yunxi accepted the tea Jiang Yunzheng brought her and mechanically poured it into her mouth. She treated it like an ox chewing peonies, not tasting a thing.","By the time she came back to her senses, the cup was empty, and Jiang Yunzheng had already taken it from her.","It had really been that easy?","She’d only mentioned it once.","She hadn’t even needed to throw a fit or go on hunger strike?","Wasn’t her mother supposed to worry that having her brother wait on her would interfere with his studies?","[System, don’t you think this mother-and-son pair is a little abnormal?]","With his back to Jiang Yunxi, Jiang Yunzheng rolled his eyes.","You’re the abnormal one. Your whole family is—","Ahem. He couldn’t curse her family. That included him, after all.","Jiang Yunzheng decided he couldn’t let her keep thinking about it, or she might discover the truth. He planned to distract her.","“Little Sister, since we have nothing else to do, why don’t I tell you about what’s been happening at the academy?”","Jiang Yunxi smacked her lips. It wasn’t a bad idea.","But...","[System, this counts as getting some gossip, right? Is there a reward?]","[Host, what are you dreaming about? Only gossip obtained through this system can earn rewards. If you get gossip through other means, go ask those other people for a reward.]","Jiang Yunxi pouted. The system was so stingy.","“Fine. Brother, tell me about what’s happened at the academy.","“Make it something funny.”","Jiang Yunzheng: You sure have a lot of requirements.","Jiang Yunzheng began racking his brains for amusing stories about the academy.","This was genuinely difficult for him.","Jiang Yunzheng was a model student—the sort who rose early and stayed up late, paid no attention to anything beyond his studies, and devoted himself wholeheartedly to reading the sages’ works.","Many people knew that he was related to the headmaster. He was also academically gifted, and the teachers at the academy thought highly of him. They often gave him extra instruction and assigned him additional work.","With such a heavy workload, when would he have had time to listen to gossip?","Still, Jiang Yunxi had no phone or internet and spent every day recovering in her room. Having someone to chat with was better than nothing, even if the person doing the chatting was rather dull.","As she listened to the gossip, Jiang Yunxi communicated with the system in her mind.","[System, how’s my brother’s health? He isn’t in poor condition like Mother and me, is he?]","Jiang Yunzheng suddenly froze in the middle of speaking.","Only when Jiang Yunxi noticed that he had stopped and looked at him strangely did he realize something was wrong. He quickly composed himself and continued.","[Not quite, but compared to people his age in the modern era, he isn’t exactly healthy either.]","[He gets up early and stays up late every day to study. He doesn’t get enough sleep, gets too little exercise, and has an unbalanced diet. He’s in a state of sub-health.","“But that’s a common problem among scholars in this era.]","Jiang Yunxi understood. In other words, she still had to be the sucker who provided him with a Body-Strengthening Pill.","[I have 2,100 points now. That’s enough to exchange for one Body-Strengthening Pill for each of the three of us.","“Should I arrange that now?]","The system replied: [Host, don’t rush. Wait a little longer.","“Have you forgotten that someone is secretly poisoning your mother? At the very least, we need to identify that person first. Your mother’s weak body and the poison in her system are all evidence.","“Once you’ve caught the culprit, you can deal with it then.”]","Jiang Yunzheng’s hand trembled, and he knocked over the teacup beside him.","He opened his mouth to ask what was going on, only to find that he couldn’t speak.","Fine. He understood. He wouldn’t ask.","Jiang Yunxi said, “Brother, why are you acting like a child? How could you be so careless?","“Suxin, clean this up quickly and bring the young master another cup of tea.”","“Brother, I kept you here to take care of me, not to cause me more trouble.”","Jiang Yunzheng wiped away a cold sweat.","It seemed Mother had yet to tell him about quite a few things.","He couldn’t ask his sister about them, so he would ask Mother later and make her explain everything.","[You and your mother can wait a little longer before using yours. Your brother can use his first.","“But it would be best to wait until we’ve earned enough gossip points to exchange for an Antidote to All Poisons and use them together.","“Otherwise, you could just nurse his health back to normal, only for someone to poison him again. That would ruin everything and waste the pill.”]","Jiang Yunzheng: Body-Strengthening Pills, Antidotes to All Poisons... What are those? I’ll have to ask Mother later.","Judging by their names, they sound like good things.","My sister really is wonderful. Whenever she has something good, she thinks of Mother and me. As her brother, I’m not as considerate as she is...","Wait, didn’t I prepare a gift for my sister? Where is it?","That’s right. The moment I returned home, I heard from Nanny that my sister was seriously ill. I was so anxious that I rushed straight to see her and forgot everything else.","I didn’t bring the gift—or even my schoolwork.","The teachers assigned me quite a lot of homework, too.","I don’t dare return to the academy for the next two days, but I can have someone bring over my assignments and the gift.","I’ll have them bring some fresh clothes as well.","With that thought, Jiang Yunzheng stood up and headed outside, calling repeatedly, “Yanqing! Yanqing!”","His page, who had been waiting outside, hurried over. “Young Master, did you call for me?”","“Go back and bring all my schoolwork here. I still need to finish the assignments the teachers gave me.","“And bring the gift I prepared for my sister.","“Also bring some fresh clothes.”","“Yes, Young Master.”","“Hurry back.”","“Understood, Young Master.”","Jiang Yunxi: [My brother even prepared a gift for me. Did he get it ready before coming home?]","The system replied: [Of course.","“Didn’t you hear what he said? He came straight to see you as soon as he returned home. He obviously didn’t prepare it at the last minute.”]","[Looks like he doesn’t have absolutely no feelings for his younger sister after all.]","[I wonder what the gift will be. Could it be silver?]","[Host, all you ever think about is money. You’re practically obsessed with it.]","Jiang Yunxi: [What can I do? I’m broke.","I can’t even afford to give my maid a reward, so I have to make my mother pay.","If I go out in the future and want to buy a snack or two, I won’t have any money for that either.]","[How can I, a noble daughter of the Marquis’s household, be this hard up?]"]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: Is my brother planning to send me silver","paragraphs":["Hearing Jiang Yunxi’s complaint, Jiang Yunzheng thought, “Is my sister really so hard up that she doesn’t even have money to buy snacks?”","“Doesn’t my sister receive a monthly allowance? Where does all her money go?”","Jiang Yunzheng had no idea that his sister received only two taels of silver a month.","How could that compare to him? Since he attended the academy, the household gave him ten taels a month as spending money.","That was merely his pocket money. His academy fees and meals were paid for separately.","Their father and mother also gave him extra spending money every month.","And because he excelled in his studies and brought honor to the household, the Marquis and the Marchioness would occasionally reward him as well.","Jiang Yunzheng was never short of money.","Jiang Yunxi, on the other hand, received only two taels a month. Although she did not have to pay the monthly wages of the servants in her courtyard, she had to pay out of her own pocket whenever she wanted to reward someone.","Her meals were provided by the main kitchen, with the daily allotment already accounted for.","But if she wanted something better, or wished to eat according to her own tastes, she had to spend her own money.","Otherwise, the kitchen servants—who had long since been spoiled by the household—would never take a sickly concubine-born young lady like her seriously.","The original Jiang Yunxi had also taken medicine for years, which had ruined her appetite with all those bitter concoctions. Naturally, she had to change things up and find ways to eat more, and that meant spending even more money.","After all that back and forth, how could her purse not be stretched thin?","And that was only because Madam Zheng occasionally supplemented her allowance.","“But the gift I prepared isn’t money. Who gives someone money as a gift? That would be terribly vulgar.”","If Jiang Yunxi had known what her brother was thinking, she would definitely have said,","“My dear brother, I don’t think money is vulgar! I love money. Just hit me with it—more is better!”","Jiang Yunxi: [System, hurry up and take a look. Is the gift my brother prepared for me money?]","System: [Host, you’d better not reveal the answer ahead of time. Just wait until you receive the gift and see for yourself. If you find out early, there won’t be any anticipation or surprise.]","From the system’s reaction, Jiang Yunxi guessed the truth.","She asked dejectedly, [You won’t tell me because my brother’s gift isn’t money, will you?]","Although phrased as a question, her tone was utterly certain.","The system said nothing, but its silence told her everything.","Jiang Yunxi: “Even if it isn’t money, it was still bought with money.”","At that moment, the system’s train of thought aligned with Jiang Yunzheng’s.","[Host, your brother bought this gift for you by saving up from his living expenses and spending a great deal of money.]","Jiang Yunzheng felt a little embarrassed. He had indeed found ways to save up money, but it was hardly fair to say he had scraped it together bite by bite.","As the young master of a marquis’s household, he wasn’t so hard up that he had to live in such straitened circumstances.","System: [If it was bought with money, isn’t that practically the same as giving you money? He put a great deal of thought into it, so don’t be ungrateful.]","Jiang Yunxi: [When was I ungrateful? I never said I didn’t like it.]","[I’m just desperately short of money. I’m so broke that whenever I think of money, my eyes practically glow gold.]","[You saw me sorting through my little treasury yesterday. Apart from those hairpins and pieces of jewelry, I had only a few dozen copper coins left.]","[And I have to save those to reward the servants.]","[Right now, I’m sick, so the Marchioness has ordered the main kitchen to let me choose whatever I want to eat and charge it to the household accounts.]","[But once I recover, that treatment will be gone. If I want to eat something that suits my taste, I’ll have to pay for it myself. I’m afraid I won’t even be able to afford a decent meal.]","Thinking about it left Jiang Yunxi feeling somewhat dispirited. She no longer felt like listening to Jiang Yunzheng’s rather uninteresting gossip about life at the academy.","She simply lay down, twisting around until her face was turned toward the wall.","“Brother, I’m tired. I want to rest for a while. You don’t need to worry about me. Go find somewhere else to do your lessons.”","Jiang Yunzheng wasn’t angry with his sister. Instead, he looked at her as she lay there sulking, his face filled with concern.","“My sister is really short of money.”","Remembering what life had been like at home before he went to the academy, he immediately understood.","It seemed those servants who fawned on the powerful and trampled on the weak had taken no small amount of money from his sister.","But in this sort of situation, there wasn’t much a secondary son like him could do to change things.","“Looks like I’ll have to tell Mother to give my sister more money each month. I’ll also give her some of my own money in secret every month.”","He remembered that some students at the academy paid others to do their assignments. Back then, he hadn’t been short of money, so he had never taken on such work.","But now that he thought about it, it seemed like a good idea.","He could review his lessons, earn money, and expand his circle of connections—all at once.","As for the person paying him and neglecting his studies, even if he didn’t take the job, that person would simply find someone else.","Thinking of the several times his father had asked whether he had enough money to spend—and how he had always answered that he did—Jiang Yunzheng suddenly wanted to slap himself.","Enough? What a joke.","Any money his father kept in his hands would eventually end up benefiting his elder brother, elder sister, and Madam Wei and her daughter. There was no way it would reach him and his siblings.","Rather than that...","He really had been too foolish before. He should have been like his second brother and thought of every possible way to...","It seemed that from now on, he would have to find more ways to get money from his father.","And so, the matter was happily decided.","If Jiang Fengtang had known what his good eldest son was thinking, he would definitely have said, “What’s so happy about that?”","His son was happy, but he certainly wasn’t.","While Jiang Yunxi was sulking and thinking about where she could get some money, Jiang Yunzheng was pondering how he could get money from their father.","Should he say that it was a classmate’s birthday—and that the classmate was the son of a noble family—and that he wanted to give him an expensive gift to grow closer to him?","Or should he say that he wanted to wish their teacher a happy birthday?","Perhaps he could claim that he had taken a fancy to some valuable inkstone and wanted to buy it.","Before he could decide, Yanqing’s voice came from outside.","“Young Master, I’m back.”","“Young Master, something has happened in our courtyard.”","His voice sounded extremely anxious.","Jiang Yunzheng was startled. Remembering his mother’s instructions, he hurriedly turned to look at his younger sister.","She was still lying with her face toward the wall, her inner voice continuing to complain to the system about how she could get money.","She had even started considering selling off some of her belongings.","She hadn’t noticed anything happening around her at all.","Jiang Yunzheng breathed a sigh of relief. Fortunately, his sister hadn’t noticed.","Worried that Yanqing might accidentally let something slip, Jiang Yunzheng walked toward the outside while calling out loudly,","“I’m coming out.”","“Keep your voice down. Miss is resting. Don’t disturb her.”","Jiang Yunzheng quickly left the bedroom. Yanqing was standing just outside in the outer room.","Even at that distance, Jiang Yunzheng still felt it wasn’t safe enough. He reached out, grabbed Yanqing, and pulled him into his younger sister’s study. Only after closing the door did he ask in a low voice,","“What happened in the courtyard? Speak softly.”","Yanqing looked uneasy.","“For some reason, Madam brought people to our courtyard. She had Fanghua tied up, along with several others.”","Jiang Yunzheng knew perfectly well who those other people were. They had to be the servants his sister’s inner voice had mentioned—those who had been bribed by Fanghua.","Well, this was something.","His sister was a young lady of the Marquis’s household, yet she was worrying over where to get money, while Fanghua had so much money that she could bribe people.","No wonder she had such deep roots as a hereditary servant of the Marquis’s household. With her parents and family all serving in trusted positions at the side of the Marquis’s household, she lived even better than the legitimate young masters and misses of the estate.","Yanqing ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​‍had no idea that her young master had managed to imagine so much in such a short time. She continued in a hushed voice,","“I heard from the nursing matron that something terrible was found on Fanghua. The Marchioness was furious. She had Fanghua bound and gagged, then sent her, along with several others, to the Heir’s Wife’s residence for the Heir’s Wife to deal with.","“The other three maids from our residence were taken away as well. Now everyone here is in a panic, and no one knows what to do.”"]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25: This Is My Brother, My Biological Brother","paragraphs":["When Jiang Yunzheng heard that, he felt reassured. It seemed Mother had indeed found the aphrodisiac, so Fanghua would have no way to deny it.","If Mother had not found the medicine, she would not have sent Fanghua straight to the principal wife.","Fanghua’s entire family served in the household, and her grandmother had even once served Madam Hou. Their roots in the residence ran deep; otherwise, Fanghua would never have managed to get into his courtyard.","Mother really had thought of everything. Once the culprits and evidence were caught together, she could send them to the principal wife and let her deal with them, sparing herself the trouble of offending anyone.","The other three maids had been sent away along with Fanghua. If they wanted to complain, they would only blame Fanghua for dragging them down. They could not fault him or his mother.","Seeing Yanqing looking completely lost, Jiang Yunzheng frowned.","“Why do you look like you’ve seen a ghost? Mother tied up Fanghua and the others, so they must have done something wrong.","“They’re the ones who committed the offense. What are you afraid of? You’re with Young Master at the academy every day. Even if they did something wrong, it has nothing to do with you.”","Yanqing thought about it and realized that Young Master had a point.","He spent every day at the academy with Young Master and had never been close to those people. They had even bullied him in the past, relying on their seniority in the household.","Fanghua most of all. She used to hover around Young Master, snatching his duties away several times and even threatening him.","They all served Young Master, so if they were punished for their misdeeds, wouldn’t that make his own position stand out? From now on, he would be the person closest to Young Master in the courtyard. He wouldn’t have to worry about suddenly losing his job.","The more he thought about it, the more he felt that their misfortune was actually good for him. Yanqing immediately calmed down.","“Young Master is right. I’ll do whatever you say. If you tell me to go east, this humble servant would never dare go west.”","Jiang Yunzheng had no time to bother with his little schemes. He only asked, “Did you bring the gift?”","“I did, Young Master.” As Yanqing spoke, he handed over a wooden box.","Jiang Yunzheng took it and opened the lid. Inside was a white jade plaque engraved with the words “Peace and No Troubles,” attached to a gold chain.","That sort of thing was not easy to find. He had visited several shops before finally locating one, and it had cost him quite a bit.","But when he thought of how short of money his younger sister was—she had even considered pawning her belongings—he worried that all his effort might go to waste if she ended up pawning this too.","His younger sister’s health had always been poor. He had wanted to find her a peace plaque for a long time, hoping it would bring her a lifetime of peace and good fortune.","He remembered that Eldest Sister had one as well.","After thinking for a moment, Jiang Yunzheng asked Yanqing, “How much money do you have left on you?”","Yanqing hurriedly pulled out his purse and checked. “A little over ten taels.”","That money wasn’t his, of course. It belonged to Young Master.","Jiang Yunzheng took out his own purse and counted what was inside: a fifty-tael banknote and a little over ten taels in loose silver.","“Give me ten taels for now. I’ll pay you back later.”","Without a second thought, Yanqing counted out ten taels and handed them over.","Jiang Yunzheng put the fifty-tael banknote and twenty taels of silver into the wooden box.","Seeing this, Yanqing quickly reminded him, “Young Master, are you planning to give all that silver to Miss? You spent all your private savings on the peace plaque, and now you barely have any money left.”","Jiang Yunzheng did not mind in the slightest.","“The two of us still have more than ten taels between us, and there’s some money in my room too. Even if we run out, I can find an excuse to ask Father for more.”","“I have my own plans. Don’t worry about it.”","Jiang Yunzheng was mainly worried that if he did not solve his sister’s money problems, she would pawn the peace plaque.","Pawnshops were all unscrupulous. They would deliberately undervalue everything.","Don’t ask him how he knew.","Jiang Yunzheng turned and left. After taking two steps, he turned back and reminded Yanqing, “Don’t tell anyone about what happened in the courtyard.","“Get things ready in the outer room and grind the ink. After I give the gift to my sister, I’ll come out and do my schoolwork.”","......","Jiang Yunxi stared dumbfoundedly at the fifty-tael banknote and twenty taels in loose silver.","[System, are you even reliable?]","[Didn’t you say the gift my brother was giving me wouldn’t be money? Then what is this?]","[Hahahaha, you useless system! Did you deliberately lie to me just to give me a surprise?]","[Hahahaha, seventy taels of silver! On my monthly allowance of two taels, it would take me almost three years to save this much.]","[Big Brother, you really are my brother.]","[Anyone who says he isn’t my real brother can come argue with me!]","The corners of Jiang Yunzheng’s lips curled upward. It seemed his gift had pleased his sister tremendously.","His last-minute decision to add the silver had clearly been the right one.","But, dear sister, do you really not recognize good jade? That white jade peace plaque alone was worth far more than seventy taels.","Jiang Yunzheng had no idea that the soul inside the body before him had long since been replaced. She was simply a country bumpkin who had never seen anything valuable.","How would she know what kind of jade it was, or whether it was real or fake? The only things she recognized were silver and that gold chain.","Jiang Yunxi was practically delirious with joy. Her eyes sparkled as she stared at the banknote and the silver.","If her brother had not been standing right in front of her, with the other maids in the room, she would have wanted to hug the banknote and silver ingots and kiss them twice.","She even felt like biting the gold chain to test whether it was really gold.","Good people, do you know how thrilling it is for a poor person to suddenly become rich?","[System, you’re such a jerk.]","[I absolutely love this surprise!]","Even the system was rendered speechless by its host. Binding itself to someone who had never seen the world was embarrassing for the system sometimes.","[Host, there are people watching. Whatever you do, don’t bite the gold to test whether it’s real.]","[Also, that jade plaque is worth much more than seventy taels.]","[The person who gave you the gift is still standing right in front of you. At least show some appreciation. Don’t ignore him completely just because you can’t take your eyes off the silver.]","Jiang Yunxi came to her senses.","Oh, right. Her sucker—no, her generous benefactor—was right in front of her. She had to keep him happy and take good care of him. Then, from time to time, she could get him to drop a few more money-making opportunities her way.","Jiang Yunxi had never cared much about those strict rules of propriety between men and women. She was used to pestering her older sister for money and had developed the reflex naturally.","She threw herself forward, wrapped both arms around Jiang Yunzheng’s arm, and began shaking it.","“Big Brother, my dearest brother, you’re too good to me!”","“I love you so much, Big Brother!”","“Your little sister was just worrying about money, and you came right over to send me some!”","Jiang Yunzheng’s face turned bright red.","His sister was far too bold. She had actually said she loved him to death. She must really be desperate for money.","He ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​‍raised his head and stared at the canopy above the bed.","Hmm. The pattern on it was quite nice. Very intricate.","“You’re my real sister. If I’m not good to you, who should I be good to?”","“If you’re ever short of money again, just tell me. Your brother will give you some.”","Looking at Jiang Yunzheng’s flushed, bashful face, Jiang Yunxi felt that she had encountered a divine older brother.","In modern times, boys his age barely had enough pocket money for themselves. They would even scheme to squeeze money out of their younger sisters.","But her brother had given her so much silver in one go, along with a jade plaque and gold chain worth even more.","Brothers like this could come by the dozen, and she wouldn’t complain about having too many.","If Jiang Yunxi had known that Jiang Yunzheng had already decided to earn money by doing his classmates’ homework and fleece their father to support her, she would have been even happier.","“Big Brother, you’re good to me, so I’ll be good to you too. Just wait until I save up a little...” She paused. “I’ll prepare a gift for you as well.”","Jiang Yunzheng knew what she meant and did not press her. He merely said, “Then I’ll be waiting.”","His little sister kept clinging to his arm and acting spoiled. Inside, he was screaming like a marmot the entire time. Jiang Yunzheng had never experienced such enthusiasm before and was completely at a loss, wanting only to escape.","“Little sister, I still have lessons to finish. I won’t keep you company anymore—I’ll go to the outer room and do my homework first.”","Worried that she might keep him from finishing his work and cause him to be punished by their tutor, Jiang Yunxi didn’t insist. She let go of his arm and said, “Then go do your homework, big brother.”","But even after reaching the outer room, Jiang Yunzheng still couldn’t settle down to study.","There was nothing he could do about it. His sister kept counting money in her head and repeatedly asking the system how much the peace token was worth, and how much the gold chain was worth.","And once she learned the prices, she let out another round of excited screams.","Jiang Yunzheng decided that if he ever wanted to make his sister happy in the future, he wouldn’t bother giving her anything else. He would just give her banknotes or gold. Those were much more practical.","After all, his sister clearly didn’t know how to appreciate fine things.","【From now on, my big brother is my favorite brother in the whole world.","As for my father—who’s that? I don’t know him.","He didn’t even come to see me when I was sick, leaving me to worry about money every day. A father like that? I don’t need him anymore!】","【They say an elder brother is like a father. From now on, my big brother is my father.】"]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26: Defiant Daughter (Part One)","paragraphs":["When his little sister said that she did not know their father and that he would be her father from then on, Jiang Yunzheng’s hand trembled as he was doing his schoolwork. A large blot of ink immediately appeared across the page he had nearly finished.","Looking at the conspicuous stain, Jiang Yunzheng felt like crying.","The teacher for this subject was notoriously fussy and placed great importance on neatness. There was no way this would pass inspection.","He picked up the page, crumpled it into a ball, and tossed it aside.","“Forget it. I’ll rewrite it.”","He glanced toward the door leading to the inner room.","“Maybe I should work somewhere else?”","Looking at the several discarded drafts beside him, he thought, “If Little Sister keeps wreaking havoc like this, when am I ever going to finish?”","But his little sister’s inner thoughts were quite interesting. He might hear some new and amusing revelation at any moment, and Jiang Yunzheng was somewhat reluctant to leave.","His eyes suddenly hardened.","“It’s not Little Sister’s fault.","Just as Mother said, I’m simply too inexperienced and haven’t been through enough hardships.”","“If ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‍I can’t even withstand this little disturbance, how will I ever take the imperial examinations in the future?","When the time comes, there might be people cooking, sleeping, snoring, or even throwing fits right beside me while I’m answering the questions.”","“I have to start training myself from now on.”","Yes, that was it.","Having successfully convinced himself not to change locations, Jiang Yunzheng once again began writing furiously.","······","The commotion Madam Zheng had caused in her son’s courtyard was so great that someone had reported it to the Heir long ago.","There were rules in the marquis’s residence: once the boys of the household began their studies, they would move out of the rear courtyard and into the front courtyard, closer to their father’s residence so that he could keep an eye on them.","By the time the Heir hurried over, however, Madam Zheng had already tied up the servant and taken her to the Heir’s Wife’s courtyard. He followed after them.","Upon learning that a maid in his son’s courtyard had nearly killed him by secretly giving him an aphrodisiac intended for animals, Jiang Fengtang was furious. If he had not been restrained, he would have kicked the maid to death himself.","He issued the Heir’s Wife an ultimatum: no matter who came to plead for mercy, the maid was to be punished severely.","If the investigation proved that the maid’s family had helped her obtain the drug, they would receive the same punishment.","As for Madam Zheng’s request that no maids be assigned to her son’s courtyard in the future, and that only male servants, matrons, and older serving women be allowed to attend him, Jiang Fengtang agreed to that as well.","Seeing that the Heir had made his position clear, Madam Zheng took her leave.","When Jiang Fengtang learned that his son was in his daughter’s courtyard, he remembered that he had been extremely busy with official duties and social engagements these past few days. He had returned home late every night and had not found the time to visit his sick younger daughter.","He had not seen his son in quite some time either. Since he was already going to comfort his daughter, he might as well see his son too. Thus, he came over with Madam Zheng.","The entire way there, Madam Zheng was anxious. She silently prayed that the Heir absolutely must not hear his daughter’s inner voice.","There was no helping it. His daughter’s thoughts were sometimes far too rebellious and scandalous.","As her biological mother, she could tolerate them, but the Heir—","Bah, no. She had been influenced by her daughter too.","Although the Heir was also the girl’s biological father, he had several other children. Because his daughter had always been frail, she had not spent much time with him. Compared with his legitimate daughter and the daughter born to his beloved concubine, she was the least favored of his three daughters.","If the Heir heard those rebellious and scandalous thoughts of hers, then surely—","Madam Zheng had once tried to politely decline his proposal, but the Heir’s paternal instincts had suddenly awakened, and he had insisted on coming to see the girl. What else could Madam Zheng do?","She could only pray fervently that he would not hear his daughter’s inner voice—or that the girl would be asleep.","Yet people always say that whatever you fear most is what happens. The moment the two of them entered the girl’s courtyard and walked a little farther inside, Madam Zheng heard her daughter’s inner voice.","[From now on, my brother is the person I love most in the world.","As for my father, who’s that? I don’t know him.]","[He didn’t even come to see me when I was sick, leaving me to worry about money every day. A father like that? I don’t need him anymore!]","[They say an elder brother is like a father. From now on, my brother is my father.]","Madam Zheng’s face twitched violently.","This child—was she trying to scare her mother to death?","She had started with something explosive right out of the gate.","Madam Zheng hurriedly looked at Jiang Fengtang, hoping desperately that he had not heard.","However...","Jiang Fengtang was looking around with a strange expression on his face.","Madam Zheng’s heart lurched. Surely the Heir had heard it?","“My lord, what are you looking for?” Madam Zheng asked, clutching her handkerchief tightly, her voice tinged with anxiety.","Jiang Fengtang said, “Did you hear something?”","Madam Zheng pretended not to understand.","“No. No one said anything just now.”","Jiang Fengtang frowned.","“How could no one have? I clearly heard someone say that her brother was the person she loved most and that she didn’t know her father.”","Madam Zheng’s heart gave another jolt.","All right, it was confirmed. The Heir could hear their daughter’s inner voice too.","But why could no one else hear it? Why only the three of them?","Could it be related to their blood ties?","But this was not the time to dwell on that. She had to cover things up quickly.","If the Heir found out that his daughter had said she did not know her father—in other words, that she did not know him—then he would...","“My lord, perhaps you’ve been too busy with official matters and are overly tired. You may be experiencing auditory hallucinations. There was clearly no one speaking just now.”","Madam Zheng turned toward the servants following them and sought their assistance.","“Did any of you hear someone speaking?”","“Replying to Madam, no.”","“No, Madam.”","······","One servant after another said that they had heard nothing.","Even the Heir’s personal attendant said he had not heard anything.","This made Jiang Fengtang begin to doubt whether he had truly imagined it.","“Perhaps I really did hear wrong,” he said, somewhat uncertainly.","Madam Zheng nodded firmly.","“You must have heard wrong.”","Inwardly, she cried out again and again:","Son, please don’t say anything else! Your father—the one you don’t recognize—is here!","Jiang Yunzheng, who had been doing his schoolwork, saw his parents enter together and hurriedly rose to greet them.","“Father, Mother.”","Although he knew from Madam Zheng that his brother was fine, Jiang Fengtang still could not help asking when he saw him,","“Yunzheng, are you all right?”","Jiang Yunzheng knew what his father was really asking about. However, he and his mother had already discussed it beforehand, and he was supposed to pretend that he knew nothing.","“Father, I’ve been doing well at the academy. The teacher and my classmates have all treated me very well. You needn’t worry.”","Jiang Fengtang turned to Madam Zheng. When he saw her give a slight shake of her head, he understood that she had not told their son anything.","“Oh. As long as you’re doing well.”","Seeing the several crumpled sheets of paper on the table, Jiang Fengtang raised his brows and could not help asking,","“Was today’s assignment especially difficult? You’ve wasted so many sheets.”","Jiang Yunzheng: “...”","How was he supposed to answer? Could he tell his father that the assignment was not difficult at all, and that he had only ruined it because Little Sister’s inner voice had startled him?","He did not need to answer, however. Jiang Fengtang picked up the assignment he had just written and read it, his brows drawing together slightly.","After setting it down, he picked up one of the discarded paper balls and unfolded it.","“Yunzheng, when you’re doing your schoolwork, you should...”","A voice sounded at precisely that moment.","[Why is there an adult man’s voice outside? It sounds as though he’s being called Father by my brother. Could that be my deadbeat father?]","[Wow, people really can’t stand being talked about. I was just mentioning him, and here he is.]","[I was unconscious for several days, and I’ve already been awake for several more. He never came to see me, but now he suddenly shows up. Could he have followed my brother here?]","[Hmph. So sons are precious treasures, while daughters are just weeds.]","[You don’t care about me, and I don’t care about you either.]","From now on, my brother is my father. Having my brother as my dad is all I need.】","Madam Zheng and Jiang Yunzheng’s faces instantly turned deathly pale.","Daughter/little sister, even if that’s only your inner thoughts, couldn’t you show a little restraint?!","Jiang Fengtang’s eyes widened in fury. So he hadn’t been hearing things earlier—someone really had spoken.","And the person speaking was his youngest daughter, who normally barely said a word whenever she saw him.","Jiang Yunxi.","“You unfilial daughter!” Jiang Fengtang roared."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27: Defiant Daughter (Part Two)","paragraphs":["After roaring “You unfilial daughter!” Jiang Fengtang strode into the inner room, intending to teach his disrespectful youngest daughter a lesson.","Madam Zheng and Jiang Yunzheng inwardly cried out that something was wrong and hurried after him.","If the Heir—if their father—was going to hit their younger sister, they had to stop him. They absolutely couldn’t let him...","Jiang Yunxi was leaning against the headboard, idly playing with the jade token and gold chain her older brother had given her, her eyes fixed on the doorway.","After hearing the furious shout of “You unfilial daughter!” an imposing, middle-aged handsome man with blazing eyes stormed inside.","The maids in the room hurriedly bowed.","“Your Grace.”","Jiang Fengtang was about forty years old. He wore a purple brocade robe and had a neatly trimmed beard. Tall and broad-shouldered, he was a dignified, handsome middle-aged man.","Looking at the rather striking man before her and hearing the maids’ form of address, Jiang Yunxi’s eyes lit up.","【So this is my father!】","【He’s actually pretty handsome. He can just barely be considered a match for my mother.】","The system said, 【Host, have you got your priorities backward? He just called you an “unfilial daughter”!】","Jiang Yunxi replied, 【Why would he curse me for no reason?","I’ve spent the past two days doing nothing but recuperating. I haven’t gone anywhere or done anything. He has no reason to curse me.","He has more than one daughter, you know. He must be cursing one of the other two, not me.】","The system said, 【He ran all the way to your courtyard and shouted “unfilial daughter.” If he wasn’t cursing you, who else could he be cursing?","It’s not as though he’s sick in the head and came to your courtyard just to curse one of his other daughters.】","Jiang Fengtang stared at his youngest daughter, who was sitting there with a bright smile, her lips unmoving, while he heard the voice in his ears. He felt as if the entire world had turned surreal.","His youngest daughter clearly hadn’t said a word. Then what was the voice he was hearing?","And whose voice was it?","Jiang Yunxi frowned. 【System, now that you mention it, that “unfilial daughter” really does seem to have been directed at me?","But what right does he have to curse me?】","【I was poisoned by the old nanny serving his mother. I barely survived that, and then she came back and tried to poison me with rat poison.","Luckily, my mother saved me.","And ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‍what did he do? Something this serious happened, yet he neither asked about it nor came to see me. He acted as though I didn’t exist.","I haven’t even called him an “unfilial father.” What right does he have to call me an “unfilial daughter”?】","Jiang Fengtang once again confirmed that his youngest daughter truly hadn’t spoken aloud. Yet the voice he heard really was hers.","He opened his mouth, wanting to explain why he had called her an unfilial daughter, but found that he couldn’t make a sound.","Looking at her father angrily pointing at himself, his mouth moving nonstop without a sound coming out, Jiang Yunxi decided that he was probably cursing her—and cursing her viciously at that.","Jiang Yunxi was not the original owner. She was no pushover.","What kind of biological father came to visit his daughter, who had only just survived a serious illness, and instead of offering comfort, immediately started cursing her?","If he wanted her to put on a show of fatherly love and filial affection, he could dream on.","She didn’t even bother calling for anyone. Holding up the jade token and gold chain in her hands, she smiled at Madam Zheng.","“Mother, look.","These are gifts my brother gave me.”","“And this.” She rummaged through the wooden box beside her. “My brother even gave me seventy taels of silver.”","“Mother, my brother really is my own brother. He treats me with all his heart.”","“You have no idea—I’ve been worrying about money every day. I only had a few dozen copper coins left.","I need money to reward the servants and to order dishes from the kitchen. How could a few dozen copper coins possibly be enough?","I originally thought that once I recovered, with no special treatment, I would have to eat coarse grain every day.","I never expected my brother to give me so much.”","“Seventy whole taels of silver. That’s nearly three years of my monthly allowance.","I won’t have to worry about money anymore.”","“Mother, my brother even said that if I ever run short, I should just ask him. He’ll give me money.”","“Mother, with a brother this wonderful, why didn’t you give me more brothers?","Having a brother is the best.”","【Unlike a certain father, who has never given me a single bit of silver all these years beyond the monthly allowance from the estate.","He grew up in the Marquis’s residence too. There’s no way he doesn’t know that the servants here fawn over the powerful and trample on the weak.","I’m only a concubine-born daughter, and a sickly one at that—an unloved girl who could die at any moment.","Who in this residence would respect me?】","【All these years, if my mother hadn’t looked after me, occasionally supplementing my allowance, and if the maids in my courtyard hadn’t secretly sold their needlework to exchange for money, I would probably have starved to death long ago.","A young lady of a dignified marquis’s household had to rely on her maids selling needlework to support her—and nearly starved to death.","If word of this got out, I wonder whose shame it would be.】","Jiang Fengtang had originally arrived in a fury, determined to teach his unfilial daughter a lesson. But after hearing these thoughts, he felt as though his heart had been struck repeatedly by a heavy hammer. The pain pierced straight through him.","He thought back over the years and realized that he truly had never given his youngest daughter any money.","His sons and his other two daughters, however, often received gifts and silver from him.","In the past, whenever his youngest daughter saw him, she barely spoke and acted timid and withdrawn. She had never seemed close to him.","So that was why...","So his youngest daughter had endured so much hardship, and there was a reason she wasn’t close to him.","Madam Zheng and Jiang Yunzheng nearly burst into tears as well.","In places they had never known about, their daughter and younger sister had actually suffered so many grievances.","Thinking back to the things she had seen while sorting through the original owner’s memories over the past two days, Jiang Yunxi felt that the resentment in her heart was enough to nourish several Evil Sword Immortals.","【I nearly died this time. After finally waiting for him, I thought he had come to visit me.","Who would’ve thought... Forget coming empty-handed—he cursed me the moment he arrived.","What on earth have I done to deserve being cursed like that?","From the moment he entered until he started cursing, I don’t think I said a single word.】","Jiang Fengtang, you may not have said a single word aloud, but your inner thoughts had certainly said plenty.","【Maybe he thinks I shouldn’t have survived at all. That I’m just wasting his family’s money by staying alive.","After all, I’m always taking medicine and need to be supported, with maids and old nurses attending to me. All of that costs money.】","Jiang Fengtang’s eyes widened. He wanted to speak up and deny it, but he couldn’t make a sound. He could only shake his head desperately.","I didn’t! I didn’t want you to die!","How could I possibly want my own daughter dead?","Jiang Yunxi thought, 【But he never considers why I’m so frail in the first place. It’s all because of the harm caused by Madam Wei, whom he dotes on and protects.】","Jiang Yunxi ground her teeth in fury. 【He’s completely blind. He refuses to cherish my mother and instead favors that vicious mother and daughter, Madam Wei and Jiang Yunshu.】","【Jiang Yunshu bribed the maids in my courtyard to make me sick from time to time, hoping to send me to an early grave.","And when my mother was pregnant and giving birth, Madam Wei repeatedly bribed midwives to harm her. My mother suffered difficult labor twice, and when she gave birth to me, she nearly died along with me.","Madam Wei even caused her to miscarry once.】","【If that child had been born, I might have had two more brothers who would have treated me with all their hearts.】","【Madam Wei is still having people poison my mother from time to time.】","【The three of us haven’t been killed by that vicious mother and daughter only because we’ve had extraordinary luck—and because the ancestors of the Zheng family have been protecting us.】","Madam Zheng’s face went deathly pale.","“My daughter, that matter concerning Madam Wei still has no evidence. Don’t go ranting about it in your head.","And saying in front of your father that the ancestors of the Zheng family protected the three of us—isn’t that just stabbing him in the heart?”","Jiang Yunzheng murmured, “So... so Mother and my sister have suffered this much.","Jiang Yunshu had people harm my sister, and Madam Wei has been harming Mother all these years.","I... I didn’t know any of it.”","“I have truly failed as a son and as an older brother.”"]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28: Disobedient Girl (Part Three)","paragraphs":["System: “Host, your older brother was poisoned too.","But your mother kept a close eye on him, so the attempt failed. Later, after he moved to the front courtyard, his wet nurse knew a little about medicine and had some skill, which helped him escape the danger.”","“As for this wet nurse, your mother asked the Zheng family to find her. The Zheng family had once shown her family kindness, and she had devoted herself to repaying them. That was why she wanted to protect your brother.”","Jiang Yunzheng thought, So I’m a pitiful little thing too, just like my mother and sister.","Jiang Yunxi asked, “Do you know who poisoned my brother?”","System: “No.","“You know I’m only a beginner system. I can only see what has happened to this person; I can’t investigate beyond that.","“Once I level up...”","“Don’t worry, don’t worry. I’ll remember that you need to level up.","“Once I... You know what I mean.”","The system secretly rejoiced.","“System, do you think I can exchange my father for someone else?","“This father of mine is truly impossible to keep. Just thinking about him makes my liver ache. How did I end up being born as his daughter? I’m so unlucky.","“I only want to change my father, not my mother or my brother.”","System: “Host, I’m afraid that isn’t possible.”","Jiang Yunxi knew it was impossible, but she had still clung to that last sliver of hope.","When that hope was shattered, she instantly felt as if all her strength had been drained away. She was utterly resigned to her fate.","Without even looking at Madam Zheng and Jiang Yunzheng, who for some reason were standing with their backs to her, or at Jiang Fengtang, who was staring at her with wide eyes and shaking his head desperately, she said, “I’m tired. I want to rest now. Make yourselves comfortable.”","With that, she lay down on her own and turned to face the wall, choosing to see nothing and hear nothing.","“You... I...” Jiang Fengtang opened his mouth, wanting to speak and explain himself, but he had no idea where to begin.","Madam Zheng’s face was already streaked with tears. Somehow, she found the strength to grab Jiang Fengtang by one arm and drag him outside.","“My lord, Yunxi is tired. Let’s not disturb her.”","Jiang Yunzheng no longer cared whether he was being disrespectful or disobedient. He grabbed his father’s other arm and dragged him out as well.","The family of three went straight to Jiang Yunxi’s study and had the servants stand guard at a distance, forbidding anyone from approaching.","The servants in the courtyard could only hear voices coming from the study. Every now and then, there would be a raised argument, the sound of crying, or something being smashed. They were so frightened that they hardly dared to breathe.","After about half an hour, the room finally fell silent.","“So all of this was told to Yunxi by that system, and it’s all true?” Jiang Fengtang asked again to confirm.","Madam Zheng nodded. “Judging from what happened with Nanny Kong, that maid, Fanghua in Yunzheng’s courtyard, and the other maids in the residence, it’s all true.”","“As for Madam Wei trying to harm me, the system said it would know the truth after Yunxi met Madam Wei in person.”","Madam Zheng concealed the fact that her daughter even suspected the Heir’s Wife.","Naturally, she also left out that she herself had suspected the Heir’s Wife many times.","“Are you certain that only the three of us can hear it?” Jiang Fengtang pressed.","Madam Zheng shook her head. “Yunxi has been recovering from her illness. These past few days, aside from the maids and nurses in her courtyard, she has only seen the three of us.","“So there’s no way to be certain...”","“I feel that it has something to do with blood relations.”","Madam Zheng voiced her guess.","Jiang Fengtang nodded. He had come to the same conclusion.","“My lord, please don’t blame Yunxi. She’s simply been too wronged.”","Madam Zheng wiped away her tears. “I never imagined Yunxi had been living in such hardship. If only I had known... If only I had given her more money.”","Jiang Fengtang’s eyes were red. “This isn’t your fault. You only receive so much each month. How much money could you possibly have?”","Madam Zheng thought to herself, I do have money. You just don’t know about it.","After her maternal family’s property was returned to them, her mother had come to visit her and secretly stuffed a considerable sum of money into her hands.","She ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​‌‍had kept it hidden, intending to save it for her son’s marriage and her daughter’s dowry. She had never mentioned it to anyone.","Every month, she had supplemented her son’s expenses and helped her daughter as well, but she had never imagined that what she gave her daughter still wouldn’t be enough.","Of course. Aside from her mother, her daughter had received no financial support from her father, grandfather, or grandmother. It was only natural that she would be short of money.","And the servants in the residence were...","“It’s all my fault,” Jiang Fengtang said. “I was the legitimate eldest son from birth, and everyone in the household respected and fawned over me. If you hadn’t told me just now, I would never have known how poorly an unfavored concubine-born child could be treated...","“No matter how you look at it, it’s all my fault.”","“It’s no wonder Yunxi isn’t close to you and resents you,” Madam Zheng hurriedly explained. “My lord, she was only speaking out of anger. Deep down, she still hopes to have a father who will dote on her.","“If she didn’t, she wouldn’t have said she wanted to change fathers. That only proves she still wants a father’s affection.","“My lord, please don’t blame her. She’s still only a child.”","“Father, please don’t blame my sister,” Jiang Yunzheng added, defending his sister as well.","Jiang Fengtang raised a hand to stop them. “Enough. You don’t need to say anything more. I understand. I don’t blame her.","“Even if someone must be blamed, it should be me.”","Jiang Fengtang looked at Jiang Yunzheng. “You bought your sister a jade token and gave her seventy taels. Are you out of money?”","“You must be. Otherwise, you wouldn’t have given her only seventy taels.”","Jiang Yunzheng rubbed his head. “I am out of money.”","Jiang Fengtang reached out and patted him. “You’re a good older brother. No wonder Yunxi even wants to call you her brother-father.”","“Father, I...”","“All right, enough. I’ll have someone bring you five hundred taels in banknotes later. Keep it for yourself. Don’t give it all to your sister again.”","He glanced toward his daughter’s bedroom, as if he could see her through the layers of walls.","“Your sister is my daughter. Supporting her is my responsibility, not yours.","“Later, I’ll personally give her the money that belongs to her and repay everything she has been deprived of over the years.”","As he spoke, a cold glint flashed through Jiang Fengtang’s eyes.","“It’s time to clean up the servants in this household as well. In just a few days, we’ve already had so many servants attempt to murder their master or betray their master.","“Yunxi has been bullied by those snobbish servants for all these years.”","“And Jiang Yunshu needs to be taught a lesson too.”","Jiang Fengtang looked at Madam Zheng. “Give me that maid and the evidence later. I’ll go and speak with Yunshu.","“As for Madam Wei attempting to harm you, we have no evidence for now. We’ll do as Yunxi suggested. Once she meets Madam Wei, we’ll see what the system says.”","Madam Zheng did not dare oppose Jiang Fengtang at a time like this. She was afraid that angering him might remind him of her daughter’s disrespectful thoughts toward him.","“Yunzheng, you can sleep here tonight if you want.","“I’ll go deal with these matters first and come back later. Tonight, I’ll dine with the two of you.”","Watching her father leave with his entourage, Jiang Yunzheng frowned.","“Mother, do you think Father truly doesn’t blame Little Sister?”","His sister was far too bold. She had actually grumbled about Father like that in her heart.","If he were their father, he would have been furious.","“He probably doesn’t blame her, does he? Didn’t your father say so himself?”","“But what if he was only deceiving us?”","Madam Zheng frowned. “How about you help your sister coax your father?”","“What good would my coaxing do? If anyone should coax him, it should be Sister.”","“Your sister resents him so deeply. Would she be willing to coax him?” Madam Zheng felt that the chances were slim.","Then she remembered the thoughts she had heard from her daughter earlier and recalled her daughter’s fondness for money. Perhaps having Yunxi coax her father was not entirely impossible after all.","“Mother, perhaps I have a way to persuade Sister.”","Madam Zheng’s eyes lit up. “Then go and persuade her quickly.","“Your father will be coming to dinner soon. If your sister is still resentful and refuses to acknowledge him, we’ll be in trouble.”","“Don’t worry, Mother. Leave it to me.”","With the grim resolve of a warrior prepared to cut off his own hand—win or die trying—Jiang Yunzheng turned and headed straight for Jiang Yunxi’s inner chamber."]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29: Struck It Rich (Part One)","paragraphs":["“You remember, little sister?” Jiang Yunzheng asked again.","Jiang Yunxi looked utterly resigned. “I remember, I remember. Brother, can you stop already?”","That boy had been droning on beside her for nearly an hour. She could recite his entire speech by now.","It was all about how, as long as they pleased their father, they would have everything they wanted.","Their father had several storehouses filled with all kinds of treasures. If the two siblings didn’t find a way to coax some of those things out of him, they would surely end up benefiting their other brothers and sisters instead.","They were neither the eldest nor legitimate, and they weren’t their father’s favorites, either—in short, they had none of the advantages.","If they waited for their father to remember them and let a little something slip through his fingers, they would be waiting until the year of the monkey.","They might as well please their father and make him happy enough to give them something.","Jiang Yunxi naturally understood the reasoning. Hadn’t she just made a few pointed, sour remarks about that cheap father of hers, subtly reminding him that his daughter had run out of money?","As far as Jiang Yunxi was concerned, the original owner had been rather foolish. She had been so short of money, yet she hadn’t even known to go to her father and complain about being poor.","A few soft words were enough to coax things out of him. Only an idiot would refuse to do that.","Back when she was in school, she had coaxed her teachers and classmates. After graduating and entering the workforce, she had become a social creature and had to coax her boss as well.","Money was hard to earn, and life was hard. That was an eternal truth.","Nothing came easily.","What Jiang Yunxi didn’t know was that the original owner had heard every one of the things she had cursed her father for in her heart.","Otherwise, Jiang Yunzheng wouldn’t have earnestly tried to persuade her to say a few nice things and placate their father later.","“Father will be coming over for a meal soon. Remember to flatter him a little more.”","Jiang Yunxi frowned. He was coming so soon? Couldn’t he at least give her some time to adjust?","She had only just cursed him in her heart.","[What does he want now? Wasn’t he just here?","Every time he comes, he calls me a ‘wayward daughter.’ What if he scolds me again later?]","Jiang Yunzheng said, “Judging from the things you’ve been muttering in your heart, Father wouldn’t exactly be wrong to call you a wayward daughter.”","“Little sister, didn’t you just promise that you’d let me explain it again?”","Jiang Yunxi’s scalp prickled. “No need, Brother. You don’t have to say it again. I remember everything.","“Don’t worry. I’ll flatter him later. I guarantee I’ll praise him so much he won’t know which way is north.”","“Go do your schoolwork. Otherwise, you’ll have to write by lamplight tonight.”","Jiang Yunzheng wanted to sigh. So many things had happened today, and he had barely done any of his schoolwork.","If he didn’t hurry, he didn’t know whether he would be able to finish it tomorrow.","After leaving his mother’s courtyard, Jiang Fengtang had originally intended to go straight to Jiang Yunxi’s courtyard.","But after walking for a while, he remembered something and returned to the front courtyard.","It was already evening when Madam Zheng finally welcomed Jiang Fengtang.","Madam Zheng had arranged for someone to keep watch outside. As soon as they saw the Heir approaching, they hurried in to report it.","The moment Jiang Fengtang entered the courtyard, Jiang Yunzheng pulled Jiang Yunxi out to wait in the outer room.","When Jiang Fengtang approached, Jiang Yunzheng quickly bowed. “Father.”","Seeing that his sister was still standing there, Jiang Yunzheng tugged on her sleeve.","Jiang Yunxi had no choice but to bow and greet him as well. “Father.”","“Why has Yunxi gotten up? Is she well enough to be out of bed?”","Madam Zheng hurriedly smiled and explained, “Her fever has gone down. She still has a little inflammation in her lungs, but she can recover slowly with proper care.","“As long as she only walks around indoors and doesn’t go outside into the wind, it won’t cause any problems.","“The children haven’t dined with you in quite some time, and Yunxi has been hoping you would spend more time with her.”","Jiang Fengtang didn’t know whether his daughter truly wanted him to accompany her more often, but since she hadn’t contradicted Madam Zheng—and her inner voice had stopped grumbling about him—he took it as the truth.","Feeling pleased, he wanted to play the part of a loving father.","He glanced at the wide-open door. “With the door open, won’t Yunxi catch a chill? We should eat in the inner room instead.”","“But if we eat in the inner room, the whole place will smell of food. Later...”","“That’s no problem. We can open the windows afterward to air it out.","“We can’t let Yunxi catch a draft.”","While the maids prepared the meal, the family of four moved into the inner room.","Jiang Fengtang first took several banknotes from his sleeve and handed them to Jiang Yunzheng. “Zheng’er, take these five hundred taels for now.","“You spent all your money buying gifts for your sister, and after giving them to her, you had none left for yourself.","“You’re studying at the academy and only return once every ten days. You can’t be short of money. When you’ve used it all, come tell Father, and I’ll give you more.”","Jiang Yunxi: [Damn, my brother gave all his money to me and made himself penniless.","“My goodness, what an absolutely perfect older brother.”]","[Other people’s brothers would rather let their sisters suffer than suffer themselves.","My brother would rather suffer himself than let his sister suffer.]","[My brother is the best brother in the whole world. I won’t tolerate anyone disagreeing.]","Jiang Yunzheng’s face flushed slightly.","Little sister, I’m not as miserable as you think. I still have some money.","I only told Father that so I could get money out of him...","But with his father right there, he couldn’t explain himself. He could only accept the banknotes. “Thank you, Father.”","Jiang Yunxi stared at the banknotes, her eyes practically shining.","[Five hundred taels! So many banknotes! I’ve never seen this many banknotes in my entire life.]","And that was completely true. She had seen tens of thousands of yuan in cash before, but she had never seen so many banknotes like this.","The largest banknote she had seen was still the fifty-tael note her brother had given her.","Seeing Jiang Fengtang produce so many banknotes with such an unconcerned expression, Jiang Yunxi confirmed that her cheap father was rich—very rich.","She couldn’t help grumbling inwardly again.","[My father really is rich, and he’s fairly generous too.","It’s just a shame that he’s never generous toward me.]","[He’s this generous even with my brother. He must be even more generous with his legitimate children, especially his beloved daughter Jiang Yunshu, Madam Wei’s precious darling.]","Jiang Fengtang couldn’t help coughing.","What kind of thing was this child saying? What did she mean by “Madam Wei’s precious darling”?","[So, we really are born to different fates despite having the same father.","I’d better stop counting on him. It’s more practical to count on my brother.]","Afraid that his sister might say something even more outrageous, Jiang Yunzheng hurriedly asked, “Father, what about my sister’s share? Didn’t you say earlier that you would...”","Jiang Yunzheng desperately shot Jiang Fengtang meaningful looks.","Dad, my dear dad, didn’t you say earlier that you were going to compensate my sister? Then hurry up and give it to her.","Can’t you see how badly she wants it? She’s practically drooling.","If I simply handed her my banknotes, wouldn’t that make you look bad?","Looking at his daughter, who stood there with her head lowered in an apparently respectful manner, her eyes fixed unwaveringly on the banknotes in her brother’s hand, Jiang Fengtang sighed inwardly.","He truly had neglected this youngest daughter over the years. Only five hundred taels, and she was already so desperate for it.","“Yunxi.”","Jiang Yunxi didn’t react. She was too busy staring at the banknotes in her brother’s hand and swallowing hard.","[System, do you think five hundred taels in banknotes would blind me if they were exchanged for five hundred taels of gold?]","Jiang Yunzheng said, “Little sister, rein in that greed of yours. At this rate, you won’t be able to hide the fact that you’re a money-grubber.”","[Host, stop thinking about that and pay attention. Your father is calling you.]","“Ah—Father. No, I mean, Father, were you calling me?”","Jiang Fengtang nodded. “Yes. Father was calling you.”","He took two thick stacks of banknotes from his sleeve and handed them to Jiang Yunxi.","Jiang Yunxi froze when she saw the stacks. Each one was several times thicker than the one he had given her brother.","All of this was for her?","She couldn’t believe it. For a moment, she simply stood there, too stunned to reach out and accept them.","“What are you waiting for? Take it,” Jiang Fengtang urged.","At ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​‌‍those words, Jiang Yunxi looked up and stared at Jiang Fengtang in disbelief. “Father, is all of this for me?”","Jiang Fengtang nodded. “Yes, it’s all for you.”"]}]);
